/* Ported from Olivia Today (outputs/olivia-today) by work/olivia-today/port-to-site.mjs. Edit the source there, then re-run the port. */
// @ts-nocheck
export default {"planets":{"sun":{"planet":"sun","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Your personal new year begins","text":"The Sun is back in your sign for the weeks around your birthday, and the spotlight swings onto you: your face, your body, the way you walk into a room. People notice you more, and you notice what no longer fits, from a haircut to a habit. Because a birthday makes you count the years, you're tempted to reinvent everything at once. Start one thing, not five.","scene":"You catch your reflection in a shop window and, on the spot, book the haircut you've been postponing since spring.","do":"Start the one change you keep promising yourself, this week.","avoid":"Turning your birthday into a yearly performance review.","ask":"What do you want people to notice about you this year?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"The month to know your price","text":"For the next four weeks the Sun lights up your money: the salary, the side income, the subscriptions you forgot you pay for, the things you own and the things that own you. It's a good month to look at the numbers soberly. You may notice how closely your mood follows your balance, because earning is how you learned to prove your worth. Price your hours as if you believed they were worth it.","scene":"On the bus home you open the banking app, find three subscriptions you'd forgotten, and feel oddly proud for finally looking.","do":"Cancel one subscription and write down what your hour costs.","avoid":"Answering “whatever you think is fair” when someone asks your rate.","ask":"What would you charge if you weren't afraid of seeming greedy?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Your words travel further this month","text":"The Sun is moving through your house of messages and short distances, so this month runs on texts, calls, errands and quick trips across town. Your ideas land better than usual, and people start quoting you back to yourself. You'll be tempted to join every conversation, because being in the loop feels like being alive. Answer the threads that matter properly; the rest can live with a thumbs-up.","scene":"You're answering your brother on the tram, booking a class on the walk home and drafting the perfect reply to a neighbour's note.","do":"Send the email, post or pitch you've been drafting in your head.","avoid":"Replying to everyone and saying nothing you actually meant.","ask":"Which conversation this month is worth more than ten quick replies?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Home becomes the main stage","text":"This month the Sun drops to the base of your chart, into home, family and the place you come back to at night. The flat, the fridge, the parents and the role you play at the family table all ask for attention. Work ambitions feel muted because something at the foundation wants fixing first. The risk is turning back into the twelve-year-old you were whenever a relative raises an eyebrow.","scene":"You spend a free Saturday rearranging the living room and realise you're prouder of it than of anything you did at work.","do":"Fix the one thing at home you step around every day.","avoid":"Taking on every family errand to prove you're the good one.","ask":"What would make your home feel like it's on your side?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"A month for showing off a little","text":"The Sun walks into your house of pleasure, flirting and making things, and for once the month wants you to have fun on purpose. Romance warms up, a hobby turns into a small obsession, and any children around you want an audience. You might hold back from what you love because doing it badly in public feels worse than not doing it at all. Be an amateur, loudly.","scene":"You post the drawing, the song or the cake you made, then check the reactions every ten minutes with a grin you'd never admit to.","do":"Book a date, a class or a night out purely for pleasure.","avoid":"Waiting until you're good at something before letting anyone see it.","ask":"What did you love doing at ten that you quietly stopped?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Fixing the way your days run","text":"For the next few weeks the Sun shines on the unglamorous machinery of your life: the work queue, the sleep schedule, the gym bag by the door, the colleague who keeps forwarding you their tasks. Small fixes pay off fast, and you feel better simply for being competent. The catch is perfectionism, when improving your routine turns into auditing yourself all day. Change one habit, not your whole personality.","scene":"On Sunday night you colour-code your calendar, set an alarm for the gym and feel almost smug about a clean desktop.","do":"Choose one habit — sleep, water, a walk — and keep it daily.","avoid":"Doing a colleague's job because it's quicker than saying no.","ask":"Which daily habit would make the next month kinder to your body?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"The month of the other person","text":"The Sun is crossing the sign opposite yours, so this month belongs to the people across the table: a partner, a business ally, an ex, a rival you can't stop measuring yourself against. You see yourself most clearly in how they respond to you. It's a good time to sign, negotiate or have the overdue talk, and a bad one to let their mood set yours.","scene":"Across a dinner table you hear yourself say “I want this to be fair”, and realise you've been waiting months to say it.","do":"Say what you want from the partnership in one sentence.","avoid":"Agreeing to everything so the evening stays nice.","ask":"What do you keep expecting from others that you could give yourself?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Opening the envelope you've been avoiding","text":"This month the Sun lights up the parts of life you usually keep in a drawer: joint money, loans, taxes, the deposit someone still owes you, and who you really trust with your body and your secrets. One honest hour with the paperwork changes a lot. You avoid the statement or the conversation because needing someone feels like losing control. Read the statement; the number is rarely worse than the dread.","scene":"At the kitchen table you finally open the letter from the tax office, read it twice and feel lighter for knowing the number.","do":"Find out exactly what you owe and what you're owed.","avoid":"Keeping money secrets from someone who shares your bills.","ask":"Who do you trust with the truth about your money and your body?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Your world wants to get bigger","text":"The Sun is moving through your house of distance and big ideas, so this month the usual streets feel small. You want a ticket, a course, a book that rearranges your head, a conversation with someone from far away. It's good timing for applications, visas, publishing or anything that needs a stamp. The risk is preaching your new theory to everyone at dinner before you've lived with it for a week.","scene":"At midnight you have six tabs open — a flight, a language app, a master's programme — and you're happier than you've been in weeks.","do":"Book the trip, enrol in the course or send the application.","avoid":"Lecturing friends about a book you started on Tuesday.","ask":"Which belief of yours would you like to test against real life?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Your work in full daylight","text":"This month the Sun climbs to the highest point of your chart, the house of career and reputation, and your work is on display whether you planned it or not. Bosses notice, clients remember your name, and a role or a raise can come up for discussion. Because recognition feels like proof the effort was worth it, you're tempted to overwork just to be seen. Ask directly instead of hoping someone spots you.","scene":"Your name comes up in a meeting you weren't invited to, and for once you feel pleased instead of anxious.","do":"Ask your manager directly for the role, raise or project.","avoid":"Staying late just so someone sees the light still on.","ask":"What do you want to be known for at work in five years?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Your people, your plans","text":"The Sun is in your house of friends and futures, so this month your calendar fills with group dinners, birthdays, community events and the kind of chat that turns into a plan. You're more visible in the crowd, which feels good and slightly exposing. You'll catch yourself measuring your life against friends' news. Use the company instead: say your wish out loud to people who can help.","scene":"At a friend's birthday you mention, half-joking, the project you've been sitting on, and someone across the table says they know just the person.","do":"Tell three friends what you're working toward this year.","avoid":"Comparing your life to the highlights in the group chat.","ask":"Which friendships pull you toward the future you actually want?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"The quiet weeks before your birthday","text":"The Sun is passing through the last house of your chart, the weeks just before your birthday, and your battery runs lower than your calendar assumes. Sleep gets longer, crowds get louder, and old memories surface at odd hours. You try to push through, because rest without a reason feels like laziness to you. Clear the backlog, sleep more, and let the new year start clean.","scene":"You spend a Sunday alone sorting old photos and unsent drafts, and feel less lonely than you did in a crowded bar last week.","do":"Finish or formally close one project before your birthday.","avoid":"Launching big new plans in the weeks before your birthday.","ask":"What are you ready to finish before your next year begins?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Aries season: the starting gun of the zodiac year. Patience runs short, courage runs high, and the best ideas are the ones you start before you've finished thinking."},"taurus":{"en":"Taurus season slows everything to the pace of a good meal. People want comfort, money they can count and plans that last; rushing anyone gets you nowhere."},"gemini":{"en":"Gemini season fills the calendar with conversations, short trips and half-read articles. Curiosity runs high and attention runs short, so write things down."},"cancer":{"en":"Cancer season pulls everyone homeward: family, food, old photos, the people who knew you before. Feelings sit closer to the surface, and kindness goes further."},"leo":{"en":"Leo season wants to be seen. Generosity, flirting, birthdays and big gestures come easily, and so does wounded pride when nobody claps."},"virgo":{"en":"Virgo season brings lists, fresh notebooks and quiet repairs. Everyone wants to get organised; the risk is criticising the people who haven't yet."},"libra":{"en":"Libra season: everyone wants things fair, pretty and agreed. Good for partnerships and making peace, slower for decisions that will upset someone."},"scorpio":{"en":"Scorpio season turns attention below the surface: money, sex, secrets, grief. Small talk thins out, and loyalties get quietly tested."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Sagittarius season widens the view: travel plans, big opinions, honest jokes. Optimism is easy to find, and so is promising more than you can deliver."},"capricorn":{"en":"Capricorn season is for long goals and serious work. Effort and results earn respect, sentiment goes quiet, and everyone counts what this year actually built."},"aquarius":{"en":"Aquarius season favours friends, causes and odd new ideas. People want freedom and better systems, and can seem cool exactly when you want warmth."},"pisces":{"en":"Pisces season blurs the edges: dreams run vivid, empathy runs high, deadlines slip. The zodiac's last month suits rest, art and finishing what's old."}}},"moon":{"planet":"moon","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Your mood is written on your face","text":"The Moon is in your sign for the next two days, so your feelings sit right on the surface: in your face, your stomach, your tone of voice. Hunger, tiredness and irritation arrive faster and louder than usual. People read you easily today, which feels exposing if you're used to looking fine no matter what. Eat first, then decide whether the problem is still a problem.","scene":"Someone asks “are you okay?” before you've said a word, and you realise you've been frowning at your screen since nine.","do":"Eat a proper meal before replying to anything that annoys you.","avoid":"Pretending you're fine while your face says otherwise.","ask":"What is your body asking for before your head joins in?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Comfort comes with a price tag","text":"The Moon is passing through your house of money and possessions, so security feels physical today: a full fridge, a soft jumper, a decent balance in the account. You crave good food and familiar things, and spending works like a sedative. Owning something solid calms the part of you that worries it could all run out. Comfort is fine; just look at the basket before you pay.","scene":"You go in for bread and come out with cheese, candles and a scarf you didn't need, calmer and slightly guilty.","do":"Cook something filling from what's already in the fridge.","avoid":"Treating a low mood with a full online shopping basket.","ask":"What makes you feel safe that doesn't cost anything?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"You need to talk it out","text":"With the Moon in your house of messages and short trips, feelings come out as words today. You think out loud, so a long voice note to your sister or a chat with a neighbour on the stairs settles more than an hour of thinking in circles. Your mind runs fast and sleep may be light. When the thoughts start looping, get out for a short walk or an errand.","scene":"You record a four-minute voice note about a minor annoyance, play it back, and feel half of it already gone.","do":"Call a sibling or a chatty friend instead of texting.","avoid":"Rereading the same message until it sounds worse.","ask":"What are you trying to say that hasn't found the right listener yet?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"You want to be home today","text":"The Moon is in your house of home and family, where it feels most at ease, and you notice it as a pull toward the sofa, the old blanket, the food someone cooked for you as a child. Social plans look exhausting; your own kitchen looks perfect. A single phone call can stir old family feelings, because home is where your oldest reflexes live. Stay in if you can, and let that be enough.","scene":"You cancel drinks, make your grandmother's soup from memory and end up texting your mum to ask how much dill goes in.","do":"Cook a dish from your childhood or call home.","avoid":"Forcing yourself out when your body is asking to stay in.","ask":"What does home need to feel like for you to rest?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"You want delight, not duty","text":"The Moon moves through your house of pleasure and play, so your mood brightens the moment something is fun and sinks the moment it isn't. You want attention, a flirt, music loud in the car, dessert before the main course. Underneath is a simple need to be enjoyed rather than relied on. Take one unproductive hour, and notice if you're sulking because nobody clapped.","scene":"You put on the song you loved at seventeen while making dinner and end up dancing with a wooden spoon.","do":"Do one thing today purely because it's fun.","avoid":"Saving the fun for after the chores are done.","ask":"When did you last feel enjoyed rather than needed?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"A tidy desk calms you down","text":"The Moon is in your house of daily work and the body, so today your mood lives in your routine. A clear desk, a walk at lunch and water before coffee steady you; skipped meals and a messy inbox go straight to your stomach. You want to fix every small thing because order feels like control when your feelings won't behave. Do the chores, then stop before you start reorganising your colleagues.","scene":"At eleven at night you scrub the bathroom, give the cat an extra treat and feel calmer than you did all working day.","do":"Eat lunch away from the screen and take a short walk.","avoid":"Fixing colleagues' mistakes to calm your own nerves.","ask":"Which part of your body tells you first that you're overloaded?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Your mood depends on one person","text":"The Moon is passing through your house of partners, so for two days your feelings take shape around one other person. A partner's tone, a friend's slow reply or a colleague's coldness lands harder than usual. You want closeness and reassurance, and you may try to earn it by being agreeable rather than asking. Ask plainly instead of testing whether they'll guess.","scene":"Your partner says “fine” in a flat voice, and you spend the next hour guessing what you did wrong instead of asking.","do":"Ask for the hug, the call or the evening together.","avoid":"Taking a tired face or a short reply personally.","ask":"What do you need from the person closest to you today?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Feelings go deep and private","text":"With the Moon in your house of intimacy and shared money, feelings go underground today. You want real closeness or none at all, and small things, like a phone turned face-down or an unpaid share of the bill, feel like signs of something bigger. That suspicion is an old lesson: trusting too soon once cost you. Name what you're afraid of, then believe the answer you get.","scene":"Awake at one in the morning, you replay a remark from dinner and check the joint account for no clear reason.","do":"Ask the direct question instead of quietly investigating.","avoid":"Checking someone's phone or online status to calm your nerves.","ask":"Where are you bracing for betrayal instead of asking for reassurance?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"You need a bigger view today","text":"The Moon is moving through your house of distance and big questions, so your mood wants room today. The usual walls feel close, and a train window, a long walk, a documentary or a talk about what life is for feeds you better than another task. Small routines feel like a cage when you're hungry for meaning. Change the scenery, even if it's only a different café.","scene":"On the way home you get off two stops early just to walk a street you've never walked, and your shoulders drop.","do":"Walk somewhere new or sketch out a trip, even an imaginary one.","avoid":"Picking a fight about politics because you're bored.","ask":"Where would you go tomorrow if nothing held you back?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Work gets under your skin today","text":"The Moon crosses the top of your chart, your house of career and reputation, so feelings follow you to work today. A boss's short email or a public compliment hits you in the chest, not just the head. You want to look competent, so you hide tiredness to keep the image intact. Do the job well, then go home and let someone see you off duty.","scene":"Your manager replies “ok.” with no emoji, and you reread your own email three times looking for the mistake.","do":"Write down what you finished today and close the laptop on time.","avoid":"Treating one curt email from your boss as a verdict.","ask":"Whose approval at work are you still waiting for?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"You need your people today","text":"The Moon is passing through your house of friends and shared plans, so your mood rises and falls with the group around you. A good conversation can fix more than an hour alone with your thoughts. If you feel oddly flat, it may simply be that you've gone too long without people who know you well.","scene":"You open the group chat meaning to send one meme and end up planning a dinner for Saturday.","do":"Message the friend you've been meaning to reply to for a week.","avoid":"Reading one quiet reply as proof that nobody cares.","ask":"Who makes you feel more like yourself after an hour together?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Your body asks for a quiet day","text":"The Moon is in the hidden house of your chart, so for two days your skin feels thinner and your feelings go quiet and strange. Crowds feel loud, dreams get vivid, and you may tear up at an advert without knowing why. That's old tiredness asking to be noticed, and pushing through only makes it louder. Keep plans light and write down what you haven't said aloud.","scene":"You put on a film you've seen five times, pull the blanket over your head and leave every message until morning.","do":"Go to bed an hour earlier than usual tonight.","avoid":"Filling the silence with scrolling until two in the morning.","ask":"What feeling have you been too busy to notice this week?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Moods run hot and fast: impatient, brave, quick to snap and quick to forgive. Move your body early, and count to five before replying."},"taurus":{"en":"Moods settle into the body: hungry, slow, stubborn, soothed by good bread and clean sheets. Comfort helps; being rushed makes everyone dig in."},"gemini":{"en":"Moods turn chatty and scattered: everyone texts, nobody finishes a sentence. Talking helps, as long as the phone doesn't sleep on your pillow."},"cancer":{"en":"Moods turn tender and homeward: people want soup, family and someone who remembers how they take their tea. Feelings sit close to the surface, so go gently."},"leo":{"en":"Moods want warmth and an audience: generous, dramatic, easily flattered and easily hurt. Give someone a sincere compliment, and wear the good shirt."},"virgo":{"en":"Moods get practical and twitchy: everyone notices the crumbs, the typo, the late reply. Tidying a drawer helps more than analysing a feeling."},"libra":{"en":"Moods seek company and fairness: pleasant evenings, matching plates, nobody upset. Decisions slow down; a small kindness works better than winning the argument."},"scorpio":{"en":"Moods sink deep and go quiet: intense, private, suspicious of small talk. One honest conversation or a long bath helps more than a crowded room."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Moods lift toward the horizon: restless, funny, impatient with detail. A walk, a plan for a trip or a big honest conversation helps more than staying in."},"capricorn":{"en":"Moods turn sober and businesslike: less chatter, more lists, a stiff upper lip. Getting one hard thing done feels better than talking about feelings."},"aquarius":{"en":"Moods cool and step back: people want space, ideas and friends, not fuss. Feelings come out sideways as opinions, so ask what's underneath."},"pisces":{"en":"Moods go soft and porous: tearful at adverts, dreamy, soaking up whatever the room feels. Music, water and a quiet evening help; alcohol hits harder."}}},"mercury":{"planet":"mercury","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Your voice walks in first","text":"Mercury is crossing your first house, so for a few weeks the way you talk is the way people meet you. You think faster, interrupt more, and start three things before lunch. Underneath it is an old habit of explaining yourself before anyone asks, because being misread feels worse than being wrong. The risk is running on nerves: half-finished sentences, cold half-drunk coffee, a jaw you clench without noticing.","scene":"Someone new asks what you do, and you hear yourself give a three-minute answer, with footnotes, before they've finished their drink.","do":"Say the short version first, then stop and let them ask.","avoid":"Over-explaining yourself to people who didn't ask for a reason.","ask":"What do you keep explaining that nobody asked you to justify?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Say the number out loud","text":"Mercury moving through your second house turns money into a conversation you've been postponing: the invoice, the raise, the subscription you forgot, the price you quote a client. You do sums in your head while brushing your teeth. The hard part isn't the maths but saying a figure aloud, because naming your price hands someone else the chance to raise an eyebrow. The risk is checking the banking app instead of making the call.","scene":"You type your rate into an email, delete it, type a lower one, and stare at the cursor for a full minute.","do":"Send the invoice or the price today, without an apology attached.","avoid":"Discounting your price before anyone has even asked.","ask":"What number do you find hardest to say out loud?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Every message feels like your job","text":"Mercury is on home ground in your third house, and the weeks speed up: messages, errands across town, a sibling who suddenly wants to talk, a neighbour with news. Your mind is quick and nosy in a good way, and you learn faster by doing than by reading. The catch is that replying instantly starts to feel like proof you're reliable, so you answer everything and say very little.","scene":"You're on the bus answering your sister, a work chat and the landlord at once, and you miss your stop.","do":"Mute two group chats and call one person back instead.","avoid":"Passing on a rumour because it's too good not to.","ask":"Which conversation this week actually changed what you think?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"The family chat wakes up","text":"Mercury in your fourth house brings the talking home: calls with a parent, the family group chat, a plumber to book, the utility bill nobody has read. Your mind drifts back to childhood rooms and things said at dinner years ago. With family you slip into the voice you had at fourteen, because that's the dialect you learned first. The risk is replaying an old argument instead of having the current one.","scene":"You call home about one small thing, and forty minutes later you're arguing about a family holiday from 2009.","do":"Book the repair you keep mentioning, or sort one drawer of papers.","avoid":"Answering a parent in the tone you had at fourteen.","ask":"Which family sentence still plays in your head, and whose voice is it?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Wit does the flirting","text":"Mercury in your fifth house makes play verbal: the flirty text you redraft three times, a story you start writing for fun, a board game that turns competitive, a child's hundredth why. Ideas come easily when nothing is at stake. You'd rather be clever than sincere, because a joke can always be taken back and a feeling can't. The risk is banter so good that nobody ever says what they want.","scene":"You spend twenty minutes on a two-line reply to someone you like, then delete the one honest word.","do":"Send one message that's warm instead of witty.","avoid":"Hiding a real compliment inside a joke.","ask":"What feeling are you joking about instead of naming?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"A list for every worry","text":"Mercury in your sixth house turns ordinary days into logistics: work email, the shared calendar, a colleague whose instructions make no sense, the dentist appointment you keep rescheduling. Your mind wants systems, and you're good at fixing a clumsy process. When you're anxious, you write a list, because a tidy list feels like control and a worry doesn't. The risk is a tight stomach and nitpicking everyone's spelling.","scene":"You rewrite tomorrow's to-do list in a nicer notebook instead of doing the first item on it.","do":"Do the ten-minute task that's been on your list all week.","avoid":"Correcting a colleague's grammar when they asked about the deadline.","ask":"What does your body do when your inbox gets full?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Every partnership becomes a negotiation","text":"Mercury in your seventh house moves the important conversations to a table for two: a partner, a business ally, a client, the contract you need to read properly. You think most clearly these weeks with one person opposite you. The snag is listening for the reply you expected instead of the one you got, because being right feels safer than being surprised. Ask before you argue.","scene":"The person closest to you says one sentence about the weekend, and you reply to the argument you rehearsed on the way home.","do":"Repeat back what they said before you answer it.","avoid":"Signing a contract you've only skimmed on your phone.","ask":"What do you want from this person, besides being right?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"The fine print gets personal","text":"Mercury is moving through your eighth house, where money and trust get tangled: the tax return, the loan terms, who pays what from a shared account, the talk about sex or debt you both avoid. Your mind turns detective and wants the real story. You'd rather research than ask outright, because asking means admitting how much the answer matters. The risk is scrolling back through old messages for evidence instead of asking once.","scene":"You read the tax letter twice before breakfast, then search one phrase online until you've convinced yourself it's a disaster.","do":"Ask the money question directly, in one plain sentence.","avoid":"Treating a short reply as evidence of a secret.","ask":"What answer are you afraid of getting if you ask straight?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Your mind buys the ticket first","text":"Mercury in your ninth house makes your mind hungry for a bigger map: a course, a language app, flights you price at 1 a.m., a visa form, a long article you finish. Opinions about politics, faith and how to live feel urgent and worth arguing over. You may collect information to avoid choosing, because a trip you're still researching can't disappoint you. The risk is winning an argument at dinner and losing the room.","scene":"You have fourteen tabs open about a city you've never been to and haven't booked a single night.","do":"Book one real thing this week: a class, a train, a weekend away.","avoid":"Turning every disagreement into a lecture with sources.","ask":"What would you study if nobody needed it to be useful?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Your words go on the record","text":"Mercury crossing your tenth house puts your words in front of people who decide things: the boss, the client, the panel, whoever reads your CV. These weeks suit pitching, presenting and asking about the next step. You over-edit, because part of you believes one clumsy sentence could undo years of work. The risk is sounding so professional that nobody can hear what you actually want.","scene":"You rewrite a three-line email to your manager seven times and still open it with “Sorry to bother you”.","do":"Send the pitch at version three, not version eleven.","avoid":"Agreeing in the meeting and complaining about it afterwards.","ask":"What do you want to be known for, in one sentence?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Ideas get better in company","text":"Mercury in your eleventh house puts your best thinking in other people's company: a friend who asks the sharp question, an online community, a meetup, the chat where half-formed plans get tested. Saying a hope aloud to people you trust makes it real enough to start. The temptation is agreeing with the group to keep your place in it, because disagreeing feels like risking the invitation.","scene":"You mention a half-serious idea in the group chat and by evening three friends are asking when it launches.","do":"Tell one friend the plan you've only told your notes app.","avoid":"Laughing along at a group opinion you privately disagree with.","ask":"Who do you think more clearly around, and when did you last call them?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Your head talks after midnight","text":"Mercury slipping through your twelfth house turns up the voice in your head and turns down everything else. You need more quiet to think, and your clearest ideas arrive in the shower, on a walk, half asleep. You also rehearse conversations you'll never have, because a draft can't hurt you and a reply can. The risk is reaching for the phone in bed when your mind wants a notebook.","scene":"You lie awake at 3 a.m. polishing the perfect reply to something a colleague said three years ago.","do":"Keep a notebook by the bed and empty your head into it.","avoid":"Telling everyone you're fine while arguing with them in your head.","ask":"What are you saying to yourself that you haven't said to anyone?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Mercury in Aries thinks in headlines: fast decisions, blunt replies, the first draft sent before the second thought. Good for starting, careless with details."},"taurus":{"en":"Mercury in Taurus thinks slowly and means it. Ideas have to be useful, solid, preferably affordable; once a mind is made up, it stays that way."},"gemini":{"en":"Mercury in Gemini is at home: quick, curious, funny, able to hold three conversations and a podcast at once. Wonderful for ideas, slippery about follow-through."},"cancer":{"en":"Mercury in Cancer listens for tone more than words and remembers what was said years ago, word for word. Kitchen-table talks beat email."},"leo":{"en":"Mercury in Leo speaks to be heard: stories with a punchline, opinions delivered with conviction, a talent for persuading a room. Feedback stings more than it should."},"virgo":{"en":"Mercury in Virgo edits everything: the plan, the spreadsheet, the sentence you just said. Precise, useful, quietly anxious, and very good at spotting the one typo."},"libra":{"en":"Mercury in Libra weighs both sides out loud and drafts the diplomatic version first. Good for negotiating, slow to deliver a plain no."},"scorpio":{"en":"Mercury in Scorpio listens for what isn't said. Questions go straight to the sore spot, secrets stay kept, and a vague answer only sharpens suspicion."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Mercury in Sagittarius thinks big and talks frankly, sometimes to the point of tactlessness. It loves the overview, skips the footnotes and promises more than the calendar holds."},"capricorn":{"en":"Mercury in Capricorn thinks in plans, deadlines and consequences. Messages turn brief and dry, like memos: excellent for contracts and hard talks, stingy with kind words."},"aquarius":{"en":"Mercury in Aquarius thinks sideways: odd connections, sudden ideas at the bus stop, strong opinions about how systems should work. Brilliant in theory, cool in tone."},"pisces":{"en":"Mercury in Pisces thinks in images and hunches, not lists. Words go soft and suggestive: lovely for comforting a friend, risky for deadlines and fine print."}},"retro":{"1":{"en":"Your self-presentation comes back for an edit: the bio, the profile photo, the way you introduce yourself, the habit of answering before you've heard the question. Slow down; a second take often lands better."},"2":{"en":"Money paperwork returns: the refund you never chased, the subscription still charging you, the rate you quoted too low last year. Recheck the numbers and renegotiate calmly; don't panic-cancel everything."},"3":{"en":"Old messages resurface: the sibling you owe a call, the neighbour you misread, the text sent to the wrong chat. Double-check addresses and times, reread before sending, and sort out misunderstandings by phone."},"4":{"en":"Family conversations loop back: a parent retelling an old story, the repair that wasn't done properly, the box of papers nobody sorted. Redo the job at home, and hear the story once more, actually listening."},"5":{"en":"An old flirtation or a shelved creative project comes back into view. Reread the old draft before starting fresh; answer the ex only if it still seems wise next morning."},"6":{"en":"Work admin comes back: the email thread nobody resolved, the instruction you misunderstood, the appointment you forgot to confirm. Repair the process, not your whole routine, and check times twice."},"7":{"en":"Old agreements return for renegotiation: a contract clause, a promise made to a partner, a misunderstanding with a client. Reread before you re-sign, ask what they meant, and let an old argument end differently."},"8":{"en":"Shared paperwork resurfaces: a tax query, an old debt, the joint account nobody reconciled, a conversation about trust left half-finished. Gather the documents, correct errors calmly and finish the talk you abandoned."},"9":{"en":"Travel plans and studies come back around: a delayed booking, a visa form with a typo, the course you dropped halfway. Recheck every date and document; going back to finish something counts as progress."},"10":{"en":"Career conversations return: the pitch that stalled, feedback from a boss you brushed off, an old employer in touch again. Revise the CV, follow up politely and hold big announcements until the details are checked."},"11":{"en":"Old friends and old plans reappear in the chat: the group you drifted from, the project everyone abandoned, the friend you owe a reply. Reconnect, rethink the plan, and check a rumour before forwarding it."},"12":{"en":"Unsent drafts and unspoken thoughts return at night: an old apology, a half-kept secret, a dream that keeps recurring. Write it down first; decide in daylight whether anyone needs to read it."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Mercury retrograde is the roughly three weeks, a few times a year, when Mercury appears to move backwards across the sky. Treat it as an editing season: reread, recheck dates, back up your phone, reopen conversations that ended badly. Sign what you must, after reading it twice."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"The days when Mercury stands still before turning back often feel stuck: replies stall, the laptop freezes, you lose your train of thought mid-sentence. Slow down, back up files and reread before you send."},"direct":{"en":"When Mercury pauses and turns forward, the jam clears slowly, not overnight. The turning day can feel foggy; a few days later, send the held reply, sign the reread contract, restart the paused plan."}}},"venus":{"planet":"venus","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"People warm to you on sight","text":"Venus is crossing your first house, the one that governs your body, your face and how you walk into a room. For a few weeks you are easier to like, and you know it: strangers smile back, the haircut works, the coat you nearly gave away looks right again. Feeling attractive makes you gentler with everyone, including yourself. The risk is saying yes to keep the smiles coming.","scene":"You catch your reflection in a shop window, stand a little straighter, and walk in to try on something you weren't going to buy.","do":"Wear the thing you've been saving for a better day.","avoid":"Buying a new look to rescue a bad mood.","ask":"When do you feel most at home in your own body?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Your taste outruns your budget","text":"Venus in your second house turns your eye to money, belongings and your own worth. You want fewer, better things: the good olive oil, the wool coat, the cup that feels right in your hand. Spending and self-worth are tangled here: it's easy to undercharge for your work, then overpay for a candle to feel better about it. These are good weeks to raise your rate and bad ones to shop when tired.","scene":"You stand at the checkout holding a beautiful, slightly ridiculous thing and tell yourself you've earned it, which might even be true.","do":"Leave the lovely thing in the basket until tomorrow.","avoid":"Treating a price tag as a verdict on your worth.","ask":"What would you charge if you believed you were worth it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Charm lives in your messages","text":"Venus is moving through your house of messages, siblings and short trips, so charm comes through your thumbs. You find the right words for the awkward text, the thank-you you owe a neighbour, the reply that makes your sister laugh after a cold month. Even the walk to the shop feels prettier. The risk is smoothing every conversation into agreement, because being pleasant feels safer than being clear.","scene":"You rewrite a two-line text four times so it sounds warm but not too keen, then send the first version anyway.","do":"Send the compliment you thought of and didn't say.","avoid":"Typing “sounds great” when you mean “not really”.","ask":"Which conversation have you been keeping pleasant instead of honest?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Love starts at the kitchen table","text":"Venus is settling into your fourth house: the flat, the family, the parents whose voices still live in your head. You want home to look and feel right — a lamp moved, fresh flowers, the dish your grandmother used to make — because when the room is in order, so are you. Calls with family go more gently than usual. The risk is buying that calm by swallowing what you actually think.","scene":"You spend Sunday afternoon moving the sofa a metre to the left and feel oddly, completely better.","do":"Invite someone over and cook one thing you're proud of.","avoid":"Nodding along at the family table to keep dinner pleasant.","ask":"What makes your home feel like yours, not just where you sleep?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Pleasure stops needing a reason","text":"Venus is in your fifth house of romance, play and making things, and gives you permission to enjoy yourself without earning it first. Flirting gets easier, a hobby you dropped wants you back, and a night of dancing beats a productive evening. You're most attractive when you're having fun, not when you're trying. The risk is chasing the rush of being wanted rather than the person who wants you.","scene":"You say yes to a last-minute drink, pick the louder shirt, and laugh harder than you have all month.","do":"Book one evening purely for fun: a gig, a class, a late film.","avoid":"Messaging an old flame only to check you've still got it.","ask":"When did you last enjoy something without needing to be good at it?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Love shows up as help","text":"Venus is moving through the part of your chart that runs your days: the to-do list, the job, the body that carries you through it. Affection here is practical. You feel loved when someone notices you're tired and quietly takes something off your plate, and you love the same way, often without saying so. The risk is keeping silent score.","scene":"You do the dishes for the third night running and catch yourself rehearsing a complaint instead of asking for help.","do":"Ask plainly for one specific kind of help.","avoid":"Turning a small chore into a test of how much you're valued.","ask":"What would make an ordinary weekday feel cared for?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Two is the easier number","text":"Venus is crossing your seventh house, the one about partners, close one-to-one bonds and the agreements you sign. The air softens between you and the person across the table: an apology lands, a negotiation finds its middle, a date feels less like an interview. You want harmony badly enough to read every pause as trouble. The risk is agreeing so smoothly that the other person never meets the real you.","scene":"You say “I don't mind, you choose” about the restaurant, then spend dinner wishing you'd named the place you wanted.","do":"Say your preference first, before asking what they'd like.","avoid":"Signing anything because the other side was charming about it.","ask":"What do you want from the person closest to you but haven't asked for?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Closeness with the lights on","text":"Venus is in your eighth house, where desire, trust and shared money overlap. Attraction gets deeper and less polite, and so do questions of who pays: the joint account, the loan to a friend, the gift that came with strings. Talking about money can feel more naked than undressing, because it shows what you fear losing. The risk is using a present or a night together to skip that talk.","scene":"You split the dinner bill to the last penny, then lie awake wondering why it felt so cold.","do":"Say one true sentence about money to the person you share it with.","avoid":"Paying for everything so that nobody can ask more of you.","ask":"Who do you trust with your body but not with your bank balance?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Falling for somewhere else","text":"Venus is travelling through your ninth house of distance, study and big ideas, so you fall a little in love with elsewhere: a city you saw in a film, a language you're learning on your phone, a lecturer who explains things beautifully. What attracts you now is whatever makes you feel larger than your usual life. The risk is romanticising faraway places until home starts to look small.","scene":"You check flights to a city you have no reason to visit, only to picture who you'd be there.","do":"Learn ten words of the language you keep daydreaming in.","avoid":"Booking an expensive escape from a life you haven't tried changing.","ask":"Who do you become in a place where nobody knows you?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Charm finally counts at work","text":"Venus is crossing the top of your chart, the tenth house of career, reputation and the people above you. You come across well in public: the interview feels warm, the pitch lands, your boss laughs in the right place. Goodwill is high, so these are good weeks to ask for the title, the budget or the move. The risk is settling for praise, because being liked feels like enough when it isn't.","scene":"You get a compliment from someone senior in the lift and replay it all afternoon, slightly embarrassed by how much it matters.","do":"Ask for one specific thing while the room likes you.","avoid":"Taking a compliment from your boss as payment.","ask":"What do you want to be known for, beyond being nice to work with?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Friendship feels like falling in love","text":"Venus is in your eleventh house of friends, groups and the future you're planning, so the sweetest moments come in company. A new friend feels instantly familiar, an old one comes back warm, and a group dinner restores you more than a date would. You feel lovable when you're included, which makes every invitation hard to refuse. The risk is spending money and evenings to keep up with a crowd you've outgrown.","scene":"You almost skip a friend's birthday drinks, go anyway, and leave with two new numbers and a plan for Thursday.","do":"Introduce two friends who would like each other.","avoid":"Splitting a pricey bill to prove you still belong.","ask":"Which friends make your hopes feel realistic rather than silly?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Love you keep to yourself","text":"Venus is moving through your twelfth house, the hidden back room of the chart where you rest and keep what you don't say aloud. Desire goes quiet and private: a crush you tell nobody about, a long bath, a song you play only when alone. Wanting someone out of reach can feel safer than wanting someone who might answer. The risk is spending these weeks in love with a maybe.","scene":"You reread an old conversation late at night, phone dimmed, and decide not to message, again.","do":"Do one kind thing today that nobody will ever know about.","avoid":"Keeping a door open for someone who never walks through it.","ask":"What are you longing for that you haven't admitted even to yourself?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Venus in Aries falls fast and says so first. Attraction is a dare: bold texts, sudden crushes, impulse buys, and boredom that arrives just as quickly."},"taurus":{"en":"Venus in Taurus loves slowly and through the senses: good bread, soft fabric, an unhurried evening. Loyalty runs deep, and so does the habit of staying too long."},"gemini":{"en":"Venus in Gemini is charmed by a quick mind. Flirting happens in words — banter, voice notes, late-night replies — and curiosity often outruns commitment."},"cancer":{"en":"Venus in Cancer loves by looking after: soup, remembered birthdays, a spare key. Tenderness comes easily, but so does the hurt of feeling taken for granted."},"leo":{"en":"Venus in Leo wants romance with a little theatre: grand gestures, being chosen in public, compliments that sound like applause. Generous, warm, and quietly wounded when ignored."},"virgo":{"en":"Venus in Virgo shows love through small fixes: the shelf put up, the typo caught, the vitamins left out. Devotion is real; so is the inner critic."},"libra":{"en":"Venus in Libra is at home: manners, beauty, fairness, the art of the second date. Peace comes easily, sometimes at the cost of wishes left unsaid."},"scorpio":{"en":"Venus in Scorpio wants depth over charm: loyalty, secrets, all-or-nothing attraction. Small talk feels like a waste, and jealousy runs closer to the surface."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Venus in Sagittarius falls for freedom and laughter: the stranger on the train, the person who says yes to the trip. Honesty is charming; clinginess kills it."},"capricorn":{"en":"Venus in Capricorn loves with a long view: a coat that lasts ten years, a person who turns up on time. Affection shows in effort, rarely in words."},"aquarius":{"en":"Venus in Aquarius falls for the friend first: the odd, independent, interesting one. Attraction runs through ideas, and closeness too soon feels like a cage."},"pisces":{"en":"Venus in Pisces loves without edges: romantic, devoted, moved to tears by a song. Kindness peaks, and so does the urge to rescue someone who won't change."}},"retro":{"1":{"en":"How you look and present yourself comes back for review: the haircut you miss, the style you outgrew, the habit of shrinking to be liked. Postpone the drastic fringe."},"2":{"en":"Money and self-worth ask for a second look: the subscription you forgot, the thing you returned and still want, the rate you've charged for years. Read the bank statement before buying anything big."},"3":{"en":"Old conversations resurface: the sibling you stopped calling, the message you never answered, the ex whose “hey, stranger” suddenly appears. Reply slowly; a kind word doesn't have to become a reunion."},"4":{"en":"Family history knocks again: the parent you've half forgiven, the flat you left too fast, the childhood dish you can't get right. Repair and rearrange; don't sign a new lease in a hurry."},"5":{"en":"Old flames and old pleasures return: the ex who likes your story at 1 a.m., the guitar under the bed. Pick up the guitar; think twice about the ex."},"6":{"en":"Old habits around work and health come back for review: the job you tolerate, the routine you abandoned, the colleague you never quite made peace with. Revise; don't quit in a mood."},"7":{"en":"Old love stories reopen: the ex who suggests coffee, the argument you two never finished, the pattern you repeat with new faces. Listen fully; decide nothing over the first coffee."},"8":{"en":"Debts of every kind come due: money you lent and stopped mentioning, the card you're still paying off, the person you shut out without a word. Be honest; don't open a joint account yet."},"9":{"en":"An old belief or a far-off place calls you back: the course you abandoned, the city you loved at twenty, the faith or teacher you outgrew. Revisit them; postpone the one-way ticket."},"10":{"en":"Unfinished business at work returns: the job you left with regret, the former boss who suddenly likes your post, the ambition you shelved to seem easygoing. Reconnect now; renegotiate once Venus turns direct."},"11":{"en":"Lapsed friendships come back around: the friend you drifted from, the one you secretly fancied, the hope you stopped mentioning aloud. Message one; you don't have to rejoin the whole chat."},"12":{"en":"Buried feelings float up: the ex who still turns up in your dreams, the crush you never confessed, the midnight comfort-shopping. Write it down before you say it to anyone."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Every eighteen months Venus appears to walk backwards for six weeks. It's a season for second looks, not first moves: exes, old wants and old spending return so you can ask what you value now. Repair what's worth it; save new vows, big purchases and drastic haircuts for later."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Venus stops before turning back, and desire wobbles: a crush cools, the thing in your basket loses its shine, an old name returns. Notice what you miss; decide nothing about love this week."},"direct":{"en":"Venus pauses and turns forward again. You start to see which ex was nostalgia and which purchase was worth waiting for. Give it a few days, then act on what survived the review."}}},"mars":{"planet":"mars","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Your fuse is shorter, your stride longer","text":"Mars is crossing your first house for the next six weeks or so, and you feel it in the body first: more appetite for effort, less patience for waiting your turn. You start things before you've finished deciding, because standing still feels like losing. The same heat makes you sharp with people who are simply slower than you. Burn it off in a workout before it burns through a conversation.","scene":"You take the stairs two at a time, book a boxing class at midnight, and feel personally offended by a slow cashier.","do":"Book one workout hard enough to leave you quiet afterwards.","avoid":"Snapping at people for not moving at your speed.","ask":"What have you been waiting for permission to start?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Fighting for what you're worth","text":"Mars in your second house turns money into a matter of pride. For these weeks you want to earn more, charge more, and stop doing the favour-priced work you quietly resent. The push comes from a simple place: you're tired of feeling cheap in your own eyes. The risk is spending in the same mood, buying the expensive thing to prove a point nobody asked you to make.","scene":"You open the invoice you've sent the same client for two years, look at the rate, and finally change the number.","do":"Name a higher price out loud and stop talking.","avoid":"Rage-buying something expensive after a bad day at work.","ask":"Where are you still accepting less because asking feels rude?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Typing faster than you think","text":"Mars in your third house speeds up your mouth, your thumbs and your driving. Replies come out sharper, debates start in the comments, and the commute becomes a contest with every car that cuts in. You're quick because you've been holding back opinions for months and the lid is loose. Use the speed to learn something hands-on; don't waste it winning a text argument with your brother.","scene":"You rewrite a reply to a neighbour four times, each version shorter and colder, then send the coldest one.","do":"Wait ten minutes before sending anything you typed while annoyed.","avoid":"Firing off replies faster than you can read them.","ask":"Which conversation are you rehearsing instead of having?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Home is where the friction is","text":"Mars in your fourth house brings heat indoors. You want to fix the dripping tap, repaint the hallway, throw out the boxes you've moved twice, and you're also quicker to bristle at a parent's tone or a flatmate's dishes. Old family tempers surface because home is the one place you stop performing patience. Put the force into the rooms before it goes into the people living in them.","scene":"You start clearing one kitchen drawer at ten at night and by midnight the whole cupboard is on the floor.","do":"Pick one repair at home and finish it this week.","avoid":"Reopening the oldest family argument over Sunday dinner.","ask":"What at home have you been tolerating that you could actually fix?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Desire stops waiting to be asked","text":"Mars in your fifth house puts desire up front: attraction, flirting, sex, the thrill of a risk you usually talk yourself out of. You're bolder about making the first move, and creative work goes faster when there's something to win. The pull comes from being tired of wanting things politely. Watch the competitive streak: a board game with the kids or a five-a-side match can become a contest you didn't need to win.","scene":"You text first, suggest the bar instead of the café, and enjoy the small jolt of not knowing how they'll answer.","do":"Make the first move on something you want, a person or a project.","avoid":"Turning a friendly game into a grudge match.","ask":"What would you go after if looking foolish cost nothing?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Racing through the to-do list","text":"Mars is moving through your sixth house, the part of your life made of work hours, chores and the body's maintenance. You can clear a backlog in a week that would normally take a month, and hard training feels good rather than punishing. Busyness calms you, so colleagues who work at a normal pace start to look lazy. The usual bill is a strained back or a skipped lunch.","scene":"You clear the inbox before your coffee cools, snap at the printer, and still feel annoyed that a colleague left at five.","do":"Do the dreaded task first, then stop at a set time.","avoid":"Judging colleagues by how fast they reply to you.","ask":"What are you trying to outrun by staying this busy?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Your partner becomes your sparring partner","text":"Mars in your seventh house turns up the heat in your closest one-to-one bonds. Partners, business allies and rivals get more direct, and so do you: arguments flare quickly, and so does attraction. Often the person across the table is acting out the anger you're too polite to own. Fight fair and finish rows on the same day, and a contract or a relationship can come out clearer.","scene":"You argue about whose turn it is to book the holiday and realise halfway through you're arguing about something older.","do":"Say what you want in one sentence, without the backstory.","avoid":"Letting your partner carry anger that is actually yours.","ask":"What do you want from them that you haven't asked for directly?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Debts, desire and the joint account","text":"Mars in your eighth house goes after what's shared: the joint account, the loan, the tax form, the deep end of intimacy. You want the truth about who owes whom, and you're less willing to pretend a debt or a trust problem isn't there. Desire runs strong and possessive, because closeness feels safer when you're the one in control. Tackle the paperwork; don't turn sex or money into leverage.","scene":"You finally open the tax letter that's sat sealed for a week, call the bank, and feel oddly turned on by your own nerve.","do":"Write down every debt you owe and every one owed to you.","avoid":"Using money or sex to win a quiet power struggle.","ask":"Where are you holding on to control because trusting feels too risky?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Restless for a bigger map","text":"Mars in your ninth house makes your world feel too small. You want to book the flight, start the course, pitch the article, or win the argument about politics at the dinner table. The push comes from a fear of staying the same person in the same town forever. Point it at a goal with a deadline; otherwise it turns into preaching at whoever sits closest.","scene":"You start a polite comment under a news post and twenty minutes later you're drafting a full essay with sources.","do":"Pay for the course or trip you keep researching.","avoid":"Trying to convert people who never asked for your opinion.","ask":"Where would you go if the only price were nerve?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Ambition with its sleeves rolled up","text":"Mars moving through your tenth house, the house of career, turns ambition into something physical. You want the promotion, the bigger client, the title on the door, and you'd rather say so in the meeting than grumble in the corridor afterwards. Part of the drive is anger at being underestimated. Use it on work people can see, and pick your clashes with bosses as if they'll be remembered, because they will.","scene":"You answer your boss's vague email with three bullet points and a deadline, and feel a small thrill pressing send.","do":"Ask for the role, raise or project you want, by name.","avoid":"Fighting your boss in public when a private word would win.","ask":"Who are you still trying to prove wrong with your work?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Rallying the group, or rowing with it","text":"Mars in your eleventh house puts fire into friendships, teams and the plans you share with them. You're the one organising the fundraiser, starting the running club or rewriting the group project at 1 a.m. The drive comes from wanting the future to arrive faster than other people seem to want it. That impatience can cost you a friend, so lead the group instead of overruling it.","scene":"You suggest one small change in the group chat and by evening you've somehow become the person running the whole thing.","do":"Ask a friend to train, build or plan something with you.","avoid":"Treating friends' slower pace as a lack of loyalty.","ask":"Which friend would you want beside you in a real fight?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Anger that keeps you up at night","text":"Mars in your twelfth house sends your drive underground. You may feel tired without a clear reason, sleep badly, or notice irritation leaking out as sarcasm because you never said the direct thing. This is a stretch for working behind the scenes, alone, without needing anyone to watch. Swim, walk, lift: give the body a private outlet, or the unspoken anger turns up at 3 a.m.","scene":"You lie awake replaying a conversation from Tuesday, polishing the sharp reply you didn't send, word by perfect word.","do":"Write the angry letter by hand, then put it in a drawer.","avoid":"Swallowing anger all day and paying for it at night.","ask":"What are you angry about that you haven't admitted to anyone?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Mars in Aries is at home: fast, direct, first through the door. Courage comes easily, patience doesn't, and a fight can flare and finish within an hour."},"taurus":{"en":"Mars in Taurus is slow to start and hard to stop. It builds with its hands, likes long dinners and slow sex, and digs in hard when pushed."},"gemini":{"en":"Mars in Gemini fights with words: quick replies, sharp jokes, ten tabs open at once. Drive scatters easily, so one finished task beats five brilliant starts."},"cancer":{"en":"Mars in Cancer fights for its people and sulks before it shouts. Anger comes out sideways — a slammed cupboard, a cold silence — so name the hurt underneath."},"leo":{"en":"Mars in Leo wants to win where people can see it. Generous, proud, theatrical in a fight, it works hardest for applause and bristles fastest when ignored."},"virgo":{"en":"Mars in Virgo fights by fixing. Effort goes into lists, systems and the gym routine, and anger shows up as criticism of how someone loaded the dishwasher."},"libra":{"en":"Mars in Libra hates open conflict and fights for fairness instead. Decisions stall while it weighs both sides, and anger hides behind a polite smile until it doesn't."},"scorpio":{"en":"Mars in Scorpio is patient, private and relentless. Desire runs deep, grudges last longer, and it would rather wait a month for the right move than waste one."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Mars in Sagittarius aims far: big plans, long hikes, blunt truths. It fights for beliefs, gets bored halfway, and says the tactless thing with a grin."},"capricorn":{"en":"Mars in Capricorn works at its best: disciplined, strategic, built for the long climb. It keeps its temper, meets deadlines, and quietly outworks louder people."},"aquarius":{"en":"Mars in Aquarius fights for causes and against being told what to do. Cool in a row, stubborn about principle, it rebels first and explains later."},"pisces":{"en":"Mars in Pisces moves like water: indirect, intuitive, easily worn down. It fights for the underdog, avoids confrontation, and works best through music, swimming or care."}},"retro":{"1":{"en":"Your own drive comes back for review. Stamina dips, old injuries ache, and a fresh start you rushed earlier asks to be done properly. Lower the weights and fix your form."},"2":{"en":"Money fights return: the raise you didn't push for, the debt you argued about, the purchase you made out of spite. Renegotiate calmly; don't rage-quit a steady income."},"3":{"en":"Old arguments resurface by text: the sibling, the neighbour, the thread you left unanswered. Car repairs and commute delays test your temper. Reread before you send, then reread again."},"4":{"en":"Family tempers from years ago come back to the kitchen table, and a half-finished home project demands attention. Finish the repair before starting the renovation; let old rows end differently."},"5":{"en":"An old flame, a dropped creative project or a risk you backed out of comes back for a rematch. Ask whether you still want it, or only want to win."},"6":{"en":"Stalled work and abandoned training plans return. A colleague conflict you thought was over can flare again, and the body asks for recovery more than new records. Fix the routine; don't overhaul it."},"7":{"en":"An old fight with a partner, ex or rival asks for a rematch. Stalled contracts return for new terms. Before you argue, check whether you're fighting this person or someone from before."},"8":{"en":"Old debts, tax questions and unfinished conversations about trust come back. Desire may cool or turn complicated for a while. Settle the paperwork and refuse the old power struggle."},"9":{"en":"A course you quit, a trip that fell through, or a visa or legal matter returns for a second round. Revisit the plan; skip the argument about who was right."},"10":{"en":"Career battles come back: the promotion that went elsewhere, the boss you clashed with, the project that stalled. Rework the pitch quietly; prepare the move now and make it once Mars turns direct."},"11":{"en":"A friendship that cooled after a row, or a group plan that stalled, asks for another look. Rejoin, repair or leave cleanly, but don't restart the old argument by message."},"12":{"en":"Buried anger surfaces at night: in dreams, in insomnia, in a grudge you thought you'd dropped. Work on it privately with a long walk, a therapist or a page of honest writing."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Every two years or so, Mars appears to move backwards for about ten weeks. Drive slows, old anger resurfaces, and stalled projects return. It's a poor time to pick new fights or launch on impulse, and a good one to finish, repair, rebuild fitness and rematch with a better plan."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Mars slows to a halt before turning backwards, and the days around it feel like pressing the accelerator in neutral. Tempers run short; hold off on the fight or the big launch."},"direct":{"en":"Mars stands still and turns forward again. The stalled project, the delayed decision, the conversation you postponed can move, slowly at first. Give it a week before you push at full speed."}}},"jupiter":{"planet":"jupiter","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"You take up more room","text":"Jupiter in your first house opens a year in which you take up more room: people notice you sooner, conversations warm up when you walk in, and starting things feels less like a risk. Part of it is simple permission, because you finally stop waiting to be asked. The trap is size for its own sake: more plans, more yeses, more second helpings than one body and one calendar can carry.","scene":"You turn up to a party where you know nobody and leave with two new numbers and a plan for Thursday.","do":"Start the project you keep calling 'someday'.","avoid":"Saying yes to every offer simply because it flatters you.","ask":"What would you start this year if you trusted your luck?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Your price goes up","text":"With Jupiter in your house of money, this is a year for earning more and, just as often, for spending more. A raise, a better rate or a second client gets easier to go after, because you finally believe your work is worth it. The trap is quiet inflation: the pay rise that vanishes into nicer coffee, a bigger phone and a subscription you forgot you had.","scene":"You quote a higher rate than last year, hold your breath, and the client simply replies, 'Fine, send the invoice.'","do":"Decide now what share of any raise goes straight to savings.","avoid":"Spending this year's raise before the first bigger payslip arrives.","ask":"What would you charge if you were sure your work was worth it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Every errand teaches you something","text":"Jupiter in your third house turns your everyday radius into a classroom: the commute, the group chat, the neighbour, the sibling you only text on birthdays. You learn fastest this year by doing — a short course, a weekend trip, a newsletter you finally start. Curiosity is generous but unfocused, so the risk is twelve open tabs, three half-finished courses and a phone that never stops buzzing.","scene":"On the train home you sign up for a weekend course, then text your brother to ask if he wants to come.","do":"Choose one course or skill and finish it before starting another.","avoid":"Promising things in group chats that you'll have forgotten by Friday.","ask":"What could you learn this year just by doing it every day?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Home gets a bigger table","text":"Jupiter in your fourth house brings growth to the most private part of life: the flat, the family, the place you go when the door closes. It's a classic year for moving, renovating, taking in a relative or making peace with a parent, because you want a base that feels generous rather than merely adequate. The risk is building more house than your life needs, or your budget allows.","scene":"You stand in an empty flat with a tape measure, already deciding where the long table goes and who sits at it.","do":"Spend on the one thing at home you use every single day.","avoid":"Filling the house with guests until there is no room for you.","ask":"What would make your home feel generous rather than just good enough?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Pleasure stops needing an excuse","text":"Jupiter in your fifth house makes this a year of more: more flirting, more making, more nights out, more time on the floor with a child or a project you love. Joy comes easily because you stop rationing it like a reward for finished work. The trap is chasing the high — the bet, the crush, the third bottle — when the quieter pleasure was the real one.","scene":"You post the drawing you nearly deleted, and by evening three strangers have asked whether you take commissions.","do":"Book one evening a week for something you do purely for joy.","avoid":"Raising the stakes every time something starts to feel good.","ask":"What did you love doing before anyone paid or praised you for it?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"More work, better work","text":"Jupiter in your sixth house enlarges the ordinary week: more tasks, more requests, and often a better job or a colleague who teaches you how to do it well. Your body responds fast to small good habits this year — a walk, earlier sleep, a real lunch. The catch is that being useful feels like luck, so you keep saying yes until the calendar has no empty squares left.","scene":"You agree to cover a colleague's project, then notice it's the fourth extra thing you've taken on this month.","do":"Keep one daily habit small enough to do on your worst day.","avoid":"Taking on extra work just because you're the one who can.","ask":"Which part of your workday would you keep even if nobody noticed?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Luck arrives through other people","text":"Jupiter in your seventh house makes this a year when the right other person tips the scales: a partner, a business ally, a good lawyer, a friend who becomes a collaborator. You grow when someone takes you seriously, and you're unusually open to a person who sees more in you than you do. The risk is handing them the steering wheel, or signing a generous-looking contract you haven't read to the end.","scene":"Over coffee, someone you've known for years says, 'We should do this together,' and for once you both mean it.","do":"Read every contract to the last page before you sign it.","avoid":"Mistaking someone's generosity towards you for a plan for your life.","ask":"Who brings out the version of you that you'd like to keep?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Other people's money opens doors","text":"Jupiter in your eighth house brings growth through what you share: a partner's income, an approved loan, a grant, a family sum, a debt that finally shrinks. Closeness deepens too, because you're willing to say what you usually swallow. The trap is that credit feels easy this year, and borrowing on optimism is still borrowing: the bill arrives after the mood has passed.","scene":"You and your partner open the banking app together, and for the first time the conversation ends in a plan instead of a silence.","do":"Before any loan, write down how and when you'll repay it.","avoid":"Borrowing on the strength of a good mood.","ask":"What would you share more freely if you trusted it would come back?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"The map gets bigger","text":"Jupiter is at home in your ninth house, and the year asks for distance: a long flight, a degree, a teacher who rearranges your thinking, the book you finally write. You grow by stepping outside the language and habits you were raised in. The risk is becoming a tourist of meaning, always booking the next trip or course and preaching last month's discovery to people who never asked.","scene":"You spread a map over the kitchen table at midnight and realise you're no longer asking whether to go, only when.","do":"Book the trip or send the application you've circled for over a year.","avoid":"Collecting certificates instead of using what you already know.","ask":"Which place or subject keeps pulling at you, year after year?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Your name travels further","text":"Jupiter at the top of your chart makes this the year your work gets seen: a promotion, a bigger client, a boss who mentions you in rooms you're not in. Ambition feels less like greed and more like an invitation it would be rude to refuse. The trap is taking every title on offer, because a bigger role brings a bigger inbox, and applause is a poor substitute for evenings you no longer have.","scene":"Your manager forwards you an email with one line typed on top: 'They asked for you by name.'","do":"Put your name on the work you've been doing anonymously.","avoid":"Accepting a bigger title without asking what it costs in hours.","ask":"What do you want to be known for in five years?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"The right crowd finds you","text":"Jupiter in your eleventh house fills the year with people: a new circle, a club, a team, a friend of a friend who knows exactly whom you should meet. Plans that felt like daydreams start to look possible once you say them aloud to the right group. The risk is accepting every invitation and ending the year with two hundred contacts and nobody to call at 2 a.m.","scene":"You mention a half-formed idea at a birthday dinner, and someone across the table says, 'I know exactly who you should meet.'","do":"Say your biggest plan aloud to three people who could help.","avoid":"Collecting new contacts while old friends quietly go silent.","ask":"Which friendship do you want to still have in ten years?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Growing where nobody can see","text":"Jupiter in your twelfth house makes this a quieter year, with growth happening offstage: in therapy, in long sleep, in a notebook, in help you give without credit. Things often work out behind the scenes, as if someone were looking after you, which makes retreat feel safe. The trap is when rest turns into hiding — another episode, another glass, another month of not saying what you want.","scene":"You cancel a plan, sleep ten hours, and wake up knowing the answer to something you've circled for months.","do":"Protect one hour a week alone, with no screen.","avoid":"Helping everyone in secret and resenting that nobody notices.","ask":"What are you quietly preparing for that you haven't said out loud?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Jupiter in Aries rewards whoever goes first: new businesses, bold applications, solo starts. Courage is contagious, though far more gets started than finished."},"taurus":{"en":"Jupiter in Taurus grows what you can touch: savings, property, gardens, good bread. Comfort feels earned and solid, while appetites for money and dinner quietly expand."},"gemini":{"en":"Jupiter in Gemini multiplies everything: courses, chats, side projects, opinions. Learning is quick and curiosity generous, but facts and gossip travel at the same speed."},"cancer":{"en":"Jupiter in Cancer brings growth home: families, kitchens, roots, the urge to protect one's own. Generosity flows most easily towards kin, and nostalgia sells unusually well."},"leo":{"en":"Jupiter in Leo makes generosity theatrical: big gestures, brave creative work, birthday parties that get out of hand. Warmth spreads fast, and so does the appetite for applause."},"virgo":{"en":"Jupiter in Virgo grows things by improving them: better systems, cleaner diets, useful skills, honest work. Progress lives in the details, next to the urge to fix everyone."},"libra":{"en":"Jupiter in Libra favours partnerships, contracts, weddings and good design. Diplomacy pays, fairness becomes fashionable, and plenty of people say yes just to keep the peace."},"scorpio":{"en":"Jupiter in Scorpio deepens rather than widens: investments, inheritances, therapy, research, long-kept secrets. People grow by facing what scares them, and power gathers in fewer hands."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Jupiter in Sagittarius is at home: travel, study, publishing, faith and big opinions all flourish. Optimism runs high, with a matching taste for preaching."},"capricorn":{"en":"Jupiter in Capricorn grows only what is earned: careers, institutions, long-term plans. Luck looks like hard work paying off, and optimism wears a suit and checks the budget."},"aquarius":{"en":"Jupiter in Aquarius grows through networks: communities, technology, causes, unlikely friendships. The future feels shared and exciting, though ideals can outrun the people meant to live by them."},"pisces":{"en":"Jupiter in Pisces makes compassion generous and boundaries thin: art, music, charity, faith, long sleep. Kindness spreads easily, but so do escapism and wishful thinking."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"For about four months each year Jupiter turns retrograde, and growth goes inward. Outside luck slows; the real work is review — the course, the move, the yes you gave too fast. Check whether what you're growing is still what you want, and keep only that."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Jupiter stands still and turns retrograde. Big plans lose some momentum for a few months, which makes this a good moment to stop adding and check what you've already said yes to."},"direct":{"en":"Jupiter stations direct. The plans you've been reconsidering can move again, now with better judgement. Pick the one that survived your doubts and give it a real start this month."}}},"saturn":{"planet":"saturn","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Becoming someone you can rely on","text":"Saturn crossing your first house is a chapter of a couple of years in which life asks you to grow up a little more in public. You may feel heavier, more tested, less able to coast on charm. What you build now — a body you look after, a way of saying no, a reputation for finishing — becomes the foundation of the next decade.","scene":"You turn down a fun but pointless plan, and for once you don't feel the need to over-explain why.","do":"Pick one commitment to yourself and keep it every day this week.","avoid":"Mistaking tiredness for proof that you're failing.","ask":"What would the most reliable version of you do differently this month?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Putting a floor under your money","text":"Saturn in your second house is a slow lesson, over two or three years, in what money is actually for. Income can feel capped and every purchase gets weighed, because some part of you is braced for not having enough. Used well, this chapter builds a floor: savings you don't touch, a price you can defend, a worth that isn't your balance. The trap is stinginess, with others and with yourself.","scene":"You walk past something you'd have bought without thinking a year ago, and the small 'no' feels surprisingly good.","do":"Write down what 'enough' means to you, in real numbers.","avoid":"Undercharging because asking for more feels like tempting fate.","ask":"What do you buy to feel safe, and does it work?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Words start to carry weight","text":"Saturn in your third house slows the fast lane of life: messages, errands, the commute, the sibling who suddenly needs you. You think twice before you hit send, because careless words now cost more than they used to. It's the right chapter for a hard, slow skill — a language, a driving test, a qualification. The risk is staying silent until you sound perfect.","scene":"You rewrite a two-line message to your sister three times, cut the sarcasm, and for once the reply is kind.","do":"Give one hard skill fifteen minutes a day, every day.","avoid":"Sending important messages late at night, angry or exhausted.","ask":"What would you say more often if you weren't afraid of sounding wrong?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Fixing the roof yourself","text":"Saturn in your fourth house puts weight on the foundations: the lease or mortgage, the boiler, the parent who needs more from you, the family rule you've outgrown. Home can feel more like a job than a refuge, because you're now fixing what used to be fixed for you. What you build here holds for decades. The trap is running your home the way a strict parent would.","scene":"You sit at your parents' kitchen table with their bills spread out, and realise you're the one explaining things now.","do":"Fix the one thing at home you've been stepping around for months.","avoid":"Carrying the family's problems as if nobody else could.","ask":"Which family rule are you still obeying that no longer fits your life?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Turning play into craft","text":"Saturn in your fifth house turns pleasure into a decision: the hobby becomes a craft, the romance asks for commitment, a child needs a firmer you. Fun can go flat for a while, because a fear of being judged sits in the front row whenever you play. The reward is creative work you're proud of, built slowly, and a love that survives an ordinary Tuesday.","scene":"You practise the same song every evening for a month, badly, and one night it suddenly sounds like music.","do":"Put creative practice in your calendar like a meeting you can't move.","avoid":"Quitting something you love because you're not good at it yet.","ask":"What would you make if nobody you knew ever saw it?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Routine becomes your backbone","text":"Saturn in your sixth house makes the daily grind the main subject: a heavier workload, a demanding manager, a body that stops forgiving late nights and skipped lunches. Your back, teeth or sleep may send the bill for years of 'I'll deal with it later'. The good news is that habits started now stick. The trap is proving your worth in overtime, as if exhaustion were a qualification.","scene":"You book the dentist appointment you've postponed for two years, and then, while you're at it, the physiotherapist.","do":"Fix your bedtime and keep it, weekends included.","avoid":"Skipping the check-up because you're too busy to be ill.","ask":"Which daily habit would your body thank you for in five years?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Promises you can actually keep","text":"Saturn in your seventh house tests how much weight your closest bonds can carry: the relationship, the business partner, the deal you've lived on without writing down. Over these two or three years, half-promises stop holding, so you commit, renegotiate or walk away. Part of you fears being trapped and part fears being left, and both make you go quiet. Whatever survives this chapter is built to last.","scene":"You and your partner sit down with a notepad and finally say out loud who pays for what, and who does what.","do":"Put one unspoken agreement with your partner into plain words.","avoid":"Keeping the peace by not saying what you need.","ask":"What are you willing to promise, and what are you no longer willing to?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Paying down what you owe","text":"Saturn in your eighth house brings the paperwork of closeness: the loan, the tax return, the joint account, sometimes a will or an estate to sort out. It's a chapter for paying down debts, money and otherwise, slowly and on schedule. Intimacy gets more honest, because trust now grows only as fast as it's earned, on both sides. The trap is controlling everything so nothing can hurt you.","scene":"You make the last payment on a card you've carried for years, then sit in the car for a minute, oddly emotional.","do":"List every debt you have, with dates, on one page.","avoid":"Lending money you can't afford to lose just to keep the peace.","ask":"Who has earned your trust slowly, and have you told them?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Earning the right to an opinion","text":"Saturn in your ninth house turns big ideas into long work: the degree, the visa, the legal case, the book that takes three drafts. Beliefs you inherited get tested against real life, and some don't survive, which can feel lonelier than doubt ever did. This is the chapter in which you stop quoting other people and start becoming someone worth quoting. The risk is rigidity: choosing a rulebook over thinking.","scene":"At eleven at night you close the textbook and realise you can now explain what baffled you three months ago.","do":"Commit to one long course of study and set a weekly schedule.","avoid":"Defending a belief you've never tested yourself.","ask":"Which of your opinions have you actually earned?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"The title comes with weight","text":"Saturn at the top of your chart is the harvest of years of work, and the audit. Responsibility lands on you — a bigger role, a team, a decision with your name on it — and whatever was built on shortcuts shows its cracks. You feel watched, because you are: people now judge you by your record, not your promise. Stay steady and this chapter gives you the authority you once had to ask for.","scene":"In a meeting, the room goes quiet and turns to you, and you realise they're waiting for your decision, not your opinion.","do":"Finish what has your name on it before starting anything new.","avoid":"Taking every criticism as a verdict on your whole career.","ask":"Which responsibility are you ready to carry, and which should you hand back?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Fewer friends, truer ones","text":"Saturn in your eleventh house thins the crowd: some friendships fade, a group chat goes quiet, and the circle that's left is smaller and sturdier. You may also find yourself running things — the committee, the team, the shared project nobody else will organise. The loneliness of this chapter is real but useful, because it shows you who turns up. Long-term hopes get serious too: fewer of them, with real dates attached.","scene":"You notice it's the same three friends who always reply, always show up and stay to help clear the table.","do":"Turn up, in person, for the friends who always turn up for you.","avoid":"Keeping friendships alive out of guilt rather than warmth.","ask":"Who would you trust with your house keys, and do they know?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Closing the old chapter properly","text":"Saturn in your twelfth house is the quiet end of a long cycle: a couple of years for finishing, clearing out and sleeping more than you'd admit. Old fears and unsaid things surface at 3 a.m., not to punish you but because they were never dealt with. Close old accounts: the therapy, the apology, the boxes from your last move. The mistake would be launching something big before the old is done.","scene":"You finally open the drawer of letters you've avoided for a year and, one envelope at a time, deal with them.","do":"Finish or honestly drop one old project this month.","avoid":"Drowning out the quiet with noise, plans and screens.","ask":"What are you still carrying that you could put down this year?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Saturn in Aries slows the sprint: fresh starts must be built to last, and leaders get judged by what they finish. Impatience costs more; disciplined courage pays."},"taurus":{"en":"Saturn in Taurus makes money, land and food serious: budgets tighten, prices get scrutinised, and value is measured by what lasts. Security is built slowly, by hand."},"gemini":{"en":"Saturn in Gemini disciplines information: rules for schools, media and platforms tighten. Fewer words carry more weight, and learning gets slower, deeper and more exact."},"cancer":{"en":"Saturn in Cancer puts weight on home and family: housing costs, ageing parents, the care nobody pays for. Feelings get guarded; belonging has to be built on purpose."},"leo":{"en":"Saturn in Leo asks for authority without applause: talent has to become craft, leaders must earn their stage, and pride gets tested. Even joy takes discipline."},"virgo":{"en":"Saturn in Virgo tightens the daily systems: health care, working conditions, standards, small print. Craft and reliability earn respect again, while perfectionism and worry run high."},"libra":{"en":"Saturn in Libra puts relationships and agreements under review: contracts, courts, marriages, alliances. Fairness becomes something built in writing, not just expected."},"scorpio":{"en":"Saturn in Scorpio drags debts, taxes, power and secrets into hard light. Trust is earned slowly, and whatever was hidden tends to come due."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Saturn in Sagittarius tests beliefs against facts: universities, courts, churches and borders face scrutiny. Optimism needs evidence, and teachers must prove what they preach."},"capricorn":{"en":"Saturn in Capricorn is at home: institutions, careers and long plans get rebuilt from the foundations. Hard work is respected, shortcuts collapse, and ambition grows up."},"aquarius":{"en":"Saturn in Aquarius builds the future by committee: new rules for technology, communities and networks. Ideals have to become working systems, and independence learns to cooperate."},"pisces":{"en":"Saturn in Pisces puts edges on what usually drifts: care work, art, faith, sleep, the screen at 2 a.m. Compassion needs limits, and dreams need a schedule."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"For four to five months each year Saturn turns retrograde, and the inspection moves indoors. What you've built — the routine, the promise, the five-year plan — gets quietly stress-tested. Fix what's cracking before it becomes a crisis, and hand back the jobs that were never yours."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Saturn stands still and turns retrograde. For a few days deadlines feel heavier and old responsibilities come back for review. Take nothing new on; reinforce whatever is already carrying weight."},"direct":{"en":"Saturn stations direct after months of review. What you repaired can carry weight again. Sign, commit, set the schedule: decisions made now tend to hold for a long time."}}},"uranus":{"planet":"uranus","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Becoming harder to predict","text":"Uranus in your first house is roughly seven years in which the person you show the world stops fitting. A haircut, a new handle online, a body you treat differently, a sudden “I'm not doing that anymore” — changes come in jolts, not plans. Underneath is a need to look like who you've become, not who you were. The risk is rebelling against people who were only describing you.","scene":"You sit in the hairdresser's chair asking for the cut you've wanted for years, and their hesitation only makes you surer.","do":"Drop one habit you keep only because people expect it.","avoid":"Torching good things just to prove you're free.","ask":"Which part of how people see you no longer feels true?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Income that refuses to sit still","text":"For about seven years Uranus jolts your second house, and money stops arriving in the shape you were raised to expect. A salary turns into invoices, a side project out-earns the job, a windfall and a lost contract land in the same season. You want to earn in a way that feels like yours, not merely safe. The risk is reading every swing as a sign to quit.","scene":"You compare this month's income with last month's, find no pattern at all, and feel more curious than scared.","do":"Open a separate savings pot for the lean months.","avoid":"Selling something you love in a panicked week.","ask":"What would you earn money doing if nobody needed to approve it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Your mind takes a new route","text":"These years Uranus runs through your house of messages, neighbours and siblings, and your mind gets restless with its old routes. You learn a skill from videos at 1 am, rethink a view you've held since school, find a sibling suddenly easier or harder to talk to. Your thinking speeds up because it's bored, not because it's sure. The risk is sending the message while it's still hot.","scene":"On the bus you have an idea so sharp you voice-note yourself three times before your stop.","do":"Write the idea down tonight, send it tomorrow.","avoid":"Picking fights in the comments just to feel awake.","ask":"Which opinion of yours is older than your current life?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"The home that keeps rearranging","text":"Uranus crossing your fourth house is roughly seven years in which home refuses to stay put. You move more than you planned, a parent's situation changes overnight, someone moves in or out, the home office quietly swallows the flat. Part of you wants roots and part of you wants a door you can walk out of. The risk is calling it freedom when you're really dodging one hard conversation at home.","scene":"You're packing boxes again, wrapping the same mugs in newspaper, and realise you've stopped hanging pictures because you assume you'll leave.","do":"Hang one picture, even in a flat you won't keep.","avoid":"Making every family change a reason to pack a bag.","ask":"What does home need to be now, not when you were ten?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Falling for what you didn't plan","text":"This seven-year stretch of Uranus in your fifth house rewrites the script for romance, play and making things. Attraction arrives fast and strange: someone outside your type, a long-distance thing, a hobby that takes over your weekends for a year and then vanishes. You want to be surprised by your own life, because predictable has started to feel like old. The risk is chasing the jolt and calling it love.","scene":"You sign up for a pottery class on a whim and leave with clay under your nails and someone's number.","do":"Book one thing this week that you'd normally talk yourself out of.","avoid":"Blowing up something steady just because it's become familiar.","ask":"When did you last surprise yourself, and what were you doing?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"The routine you can't stand anymore","text":"These are the years Uranus rewires your sixth house: the job, the calendar, the body that has to keep up. Nine-to-five starts to feel like a cage, a new tool changes how you work overnight, your sleep or nerves demand a schedule you didn't choose. You work best when nobody stands over you. The risk is quitting the job when only the timetable needed to change.","scene":"You move your laptop to the kitchen at 6 am because it's the only hour nobody can ask you for anything.","do":"Rearrange one fixed hour of your day to suit your body.","avoid":"Treating every new rule at work as a personal insult.","ask":"Which part of your workday would you keep if you could redesign it?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Closeness that needs more air","text":"For around seven years Uranus sits in your house of partners and one-to-one deals, and closeness has to make room for freedom. You're drawn to people who won't be pinned down, a partner suddenly changes jobs or cities, a contract ends early or a new one starts in a week. You want someone beside you, not breathing down your neck. The risk is slamming a door that only needed to open wider.","scene":"Your partner books a solo trip, and you notice the first feeling is not hurt but a strange, quiet envy.","do":"Say out loud how much time alone you need each week.","avoid":"Ending a relationship by text to skip the hard conversation.","ask":"What kind of freedom would let you stay?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Sudden turns in what you share","text":"Uranus moving through your eighth house is a seven-year stretch of jolts in what you share: a joint account, a loan, a partner's income, the trust you hand someone in bed. An inheritance, a tax bill or a debt you clear in one go can change the maths overnight. Underneath is a refusal to feel owned, by a lender or by a lover. The risk is cutting ties before reading the small print.","scene":"You finally read the loan agreement line by line and realise you've been paying for a life you left years ago.","do":"List every shared account and subscription you're still tied to.","avoid":"Signing anything joint in a week you feel reckless.","ask":"Whose money or approval do you still feel owned by?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Outgrowing what you were taught","text":"Uranus in your ninth house spends some seven years redrawing the map of what you believe. A last-minute ticket stretches into months abroad, an online course replaces the degree you never finished, a faith or politics you grew up with stops making sense in one conversation. You learn fastest when you're slightly lost. The risk is swapping one dogma for a shinier one.","scene":"You're in a city where you can't read the signs, and for the first time in years your head goes quiet.","do":"Sign up for the course you keep bookmarking.","avoid":"Lecturing friends about the worldview you adopted last month.","ask":"Which belief did you inherit rather than choose?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"A career that changes lanes","text":"Uranus in your tenth house is a seven-year chapter in which your career refuses to follow a ladder. You change fields, go freelance, get restructured out of a role you'd outgrown anyway, become known for a side skill rather than the title. You'd rather be strange and respected than safe and invisible, so bosses who need control feel unbearable. The risk is burning a reference you'll want in two years.","scene":"Someone asks what you do for a living, and the honest answer takes three sentences and makes you grin.","do":"Write down the work you'd do if job titles didn't exist.","avoid":"Quitting in the meeting instead of after the plan.","ask":"What do you want to be known for that isn't on your CV?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Finding your strange people","text":"Uranus is at home in your eleventh house of friends and future plans, and for seven years or so your circle reshuffles. Old friends drift as your life changes speed, and new ones arrive through a forum, a protest, a running club, a late-night side project. You need people who don't flinch at the version of you that's coming. The risk is dropping loyal friends because they're no longer exciting.","scene":"You leave a group chat you've muted for a year and join a much odder one the same evening.","do":"Go once to the meetup you keep scrolling past.","avoid":"Measuring old friendships by how new they still feel.","ask":"Who gets excited when you describe the future you want?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Breaking the pattern nobody sees","text":"Uranus in your twelfth house is a quiet seven years with sudden flashes in the dark. Sleep goes strange, insights arrive at 3 am, a stranger's offhand remark cracks open a habit you've repeated since childhood. Much of the rebellion is private, because you'd rather not be watched while you're half-changed. The risk is lying awake with the realisation instead of acting on it in daylight.","scene":"You wake at 3:40, see the old pattern with total clarity, and type it into your notes before it fades.","do":"Keep a notebook by the bed and use it tonight.","avoid":"Scrolling in the dark to drown out the restlessness.","ask":"Which habit would you break if nobody ever found out?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Uranus in Aries breaks things open fast: start-ups, protests, solo ventures, a hunger to be first. Patience runs thin, and new ideas arrive with elbows out."},"taurus":{"en":"Uranus in Taurus jolts money, food and land: new currencies, unstable prices, farming rethought. What felt solid turns out to be negotiable, especially what's in your wallet."},"gemini":{"en":"Uranus in Gemini rewires how we talk, learn and get around: new devices, AI in every inbox, faster news, transport rethought. Attention scatters; minds change mid-sentence."},"cancer":{"en":"Uranus in Cancer rearranges home and family: new ways of living together, homes that double as offices, kinship chosen, not inherited. Belonging gets redefined at the kitchen table."},"leo":{"en":"Uranus in Leo electrifies fame, art and play: new kinds of celebrity, rebellious self-expression, children raised to stand out. Everyone wants a stage, and the stage keeps moving."},"virgo":{"en":"Uranus in Virgo reinvents work and health: new tools at the desk, alternative medicine, wellness gadgets, jobs automated. Routines get rebuilt, often around a machine."},"libra":{"en":"Uranus in Libra rewrites marriage and partnership: divorce becomes ordinary, new kinds of couple appear, fairness gets argued in public. Relationships need room to breathe."},"scorpio":{"en":"Uranus in Scorpio cracks taboos open: sexual revolutions, financial shocks, secrets leaked overnight. What was buried comes up without warning."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Uranus in Sagittarius rattles belief and borders: cheap flights, new religions, global study, information crossing every frontier. Restlessness for the wider world becomes a generation's signature."},"capricorn":{"en":"Uranus in Capricorn shakes institutions: banks wobble, governments get tested, old hierarchies crack. Careers stop following ladders, and authority has to earn respect again."},"aquarius":{"en":"Uranus in Aquarius, its own sign, speeds up the future: networks, online communities, new social movements, technology that rewires friendship. Being different becomes a group identity."},"pisces":{"en":"Uranus in Pisces unsettles art, faith and escape: virtual worlds, new spiritual movements, music and film reinvented. The line between real and imagined gets strange."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Every year Uranus spends about five months appearing to move backwards. The urge for change goes underground: plans to quit, move or break free get tested in private before they're acted on. It's a good season to rethink a rebellion, finish an experiment, or notice which freedom you actually want."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Uranus stands still before turning back, and restlessness spikes for a week or two: urges to quit, cut, move or blurt the truth. Note them down; act on the ones still burning in a month."},"direct":{"en":"Uranus turns forward again after months of inner rehearsal. Changes you've been quietly planning — the move, the new job, the clean break — start to feel possible in daylight. Begin with the smallest irreversible step."}}},"neptune":{"planet":"neptune","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Harder to pin down, even to yourself","text":"Neptune in your first house is a misty decade or more in which the edges of who you are soften. People see what they want in you, and because blending in feels kinder than disagreeing, you become the mirror of whoever's in the room. Your body grows more sensitive: to coffee, alcohol, crowds, a sad film. The risk is losing your outline so slowly you don't notice it going.","scene":"You catch your reflection in a shop window and, for a second, can't decide whether you look like yourself.","do":"Say one clear preference out loud today, even about lunch.","avoid":"Agreeing with everyone and calling it being easygoing.","ask":"Who are you when nobody is looking at you?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"The banking app you avoid opening","text":"For well over a decade Neptune washes through your second house, and money turns foggy. You give generously, undercharge for work you love, avoid looking at your account for weeks and then wonder where it went. Part of you suspects that caring about money would make you less kind. The risk is letting the fog set your worth, when a spreadsheet would do it better.","scene":"You pay for everyone's drinks again, then check your balance in the taxi and feel a small cold drop.","do":"Look at your last month of spending, all of it, tonight.","avoid":"Working for free because asking for money feels unkind.","ask":"What would you charge if you believed your work was worth it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Hearing the tone, missing the detail","text":"For more than a decade Neptune drifts through your third house, and your thinking turns more image than list. You daydream on the commute, write better at midnight than at a desk, and miss the detail in a message everyone else caught, because you're listening to tone, not words. A sibling or neighbour can feel close one month and unreadable the next. The risk is replying to what you imagined someone meant.","scene":"You reread a short text from your sister four times, each time hearing a different tone of voice.","do":"Ask what they meant before you write back.","avoid":"Signing something you've only skimmed on your phone.","ask":"Which conversation are you having only in your head?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Home that lives in memory","text":"Neptune in your fourth house is a long chapter in which home becomes partly a feeling you chase. You may live far from where you grew up, care for a parent whose needs are hard to see clearly, or cook your grandmother's soup just to smell her kitchen again. What you miss is often a time, not a place. The risk is waiting for the perfect home and never unpacking this one.","scene":"You stand in a new flat that's perfectly fine and still feel homesick for somewhere you can't quite name.","do":"Make one corner of this home unmistakably yours tonight.","avoid":"Taking on a parent's sadness as if it were yours.","ask":"What did home smell, sound or taste like when you felt safe?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Falling for the person you imagine","text":"Neptune in your fifth house is a decade or more when romance, art and play all go soft-focus. You fall for who someone could be, write songs or stories you didn't know were in you, and lose whole evenings to films, wine or a crush who never quite texts back. You'd rather be moved than be sure. The risk is loving the dream so hard you miss the person in front of you.","scene":"You've built a whole future with someone from three conversations, and you already know which song would play at the wedding.","do":"Spend one evening making something, not consuming something.","avoid":"Rescuing a lover and calling it romance.","ask":"Do you like this person, or the story you tell about them?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Days that won't hold their shape","text":"Neptune's long stay in your sixth house, fourteen years or so, dissolves the edges of your workday. Job descriptions go vague, you end up doing the emotional chores nobody put in your contract, and your body reacts to things it used to shrug off: caffeine, late screens, a colleague's bad mood. You absorb the room before you notice you've done it. The risk is burning out quietly while calling it being helpful.","scene":"You stay late fixing a colleague's mistake, tell yourself it's nothing, and then can't sleep for the headache.","do":"Write tomorrow's three tasks on paper, and log off at six.","avoid":"Taking on a coworker's mood as your own job.","ask":"Which part of your day leaves you drained, and why?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"The partner you keep idealising","text":"Neptune in your seventh house is a long era, often fourteen years, in which close relationships are soaked in longing. You see the best in a partner, sometimes a version only you can see, and drift toward people who need saving or who seem to read your mind. Agreements stay unspoken because spelling them out feels unromantic. The risk is forgiving the same thing so often it stops being forgiveness.","scene":"Your partner forgets the thing again, and you're already explaining to yourself why it isn't really their fault.","do":"Say one expectation out loud, plainly, without softening it.","avoid":"Mistaking being needed for being loved.","ask":"What do you keep forgiving that you've never actually discussed?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Where you end and they begin","text":"For a decade and more Neptune moves through your eighth house, and the line between yours and theirs goes blurry. Joint money gets vague, a loan to a friend turns into a gift nobody discussed, an inheritance drags on in paperwork and old family feelings. In intimacy you want to dissolve completely, and you can lose yourself in the trying. The risk is trusting a feeling where a written agreement belongs.","scene":"You lend money to someone you love, and neither of you mentions it again, though you think about it every month.","do":"Put one shared money arrangement in writing this week.","avoid":"Paying someone's debt to avoid a painful conversation.","ask":"What have you handed over that you'd like to have back?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Searching for something to believe","text":"Neptune in your ninth house is a long era of searching: for a teacher, a faith, a place that feels like the answer. You read late into the night, book a retreat, fall for a city before you've seen it in winter, or quietly lose a belief that held you up for years. You want meaning to arrive whole. The risk is handing your judgement to the first voice that sounds certain.","scene":"You watch a lecture at midnight, then another, and wake up having half-planned a move to a country you've never visited.","do":"Check one claim you've accepted before you share it.","avoid":"Following a teacher who discourages questions.","ask":"What are you hoping someone else will finally explain for you?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Work that has to mean something","text":"Neptune spends well over a decade in your tenth house, and success stops being enough unless it means something. A career that looks good on paper feels hollow, while work in care, art, film or a cause pulls at you even when it pays less. Your public image gets harder to control: people project onto you, for better and worse. The risk is waiting for a calling instead of drafting a plan.","scene":"A recruiter offers more money, and you hear yourself asking whether the job will help anyone.","do":"Write the next practical step toward the work you dream about.","avoid":"Letting a boss's charm stand in for a contract.","ask":"What would meaningful work look like on an ordinary Tuesday?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Giving yourself to a cause","text":"Neptune in your eleventh house is a long era in which friendship and the future you dream of blur together. You give hours to a cause, a choir, a volunteer group or an online circle that feels like belonging. Being needed feels so much like being wanted that you miss which friends only call when they want something. The risk is giving everything to a group that never asked what you need.","scene":"You volunteer to organise the group's fundraiser again, though last year you cried in the car afterwards.","do":"Tell one friend honestly what you need from them.","avoid":"Saying yes to every group request to feel included.","ask":"Which friendships give back, and which ones only take?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"The quiet that refills you","text":"Neptune in your twelfth house, its own territory, is a long era with thin walls between your feelings and everyone else's. Dreams get vivid, you cry at adverts, you need more sleep and more hours alone than people around you understand. Solitude refills you, but a bottle, a feed or a show at 2 am can feel the same from the inside. The risk is escaping when you only needed to rest.","scene":"You cancel plans, turn off every light but one, and feel the week drain out of your shoulders.","do":"Book one evening alone with no screen and no drink.","avoid":"Calling it rest when it's really hiding.","ask":"What are you trying not to feel when you reach for the phone?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Neptune in Aries dreams in the shape of courage: new heroes, faith in starting over, ideals that demand action. The line between bravery and recklessness blurs."},"taurus":{"en":"Neptune in Taurus romanticises land, food and the body: a longing for slow living, real bread, money that feels solid. Comfort becomes a kind of faith."},"gemini":{"en":"Neptune in Gemini blurs words and facts: rumours travel faster than news, stories feel truer than data, and everyone talks at once. Language turns dreamy and slippery."},"cancer":{"en":"Neptune in Cancer idealises home, homeland and mother: nostalgia runs high, families become sanctuaries or myths, and the longing to belong somewhere is everywhere."},"leo":{"en":"Neptune in Leo turns glamour into faith: film idols, grand romance, the spotlight as salvation. A generation learns to long for the great love story."},"virgo":{"en":"Neptune in Virgo dreams through work and health: duty as devotion, cures and diets as hope, service as a calling. Worry and perfectionism seep into ordinary days."},"libra":{"en":"Neptune in Libra idealises love and fairness: peace songs, soulmates, the dream of the perfect partnership. Harmony is worshipped, and conflict gets quietly avoided."},"scorpio":{"en":"Neptune in Scorpio romanticises the forbidden: sex, death, secrets, the occult. Intensity passes for love, and fear and desire blur in the collective imagination."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Neptune in Sagittarius dreams of the whole world: gap years, gurus, globalisation, faith in a future without borders. Belief spreads easily, and so does wishful thinking."},"capricorn":{"en":"Neptune in Capricorn dissolves trust in institutions: banks, money and governments turn out to be stories we agreed to believe. Success is idealised, then quietly doubted."},"aquarius":{"en":"Neptune in Aquarius dreams of connection through machines: online utopias, global networks, faith in technology to save us. Belonging moves online, and loneliness follows it there."},"pisces":{"en":"Neptune in Pisces, its own sign, floods the collective with feeling: streaming, escapism, spiritual searching, compassion for strangers. Boundaries soften, and fact and fiction blur."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"For about five months each year Neptune appears to move backwards, and the fog thins a little. Illusions you've been living inside become easier to see: the job, the person, the habit you romanticised. It's a season for honest reality checks, quieter faith and fewer rescues."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Neptune pauses before turning back, and the haze thickens for a while: dreams get loud, motives blur, and it's easy to believe what you'd like to. Delay big promises until it clears."},"direct":{"en":"Neptune turns forward, and imagination flows outward again. Ideals you tested in private can go into the world now: the song, the cause, the generous act. Keep the reality checks you learned."}}},"pluto":{"planet":"pluto","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Shedding the person you were","text":"Pluto crossing your first house is one of the longest chapters of your life, often fifteen years or more, and what it rebuilds is you. The body changes, sometimes through illness, sometimes through discipline, and so does the way people react when you walk in. You become more intense, harder to fool, less willing to perform. The risk is controlling everything about yourself because the change frightens you.","scene":"Someone from school doesn't recognise you at first, and you realise you don't miss the person they remember.","do":"Stop doing one thing you only do to seem harmless.","avoid":"Treating every comment about your looks as an attack.","ask":"What part of your old self are you ready to bury?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Rebuilding what you're worth","text":"Pluto in your second house is a long era in which money stops being neutral and becomes a question of power. You may lose an income and rebuild it from nothing, clear out possessions you've carried for a decade, or chase a number in your account until it feels like safety. Underneath is the fear of ever depending on anyone again. The risk is turning savings into a fortress with no door.","scene":"You check your savings for the third time today, not to spend them, just to feel the floor under your feet.","do":"Name the exact amount that would make you feel safe.","avoid":"Using money to control the people who depend on you.","ask":"What did you learn about money the day you felt powerless?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Saying the thing nobody says","text":"For a good fifteen years Pluto works through your third house, and the way you think and talk gets taken apart, piece by piece. You research things obsessively, notice what people avoid saying, and small talk starts to feel like lying. A sibling rivalry, an old family story or a neighbour feud comes up for a final reckoning. The risk is using your sharper words as weapons.","scene":"Your brother says one sentence at dinner, and twenty years of family history suddenly rearranges itself in your head.","do":"Ask the question you've avoided asking your sibling.","avoid":"Winning an argument by saying the cruellest true thing.","ask":"Which family story have you never questioned out loud?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"What ends with you","text":"Pluto in your fourth house is a deep chapter in which the foundations of home and family get dug up and relaid. A parent ages, a house is sold, an old secret surfaces at the kitchen table. You carry family habits older than you, from the silences to the tempers, and this is the era to decide which end with you. The risk is fighting for control of a home instead of building one.","scene":"You clear out your parents' attic and find yourself keeping a single cracked cup and nothing else.","do":"Name one family habit you refuse to pass on.","avoid":"Turning a house into a battlefield over who's in charge.","ask":"Which family rule are you still obeying without meaning to?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Desire with teeth","text":"Pluto in your fifth house is a long era in which love, pleasure and creative work become all-or-nothing. A romance takes over your life, a project eats your weekends for years, becoming a parent or seeing your child through a hard year rearranges your priorities. You want to be changed by what you love, so half-hearted fun feels like a waste. The risk is mistaking obsession and jealousy for proof of love.","scene":"You check whether they've seen your story, then check again, and hate how much the answer matters.","do":"Pour tonight's intensity into something you make, not someone you watch.","avoid":"Testing a lover's loyalty to feel in control.","ask":"What do you want so much that it frightens you?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Rebuilding the body and the workday","text":"For fifteen years or more Pluto grinds through your sixth house, and daily life is stripped to the studs and rebuilt. Exhaustion or a doctor's warning makes you change how you eat and sleep for good, a workplace power struggle forces you out or up, a habit you've hidden for years finally has to go. You crave control of your routine because chaos once cost you. The risk is turning health into a punishment.","scene":"You throw the cigarettes in the bin at the bus stop and know, this time, you won't buy more.","do":"Change one daily habit and tell nobody until it sticks.","avoid":"Fighting a colleague for control of a project nobody owns.","ask":"Which habit runs you, rather than the other way round?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Who holds the power between you","text":"Pluto in your seventh house is a long era in which close relationships become the place you're remade. A marriage deepens or ends, a business partner turns rival, someone gets under your skin so completely you can't go back. Every bond turns into a quiet tug-of-war over who needs whom more, because you've learned what it costs to be the one who needs. The risk is controlling a partner to avoid being left.","scene":"You win the argument about whose turn it is to compromise, and the flat feels colder than before.","do":"Tell your partner one need without attaching a condition.","avoid":"Keeping score of who apologised first.","ask":"What are you afraid would happen if you stopped holding the reins?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"What you owe and what you inherit","text":"Pluto in your eighth house is on home ground, a long era in which shared money, intimacy and loss go all the way down. An inheritance, a divorce settlement or a debt can force a total rethink, and grief can change who you trust. Sex and closeness stop being casual because you want someone to see the parts you hide. The risk is using secrets or money as a hold over someone.","scene":"You sit with a solicitor going through a parent's papers and learn more about them in an hour than in thirty years.","do":"Write down every debt and who it binds you to.","avoid":"Signing away your share to end an argument faster.","ask":"What would you let someone see if you trusted them fully?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Beliefs that burn down and regrow","text":"Over fifteen or twenty years Pluto moves through your ninth house, and the worldview you were handed is torn down. A move abroad changes far more than your address, a degree or a long legal fight eats years, a faith you held breaks and something tougher grows in its place. You need answers you've earned, not borrowed. The risk is becoming as rigid about the new truth as you were about the old.","scene":"You defend a view you'd have mocked ten years ago, and notice you're not embarrassed, just sure.","do":"Read one serious argument against what you now believe.","avoid":"Converting friends to the truth that saved you.","ask":"Which belief would you still hold if it cost you something?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Ambition that wants real power","text":"Pluto in your tenth house is often the better part of two decades in which your career becomes the arena where you're tested. You may climb fast, lose a role you'd built your identity on, or end up in charge of the people who once ran you. Ambition sharpens because being powerless at work feels like being powerless everywhere. The risk is becoming the boss you swore you'd never be.","scene":"Your old boss emails asking for advice, and you take a long, slightly too satisfied moment before replying.","do":"Write down what you'd do with power you already have.","avoid":"Staying in a role because leaving feels like losing.","ask":"What would success look like if nobody had to lose?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Fewer friends, truer ones","text":"Pluto spends two decades or so in your eleventh house, and your circle gets cut back to the roots. Friendships that run on habit end, sometimes painfully, while a few deepen into something close to family, and a movement or cause can become your life. Shallow belonging starts to feel lonelier than being alone. The risk is letting a group decide who you're allowed to be.","scene":"You realise the friend you see every week hasn't asked about your life in months, and you stop making excuses for it.","do":"Tell one friend what they've meant to you, specifically.","avoid":"Staying in a group out of fear of being talked about.","ask":"Which friendship would survive you telling the whole truth?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"What lives in the basement","text":"Pluto in your twelfth house is a long, underground era in which the real work happens where nobody can see it. Old fears surface in dreams, therapy goes deeper than you planned, a compulsion you've kept private loses its grip or tightens it. You've survived by keeping certain things locked away, and they want out. The risk is guarding the secret so hard it starts to run your days.","scene":"You finally tell one person the thing you swore you'd take to the grave, and the ceiling stays where it is.","do":"Write the unsayable thing on paper, then decide who sees it.","avoid":"Feeding a private compulsion and calling it coping.","ask":"What are you still protecting that no longer protects you?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Pluto in Aries reforges power through force and will: new leaders, new weapons, pioneers who refuse permission. Courage is tested, and so is the hunger to dominate."},"taurus":{"en":"Pluto in Taurus rebuilds wealth and land: who owns the soil, the money, the food supply. Old fortunes fall, and new ones dig in for generations."},"gemini":{"en":"Pluto in Gemini turns information into power: printing, propaganda, wars over who controls the message. Words become weapons, and literacy becomes freedom."},"cancer":{"en":"Pluto in Cancer strips home and homeland to the bone: displaced families, rebuilt nations, food and shelter as matters of survival. Belonging becomes a fight."},"leo":{"en":"Pluto in Leo concentrates power in personalities: stars, strongmen, youth cultures that demand to be seen. Self-expression becomes a matter of pride and survival."},"virgo":{"en":"Pluto in Virgo overhauls work and health: automation, new medicine, the workplace rebuilt around efficiency. Control moves into the details of daily life."},"libra":{"en":"Pluto in Libra puts power inside relationships: marriage rewritten, divorce and equality fought over, diplomacy as a battleground. Who gives way to whom becomes political."},"scorpio":{"en":"Pluto in Scorpio, its own sign, drags sex, death, debt and secrets into the light: crises of intimacy, hidden fortunes, taboos broken for good."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Pluto in Sagittarius remakes belief and borders: globalisation, religious extremes, information without limits. Truth becomes something people fight to own."},"capricorn":{"en":"Pluto in Capricorn strips institutions bare: banks fail, governments are exposed, corporations grow huge. Power shows its machinery, and trust in authority is rebuilt or lost."},"aquarius":{"en":"Pluto in Aquarius moves power into networks: algorithms, platforms, online crowds, collectives that can topple a government or quietly steer it. Whoever owns the code owns the future."},"pisces":{"en":"Pluto in Pisces remakes faith and feeling: mass longing, new faiths, crises of water and addiction, medicine for the mind. Power hides in what can't be seen."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Pluto spends about five months of every year appearing to move backwards, and its battles go indoors. The struggle with a boss, a parent or a habit becomes a private reckoning. It's a season for therapy, long walks with hard thoughts, and letting something finish dying properly."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Pluto stands still before turning back, and whatever has a hold on you grips harder for a few weeks: an obsession, a rivalry, a fear about money. Naming it plainly loosens it."},"direct":{"en":"Pluto turns forward after months of digging, and what you've faced in private starts to show in your choices. Make the move you've been circling: say the hard thing, claim what's yours, end what's finished."}}}},"aspects":{"sun-moon":{"conj":{"en":"New moon: what you want and what you feel finally agree, though the tank reads low. Start one small thing today — a savings pot, a running plan, a first page — and go to bed earlier than your pride suggests."},"soft":{"en":"Head and heart pull in the same direction today. Plans feel doable and people feel easy, so sort the family pickup schedule, cook something proper, or finish the task you've been postponing because of mood."},"hard":{"en":"What you need and what you're pushing for pull apart, so small things — a late reply, a sink full of dishes — feel like verdicts. Name the need before you argue the point, and finish one thing instead of starting three."}},"sun-mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Thought and intention fuse: you know what you mean and you say it. Good days for pitches, applications and the message you've redrafted for a week. The blind spot: you're so sure of your point that you stop hearing anyone else's."},"soft":{"en":"Words come out the way you meant them. Use it for the cover letter, the awkward email, or one honest explanation you owe someone."},"hard":{"en":"You talk faster than you listen. Before you send anything heated, read it out loud once and delete the last line."}},"sun-venus":{"conj":{"en":"Charm comes easily, and so does spending. People warm to you, compliments land, and a haircut or a new jacket feels like a fine idea. Use the goodwill to repair one cooled friendship; sleep on any purchase bigger than a week of groceries."},"soft":{"en":"Pleasant company and easy apologies. Invite someone to dinner, or say out loud the warm thing you usually only think."},"hard":{"en":"Wanting to be liked competes with wanting to be yourself. Notice where you're agreeing just to keep the evening smooth."}},"sun-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Drive and identity fuse: you want to win, and you want it now. Good for a hard workout, a wardrobe purge or asking for the raise. Watch the short fuse in traffic and in the group chat — not every delay is an insult."},"soft":{"en":"Effort turns into results without drama. Start the project you've been circling, carry the boxes, call the landlord. Courage is cheap this week, so spend it on the task you've been avoiding longest."},"hard":{"en":"Irritation rises fast and looks for a target: a slow colleague, a partner's tone, the printer. The heat is useful if you aim it — a sprint, a heavy bag, a scrubbed oven — before it lands on a person."}},"sun-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Confidence and luck travel together. Aim a little higher than usual and say yes to what's offered generously — but watch the urge to promise more than one week can hold."},"soft":{"en":"A clean line of good timing: effort is met halfway. Ask for the favour, send the pitch, book the trip, introduce two people who should know each other. Generosity, given or received, travels further than usual, so say exactly what you want."},"hard":{"en":"Big appetite, thin margins. Optimism outruns the facts, so keep the vision and check the numbers before you commit time or money you don't have. One fewer yes this week is a gift to next month."}},"sun-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Effort feels heavier and praise thinner. Someone in charge — a boss, a parent, your own inner accountant — wants proof. Use it: file the tax form, set the budget, take a deadline you can actually keep. Rest counts as discipline too."},"soft":{"en":"Steady work gets noticed. Senior people are more willing to listen, and slow tasks — the spreadsheet, the dentist booking, the lease renewal — go smoothly. Ask for the structure you need: a clear brief, a fixed date, a signature."},"hard":{"en":"A wall appears where you expected a door: a rejection, a delay, a 'not yet' from someone with authority. It stings because you want to be taken seriously. Treat it as a spec, not a verdict — ask what exactly would change the answer."}},"sun-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Restless with your own routine, you want to quit, move, cut your hair and rewrite the plan by Friday. Some of it is overdue. Make one bold change you can undo — a new route, a new class — before you torch anything permanent."},"soft":{"en":"Good days for a smart experiment. An unexpected idea, contact or app fixes an old problem, and people respond well to your less conventional side. Try the shortcut, pitch the odd idea, say yes to the last-minute invite."},"hard":{"en":"Plans break at short notice: a cancelled train, a changed brief, someone's sudden 'I need space'. The jolt shows where you've been holding on too tightly. Keep a spare hour in the diary, and make no big decisions while your pulse is up."}},"sun-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Edges blur. You feel kind, porous and slightly unfocused, and the to-do list loses to daydreams. Good for music, painting, a long bath or quietly helping someone. Bad for contracts and first impressions — check the facts, and lend nothing you can't lose."},"soft":{"en":"Imagination and compassion run easily. Write the first draft, plan the room makeover, call the friend who's having a hard month. Your read on people is reliable now — trust the quiet sense of who needs a softer word."},"hard":{"en":"Fog and fatigue: deadlines slip, messages get misread, and it's tempting to escape into a series, a bottle or someone else's crisis. Write things down, confirm times in writing, and ask the plain question even if it feels rude."}},"sun-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Intensity rises. You want control — of the project, the money, the story — and you notice who holds power over you. Use the force for one deep clean: cancel the subscription, have the hard talk, delete the thread you reread at night."},"soft":{"en":"Focus goes deep. You can get to the bottom of a budget, a medical question or a messy file, and people trust you with the real story. Ask the question underneath the question, and renegotiate while you hold the stronger hand."},"hard":{"en":"Power struggles surface: a boss who micromanages, a partner who won't budge, your own need for the last word. Something wants to end. Decide what you're willing to lose before you fight, and don't use secrets as leverage."}},"moon-mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Thoughts arrive with feelings attached, so you start talking about what's bothering you before you've decided to. Good this afternoon for a voice note to someone close or a page of journaling; bad for answering work email while annoyed."},"soft":{"en":"Easy conversations today. You find the right tone with a parent, a neighbour, a child's teacher. Use the afternoon for the calls you've been dodging, a shopping list that actually covers the week, or the small admin pile."},"hard":{"en":"Head and gut disagree today, and it shows in your texts: too long, too sharp, sent too fast. One comment can loop in your mind for hours. Wait twenty minutes before replying, and eat something before any serious conversation."}},"moon-venus":{"conj":{"en":"Soft mood, sweet tooth. You want comfort — a good meal, clean sheets, someone's hand — and you're kinder than usual. Lovely for a date or making up after a cold week; just notice if shopping is standing in for a hug."},"soft":{"en":"People are easy to be around today, and you're easy to forgive. Host a small dinner, send the thank-you note, buy flowers for the kitchen table. This afternoon small pleasures repair more than big gestures."},"hard":{"en":"You want affection but feel slightly unappreciated, so a forgotten text or a tired partner hits harder than it should. Comfort-spending and comfort-eating tempt. Ask for the hug directly instead of testing whether anyone notices."}},"moon-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Quick temper, quick hands. Feelings turn straight into action: you clean the flat in an hour, snap at the slow driver, text before thinking. Burn it off in the body first — a run, a hard class, carrying something heavy."},"soft":{"en":"Feeling and drive agree today: you want to do something, and you can. Tackle the chore that has a deadline, stand up for a friend, or have the honest talk while your nerve is still warm."},"hard":{"en":"Irritability runs high today: hunger, noise and other people's pace feel like provocations. Arguments flare at home over nothing — the thermostat, the dishwasher. Eat on time, move your body, and lower your voice one notch before you answer."}},"moon-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Big heart, big portions. Optimism and generosity flood in, and you want to feed people, plan holidays and say yes. Lovely for family time or a hopeful conversation; just leave room for tomorrow's appetite and budget."},"soft":{"en":"A lucky, open-handed mood this afternoon. People are kinder, small favours come easily, and good news travels. Ask a relative for help, invite someone new to lunch, or book the class you've been meaning to try."},"hard":{"en":"Too much of a good thing: another drink, another helping, one more promise to help. Feelings inflate, so a minor slight feels like betrayal and a small win feels like destiny. Halve the portion and postpone the big commitment until tomorrow."}},"moon-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"A heavy, sober mood: you feel older, lonelier or simply tired, and fun looks like work. It passes by tomorrow. Use it for dull, solid tasks — bills, a deep clean, a call to a parent — and go to bed early."},"soft":{"en":"Calm, practical feelings today. You keep promises without strain, and others rely on you. Good for prepping the week's meals, setting a budget with a partner, or an honest talk with an older relative about something real."},"hard":{"en":"You feel unsupported or judged, and a cool reply from a parent or boss lands like rejection. Old guilt surfaces. Make no lonely decisions today: do one responsible thing, then one kind thing for yourself — a warm meal, a bath."}},"moon-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Restless and twitchy today: you can't sit still, change plans on a whim, and crave something different. Sleep may be patchy. Take a new route, move the furniture, message someone unexpected — but don't quit anything before tomorrow."},"soft":{"en":"A light, curious mood this afternoon. You enjoy surprises and improvise well: a last-minute plan, a fix nobody else saw, a funny reply that breaks the tension. Say yes to the spontaneous invite."},"hard":{"en":"Nerves on edge: a sudden change of plans, a cancelled meeting, a partner who needs space just when you need closeness. You want freedom and comfort at once. Keep a buffer in the schedule and skip coffee after lunch."}},"moon-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"A dreamy, absorbent mood: you pick up everyone's feelings and lose track of your own. Music, swimming, a nap or a film heal well today. Keep away from wine-fuelled confessions and from lending money to a sad story."},"soft":{"en":"A tender, intuitive afternoon. You know what someone needs before they say it, and creative work flows. Sketch, cook without a recipe, call the friend who's grieving, or sit through a child's long story — patience comes naturally today."},"hard":{"en":"Foggy and thin-skinned today: you misplace keys, misread a tone, feel vaguely guilty about nothing specific. It's tempting to drift into scrolling or a second glass. Drink water, set one alarm for the important thing, and check before assuming."}},"moon-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Feelings run deep and private today. Jealousy, an old hurt or a sudden urge to purge the wardrobe can surface from nowhere. Let it work for you: clear one drawer, write the unsent letter, and keep the 3 a.m. thoughts out of the group chat."},"soft":{"en":"Emotional courage comes easier this afternoon. You can hear a hard truth without falling apart, and others open up to you. Good for therapy, a frank talk about money with family, or finally clearing out what you've outgrown."},"hard":{"en":"Intense and suspicious today: a delayed reply reads as a sign, and you want to control what you can't. Old family patterns flare. Notice the urge to check someone's phone or win the fight; do something physical first, then talk."}},"mercury-venus":{"conj":{"en":"Words get warmer. Compliments, flirting and diplomacy come easily, so it's a good stretch for love letters, negotiations, design choices and calming a tense email thread. Say the appreciative thing out loud; don't use charm to dodge the actual question."},"soft":{"en":"Tact is easy these days. Use it to ask for a discount, write the wedding toast, clear up a misunderstanding with a colleague, or finally say what you love about someone. Pleasant words open doors that blunt ones would slam."},"hard":{"en":"Saying the nice thing and saying the true thing feel like opposites. You soften feedback until it means nothing, or agree to a plan you dislike. Be kind and clear in the same sentence, and price your work honestly."}},"mercury-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Sharp mind, sharp tongue. You think fast, type fast and win debates — good for deadlines, cold emails and fixing what broke yesterday. The cost is tone: re-read before sending, and argue with the point, not the person."},"soft":{"en":"Decisive thinking. You cut through a messy meeting, make the call nobody wanted to make, and finish the paperwork in record time. Pitch, haggle or write the complaint letter now — you sound firm without sounding hostile."},"hard":{"en":"Arguments start in comment threads and end with slammed laptops. Everyone's sure, nobody's listening, and haste causes small accidents — a typo to the boss, a scraped bumper. Sleep on the angry email and slow down in traffic."}},"mercury-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Ideas get big and talk gets generous. Good for pitching, teaching, planning a trip or signing up for a course. The risk is overpromising: you tell three people 'easy, by Friday'. Write the plan down and cut it by a third."},"soft":{"en":"Good news and good conversations. A contract, an application or a hard question gets a fair hearing, and new material sticks. Send the proposal, ask the expert, book the consultation, read the long article you saved."},"hard":{"en":"Too many words, too few details. You skim the contract, exaggerate in the meeting, or argue about principles instead of the plan. Read the small print, double-check the flight date, and let someone else talk for a while."}},"mercury-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Serious, careful thinking. Words come slowly but carry weight, so it's a strong stretch for contracts, exams, budgets and the email that has to be exactly right. Worry gets louder too — write the list instead of rehearsing it at night."},"soft":{"en":"Clear, structured thinking. Paperwork that scared you turns out manageable, and senior people respect your precision. File the forms, finish the report, put agreements in writing. A short, plain message beats a long clever one."},"hard":{"en":"Communication gets stuck: delayed replies, a 'no' to your proposal, criticism that feels personal. You start doubting your own competence. Ask for specific feedback, fix one concrete thing, and don't read silence as a final answer."}},"mercury-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Lightning-fast ideas and abrupt news. You see a solution sideways, say something surprisingly blunt, or change your mind three times by lunch. Write every idea down — two will be good — and back up your files before the tech misbehaves."},"soft":{"en":"Inventive thinking. A new tool, a fresh angle or a stranger's comment solves something you've been stuck on for weeks. Brainstorm, rewrite your CV, try the app, message the person you met once at a conference."},"hard":{"en":"Nerves and glitches. Plans change by text, the Wi-Fi drops mid-call, and someone says something so blunt the meeting freezes. It may be you. Pause before reacting, keep a backup copy, and don't quit in a reply-all."}},"mercury-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Imagination floods language. Poems, lyrics, stories and gentle conversations flow, while spreadsheets and directions fall apart. Give these days to creative drafts and patient listening, and confirm every time, address and number twice."},"soft":{"en":"Words carry feeling. You find the right way to comfort, persuade or describe something hard to name. Write the eulogy, the song, the fundraising post, or the message that helps a friend feel less alone."},"hard":{"en":"Mixed signals and half-truths. A promise is vaguer than it sounded, a detail goes missing, and you hear what you hoped to hear. Get it in writing, don't sign or send money on a feeling, and say plainly what you mean."}},"mercury-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Thinking turns investigative. You want the real reason, the hidden clause, the whole story, and you can be persuasive to the point of pressure. Research, audit, interview — and notice if you're interrogating a partner instead of asking."},"soft":{"en":"Penetrating focus. You can read between the lines of a contract, a medical report or a hesitant friend's message. Good for research, negotiation, therapy, or the honest conversation that finally changes something."},"hard":{"en":"Words become weapons. Someone pushes, someone digs, a secret slips out, and an argument goes straight for the sore spot. Before you say the thing that can't be unsaid, ask what you actually want to change — then say only that."}},"venus-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Desire wakes up. Attraction, flirting and creative drive run together, and you notice who you actually want, not who's convenient. Make the move, plan the date, start the art project — and don't let jealousy do the talking."},"soft":{"en":"Chemistry comes easily. Romance, intimacy and teamwork flow, and making up after a fight takes one honest sentence. Ask someone out, plan a weekend for two, or pair up on a project with someone whose rhythm matches yours."},"hard":{"en":"Wanting and pleasing collide. Sexual tension, irritation with a partner, or a fight over who does more around the house can flare. You crave closeness and independence at once. Ask for what you want without turning it into a complaint."}},"venus-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"An abundant mood: generosity, good food, gifts and easy affection. Social plans multiply and people say yes. Throw the dinner, pitch the creative idea, buy something beautiful — once. The only real risk is overspending to keep a pleasant feeling going."},"soft":{"en":"Warmth with a payoff. Relationships, sales and creative work get a lift, and a kind word comes back with interest. Ask for the rate you deserve, reconnect with an old friend, say yes to the invitation that feels like a treat."},"hard":{"en":"Too much sweetness: overdoing food, shopping or flattery, and saying yes to everyone so nobody is disappointed. Pick one party, set a spending cap before you open the app, and notice who flatters you for a reason."}},"venus-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Love gets serious. Commitment, loyalty and boundaries matter more than romance, and you may feel lonely or tested. Good for defining a relationship, setting a budget, or ending something that only looked good. Choose quality over quantity, in people and in purchases."},"soft":{"en":"Steady affection. Long relationships deepen, older people give good advice, and money decisions come out sensible. Plan the shared savings, renew the lease, have the talk about next year, or buy the coat that will last ten winters."},"hard":{"en":"Love feels rationed: a partner seems cold, a date cancels, money's tight, and you wonder whether you're enough. Don't buy affection or beg for reassurance. Name one specific need, and pay off one small debt — it soothes better than shopping."}},"venus-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Sudden attraction and restless taste. You fall for someone unexpected, crave a new style, or want more freedom inside a relationship. Try something different — a new haircut, a different kind of date — before making permanent changes to a person or a bank balance."},"soft":{"en":"Pleasant surprises in love and money: a spontaneous date, an unusual gift, an unexpected compliment or side income. Say yes to the last-minute plan, try the gallery or class you've never been to, and flirt a little."},"hard":{"en":"Love meets freedom, and something jolts. A partner pulls away, a crush appears out of nowhere, or a purchase is pure impulse. Ask for space without punishing, return what you bought on a whim, and give the new feeling a week before you act."}},"venus-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Romance in soft focus. Music, art, longing and tenderness are heightened, and you see the best in people — sometimes more than is there. Make something beautiful, plan a dreamy date, but keep your bank card and your judgement in your own hands."},"soft":{"en":"Compassion and imagination are generous. Love feels kind rather than dramatic, and creative work has a quiet beauty. Donate, volunteer, write the love letter, repaint a room, or forgive someone who has genuinely been trying."},"hard":{"en":"Rose-tinted glasses. You idealise someone, ignore a red flag, or spend on a fantasy, and disappointment lives in the gap between the dream and the person. Ask the boring question, check the price twice, and watch who shows up reliably, not beautifully."}},"venus-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Attraction turns magnetic, even obsessive. Desire, jealousy and the wish to merge completely run high, and money questions inside love surface. Feel all of it, but don't check their phone. Good for intimacy, deep honesty and a creative project you give everything to."},"soft":{"en":"Love deepens through honesty. Trust grows, intimacy heals, and you can talk about money, sex or the past without blowing up. Have the real conversation, rework a shared budget, or commit fully to the person or project you chose."},"hard":{"en":"Love turns into a power struggle: jealousy, control over money, emotional blackmail, an ex resurfacing. You want all or nothing. Notice where you're testing someone instead of trusting them, and step back from anyone who needs you small."}},"mars-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Big push, big confidence. You want to go further, faster — a longer run, a bolder pitch, a bigger project. Good for launches, sport and starting the thing you've delayed. Pace yourself: overreaching shows up as a pulled muscle or an overbooked calendar."},"soft":{"en":"Effort pays off generously. Courage meets opportunity, so the sports goal, the business move or the hard conversation lands well. Apply for the bigger role, sign up for the race, propose the plan — momentum is on your side this week."},"hard":{"en":"Overconfidence and impatience. You take on too much, argue on principle, or spend to feel bigger, and risky moves look braver than they are. Finish what you started before adding more, and read the fine print on anything 'once in a lifetime'."}},"mars-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Effort meets resistance. You push and the door pushes back: paperwork, a slow boss, a body that wants rest. Frustration builds. Treat it like strength training — steady reps, not a sprint. One well-built task beats ten half-started ones."},"soft":{"en":"Stamina with a plan. Ambition stops fighting patience, so long, unglamorous work finally moves: the renovation, the thesis chapter, the debt payoff, the training block. Pick the hardest task, break it into steps, and do the first two before lunch."},"hard":{"en":"One foot on the gas, one on the brake. Delays, rules and other people's caution make you furious, and pushing harder only strains your back, your budget or the relationship. Stop forcing the locked door; find the person who has the key."}},"mars-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Sudden bursts of action and impatience. You quit the class, book the flight, take the risky shortcut, say exactly what you think. Good for breaking a stuck pattern; bad for fast driving and sharp knives, because haste causes small accidents now."},"soft":{"en":"Bold, inventive action. The unconventional approach works: a new workout, a fast pivot at work, a clever fix for a broken thing. Run the experiment, change the routine, say yes to the adventurous plan — your reflexes are quick now."},"hard":{"en":"Short fuses and sudden blow-ups. A minor annoyance turns into a slammed door or a resignation letter, and machines and plans fail at the worst moment. Work your body hard, add a buffer to travel, and make no irreversible moves while angry."}},"mars-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Drive goes soft and foggy. You want to act but can't find the target, and fatigue arrives early. Good for dance, swimming, yoga, art or volunteering. Skip the passive-aggressive standoff — say plainly what you want instead of sighing."},"soft":{"en":"Action guided by intuition and compassion. Effort feels lighter when it serves something beyond you. Join the park clean-up, help a neighbour move, practise an art, take a long swim. These days quiet persistence achieves more than force."},"hard":{"en":"Motivation leaks away. Confusion, low stamina or a hidden conflict makes it hard to fight for anything. Someone may be quietly working against you — or you're avoiding a fight. Rest without guilt, get the facts first, and choose one clear goal."}},"mars-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Raw force. Ambition, anger and desire run at full volume, and a week can do a month's work. Use it to renovate, clear out, train hard or rebuild a plan from scratch. Don't aim it at a person — the backlash matches the push."},"soft":{"en":"Concentrated, unstoppable effort. You can finish what others gave up on: a stubborn repair, a long negotiation, a fitness goal, a rescue job at work. Choose the one thing you want most and give it everything — the effort compounds."},"hard":{"en":"Power struggles and compulsion. Someone pushes, you push back harder, and it escalates — at work, at home, on the road. Rage can feel righteous. Walk away before it turns ugly, burn the anger off at the gym, and make no threats."}},"jupiter-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"A twenty-year reset of how societies grow and govern. Economies, institutions and careers reorganise around new rules — the last one, in late 2020, moved work onto screens. Personally: decide which long project deserves your next two decades, and start it modestly."},"soft":{"en":"A sensible season for growth. Expansion and caution cooperate: markets, institutions and businesses can grow without overheating, and long plans get funded. Make one ambitious move with a realistic budget — a mortgage, a degree, a business you can sustain."},"hard":{"en":"A collective tug-of-war between growth and limits: stimulus against austerity, hope against rules, boom against correction. You feel it as a clash between ambitions and obligations. Expand where the foundation already holds; cut back where it doesn't."}},"jupiter-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"A collective appetite for breakthrough: tech booms, sudden market leaps, mass enthusiasm for the new. Opportunities appear fast and disappear just as fast. In your own life, back the idea that excites you — but only with money you could survive losing."},"soft":{"en":"A wide opening for innovation. New tools spread quickly, unusual careers become viable, and the old way stops being the only way. Learn the new skill, launch the side project, apply abroad — luck favours people willing to experiment."},"hard":{"en":"Restless times: bubbles, sudden reversals, revolts against the way things are run. People want freedom faster than systems can adjust. Personally, don't quit a stable job on the strength of one good week — test the leap with a side step first."}},"jupiter-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Collective idealism and collective fog. Faith, charity, art and spiritual seeking surge, and so do hype, scams and bubbles built on a good story. Give generously, make something beautiful — and research any investment that sounds like a miracle."},"soft":{"en":"A gentle collective tide toward compassion and imagination. Humanitarian causes gain support, art and film find wide audiences, and faith turns less dogmatic. Volunteer, donate monthly, take the creative course — goodwill grows when it's practical."},"hard":{"en":"A period of inflated promises: miracle cures, get-rich schemes, leaders selling a dream. Collectively, hope outruns evidence. In your own life, keep the faith but verify the facts, and give to causes whose results you can actually see."}},"jupiter-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Concentrated collective power: huge fortunes made, institutions growing bigger and more controlling, ambition on a grand scale. Wealth and influence change hands. Personally, aim for long-term leverage — skills, ownership, savings — rather than a quick win."},"soft":{"en":"Favourable years for deep regeneration. Money flows into rebuilding, research breakthroughs scale up, and people find leverage to shift entrenched situations. Use it to pay down debt, invest for the long term, or rebuild a career on firmer ground."},"hard":{"en":"Collective struggles over wealth and control: monopolies challenged, scandals exposed, ambition that overreaches. Personally, watch for deals that ask you to hand over too much control, and don't stake what you can't afford to lose on a shot at more."}},"saturn-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Old order and new invention collide and fuse — the late-1980s conjunction coincided with the fall of the Berlin Wall and the birth of the web. Structures crack and rebuild. Personally: decide which rules still protect you and which you've outgrown."},"soft":{"en":"Practical innovation. Reform happens without revolution: new technology gets sensible rules, old institutions modernise, stable professions absorb new tools. Good years to retrain, update a business model, or build structure around a freer way of working."},"hard":{"en":"Collective tension between control and freedom: restrictions against liberties, old industries against disruption, rules that feel broken but won't budge. Personally, you're stuck between security and change. Make the change in small, structured steps, not one dramatic exit."}},"saturn-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Dreams meet the reality check: the 1989 conjunction saw ideologies collapse, and the 2026 one asks what our ideals will actually cost to build. Collectively, faith gets audited. Personally, give your vaguest dream a budget, a date and a first boring step."},"soft":{"en":"Ideals take practical form. Charities become institutions, art finds funding, compassion turns into policy. Personally, these are good years to turn a calling into a job — the studio, the clinic, the course you've dreamed of teaching."},"hard":{"en":"Years of disillusionment: institutions lose credibility, propaganda and fear blur the facts, systems quietly erode. You may feel your hopes dissolving under pressure. Keep one dream, give it a structure, and let the rest go without bitterness."}},"saturn-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"A heavy collective reckoning, roughly every 35 years: systems that stopped working are exposed, and power structures harden or collapse. Personally, it is a time to rebuild one area of life from the foundation up, patiently and with no shortcuts."},"soft":{"en":"Slow, serious rebuilding. Governments and companies can reform what's rotten, long-term infrastructure gets built, and discipline pays off deeply. Personally, commit to the change that takes years: clearing the mortgage, mastering the craft, rebuilding your health."},"hard":{"en":"Collective pressure between authority and upheaval: rules tighten, budgets shrink, people argue about who holds power. Fear makes systems rigid. Personally, notice where fear makes you rigid, and choose the hard change before it is chosen for you."}},"uranus-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"A once-in-a-lifetime fusion of invention and imagination: the early-1990s conjunction gave the world the web, raves and a new language for dreams. Generations born under it think in networks. Personally, it's the deep reason you want technology to mean something."},"soft":{"en":"A long, quiet current in which technology and imagination cooperate: digital art, online communities, tools that make inspiration easier to share. Use those tools to make something beautiful or useful — the gap between dreaming and building is narrower than it was."},"hard":{"en":"Collective confusion between invention and illusion: tech utopias that turn into nightmares, disinformation at the speed of light, revolutions that dissolve into mist. Be sceptical of the shiny promise, and keep one offline habit that brings you back to earth."}},"uranus-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"The generational detonation of the 1960s: civil rights, the sexual revolution, youth in revolt against the old order. Those born under it carry a radical streak. Personally, it's the stubborn part of you that refuses to live by rules that crush people."},"soft":{"en":"A long window in which radical change can happen without wreckage: reforms take root, technology redistributes power, old taboos fade. Use it to make one deep change stick — a new city, a new profession, a new relationship with your body."},"hard":{"en":"Years of upheaval: protest movements, financial shocks, institutions shaken by what they hid. Change arrives whether or not you plan for it. Choose the change you can steer — a job, a city, a habit — before a bigger one is chosen for you."}},"neptune-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"The seed of a 500-year cycle, last planted around 1892, when electricity, cinema, psychoanalysis and mass ideology were born together. A collective dream reshaped the world. Personally, it's ancestral weather: the beliefs your great-grandparents built their lives on."},"soft":{"en":"A slow undercurrent running since the 1940s: beliefs change the way coastlines do, too slowly to see in a year. Your grandparents' rules about work, faith and family soften without anyone voting on it. Notice one inherited fear and ask whether it's still yours."},"hard":{"en":"A rare collective strain between dreams and power, historically felt when empires and faiths cracked at the same time. Ideals become weapons and grief goes underground. Personally, separate what you truly believe from what you were simply taught to fear."}}},"transits":{"sun>sun":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is back on your natal Sun: your solar return, the birthday reset. Birthdays sting because you quietly compare yourself with the person you planned to be by now. Skip the audit. Write one sentence about what this next year is for, and let someone buy you cake."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is in easy step with your natal Sun: for a day or two you feel like yourself, with more stamina and less second-guessing, because nothing is asking you to be someone else. Spend it on something with your name on it: the pitch, the application, the haircut."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is squaring off with your natal Sun: for a day or two, the plan you made around your birthday meets real life. You feel tired or oddly unseen, mostly because you're carrying tasks that aren't yours. Hand one back, politely, before it becomes a grudge."}},"sun>moon":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Moon: feelings you usually manage alone show on your face, and your needs get harder to hide. For a day or two, name one out loud — an early night, a hand with dinner — before it sours into a mood."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is in easy contact with your natal Moon: what you want and what you need agree for once, so your shoulders drop and home feels good to come back to. Use the next day or two to settle the family plan or home decision you've been circling."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is pressing on your natal Moon: the goal and the need pull apart, and the body takes the hit — a tight jaw, a bad night, sugar at four. You keep going as if rest were optional. For a day or two, choose the need once, on purpose."}},"sun>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Mercury: your head is clear, your sentences come out finished, and people listen. For a day or two, send the pitch or write the difficult email. The catch is hearing yourself so well you stop hearing others — ask one real question back."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is in friendly contact with your natal Mercury: you can explain what you want without rehearsing it twelve times, because you're not fighting your own doubts. For a day or two, say out loud the thing you've been drafting in your head in the shower."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is at odds with your natal Mercury: pride gets into your sentences. A neutral comment reads as criticism, and you want to win the thread rather than end it, because being right feels like being seen. For a day or two, reread before you send."}},"sun>venus":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Venus: you look good to yourself, and other people notice. Wanting nice things stops feeling like a flaw for a day or two. Wear the good shirt, book the table, and quote your real rate instead of the apologetic one."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is flattering your natal Venus: people warm to you because you're relaxed rather than trying, and money talk goes smoother than expected. For a day or two, plan the date, buy the small good thing, or ask for the better price."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is chafing against your natal Venus: you want proof you're worth something, and the wanting leaks out — a basket of things you don't need, a sulk when nobody mentions the haircut. For a day or two, say what you'd like to hear instead of testing people."}},"sun>mars":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Mars: your engine turns over and you want to start, compete, finish. Slow people and slow wifi become personal insults, because ambition and temper share a fuse. For a day or two, aim it at one hard task, then at the gym."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is giving your natal Mars a tailwind: effort pays back quickly and your body has more in it than usual. Confidence here comes from moving, not from thinking about moving. For a day or two, start the thing you've been postponing — the run, the course, the wardrobe clear-out."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is clashing with your natal Mars: your will meets resistance and takes it personally. A colleague's tone, a long queue, a partner's one-word text can set you off. For a day or two, burn it off physically — stairs, a run, a heavy bag — before you reply to anyone."}},"moon>sun":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Sun: for a few hours today, what you feel and who you are point the same way. You're easier to read and easier to like. Do the visible thing now — the call, the post, the ask — while your face and your words agree."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is lending your natal Sun a few good hours: your mood backs your plans, so the body has fuel and the to-do list looks doable. Nothing in you is arguing. Use the window for one task that needs heart and nerve: a first draft, a tricky call."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is pulling against your natal Sun: for a few hours, your mood and your plans want different things, and you feel off without knowing why — hungry, touchy, slightly exposed. Eat something real, and don't judge your whole life by one bad mood."}},"moon>moon":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is back on your natal Moon: your lunar return, the monthly reset of your emotional clock. For a few hours you're thin-skinned, and your oldest needs surface — your food, your bed, your people. Meet them plainly, then notice which one you've been skipping all month."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is in easy step with your natal Moon: for a few hours your body and mood cooperate, and you know what you need without having to argue for it. Cook something familiar, tidy one corner, call someone who knew you at fifteen."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is squaring off with your natal Moon: for a few hours your needs and your day don't match — you crave quiet in a loud office, or company when everyone's busy. Your stomach notices first. Eat, drink water, and don't text anyone from this mood."}},"moon>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Mercury: for a few hours, feelings find words fast. You talk more, replay old conversations, start the long voice note. Good for a heart-to-heart, risky for a work email, because your mood is doing the typing. Draft now, send after dinner."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is in friendly contact with your natal Mercury: for a few hours you can say how you feel without the usual tangle, because head and gut are using the same language. Write it down, or tell someone what you need without blaming them."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is needling your natal Mercury: for a few hours your mood edits what you hear. A short reply reads as cold, a question as an accusation, because the feeling arrives first and the reasons get invented after. Ask what they meant before you answer what you heard."}},"moon>venus":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Venus: for a few hours you want softness — good bread, clean sheets, a hand on your back. Pleasure calms you quickly now because mood and taste agree. Say yes to the small nice thing, and tell someone you'd like company tonight."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is warming your natal Venus: for a few hours you like yourself, so other people find you easy to like. Small talk with the barista turns into a laugh. Use the mood to make up with someone after a cold few days."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is pressing on your natal Venus: for a few hours you want comfort and grab the nearest version — a full basket, a second dessert, an ex's profile. The need is real; the target is off. Name the feeling first, then see if you still want the thing."}},"moon>mars":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Mars: for a few hours feelings go straight to your hands. Irritation flares hot, so does desire, because there's no gap between feeling and doing. Spend it on a hard workout or the jammed drawer, not on the group chat."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is backing your natal Mars: for a few hours you want to act and your body agrees, so courage costs less. Use the window for the chore you've been dodging, a hard set at the gym, or a firm, friendly no."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is provoking your natal Mars: for a few hours small things — a slow till, a sigh from your partner — land as attacks. Usually it's tiredness or hurt wearing armour. Get it out of your body before you answer: a brisk walk, cold water, ten push-ups."}},"mercury>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Sun: for a day or two, your thoughts circle you — your plans, your reputation, what you should have said. Calls and forms with your name on them pile up. Update the CV or bio, and talk to yourself like a decent colleague would."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in friendly contact with your natal Sun: for a day or two you can explain what you want in one go, because your words and your aims agree. Pitch yourself, sign up for the course, answer the recruiter. People get your point first time."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is at odds with your natal Sun: for a day or two, feedback sounds personal and you over-explain yourself, because your pride is listening for criticism. Expect crossed wires about who said what. Check the thread before reacting, and don't defend what nobody attacked."}},"mercury>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Moon: for a day or two your feelings want words. You go over what your mother said, text home more than usual. At night the talking can turn into looping. Say it once to one person who listens, then put the phone down."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in friendly step with your natal Moon: for a day or two, talking things through actually calms you, because once it's named, a feeling shrinks. Make the family call, have the sensible chat about chores, write down what you need."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is snagging on your natal Moon: for a day or two, an offhand comment lands in a soft spot, and you answer sharper than you feel. Arguing facts won't fix a mood, because the hurt isn't about the facts. Say “I need a minute” and take it."}},"mercury>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is back on your natal Mercury, where it stood when you were born: for a day or two you think in your own voice, not the one you borrow for meetings. Shelved ideas resurface. Open the old notes file; one of them is ready."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in friendly contact with your natal Mercury: for a day or two your mind works the way it likes to, so fiddly things — the tax form, the new app, the long article — stop feeling like effort. Learn one thing properly, then explain it to someone."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is squaring off with your natal Mercury: for a day or two the facts arrive in a shape your mind doesn't like, so you skim, assume, misread. Wrong time, wrong attachment, wrong person in cc. Read every message twice, and check dates against the calendar."}},"mercury>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Venus: for a day or two your words come out warm and a little flirty, because you're thinking about what you like. Send the compliment, write the note, negotiate the price — charm helps with money, too."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in a sweet angle to your natal Venus: for a day or two, kind words come easily and land well, so it's a good moment to repair things. Apologise for the sharp text, plan a date, or settle the shared budget without a fight."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is tangling with your natal Venus: for a day or two you analyse affection instead of feeling it — rereading their text, counting the kisses, wondering what “ok” meant. Money talk can sour the same way. Call instead of typing; tone carries what text drops."}},"mercury>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Mars: for a day or two your words get an edge and your patience gets short. You think fast and say it faster. Use it to write the complaint, chase the late invoice, argue the case — and wait ten minutes before sending anything personal."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is backing your natal Mars: for a day or two you decide quickly and act on it the same afternoon, because thinking and doing aren't arguing. Clear the admin backlog, give one straight instruction, book the thing you keep researching."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is clashing with your natal Mars: for a day or two, words turn into fights fast — a comment thread, a sibling, a driver who cuts in. Your mind wants a target for the heat. Write the furious reply, delete it, and go for a run."}},"venus>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is crossing your natal Sun: for a day or two you're easier to like and you can tell — softer face in the mirror, a stranger holding the door, a friend picking up the bill. You don't have to earn it. Accept the invitation and the compliment without arguing."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is in sweet contact with your natal Sun: for a day or two, goodwill comes cheap. You get further with warmth than with pushing, so book the photos, the haircut, the meeting where you need someone on your side. Wear the colour you usually save."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is tugging at your natal Sun: for a day or two you want to be liked so much you'll bend for it — agreeing to plans you don't want, paying for the round, laughing at unfunny jokes. Do one thing today purely because you enjoy it, audience or not."}},"venus>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is touching your natal Moon: for a day or two, comfort comes easily. A small kindness lands exactly where you needed it, and home, food or a familiar person soothes more than usual. Receive it without rushing to pay it back."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is at a gentle angle to your natal Moon: for a day or two the people at home feel easy to love, because pleasure and safety want the same thing. Cook for someone, put flowers on the kitchen table, mend a small rift with family."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is pressing on your natal Moon: for a day or two, what you want and what makes you feel safe disagree. A purchase, a date or a sweet thing may be standing in for reassurance you haven't asked for directly. Ask for the reassurance first, out loud."}},"venus>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is crossing your natal Mercury: for a day or two you choose words for how they'll feel, not just what they mean. Good for the birthday card, the toast, the message that mends a quarrel. Write the thing you'd only say after two glasses of wine."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is smoothing the way for your natal Mercury: for a day or two you can say difficult things kindly and people hear the kindness first. Use it for the awkward email, the favour you need to ask, or the price you want to negotiate down."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is at odds with your natal Mercury: for a day or two you say what pleases instead of what's true — yes to the plan, praise for the bad idea, a purchase because the salesperson was lovely. Before agreeing, ask yourself what you actually think."}},"venus>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is back on your natal Venus: your Venus return, the roughly yearly reset of what you love and what you think you're worth. Your taste is unusually clear for a day or two. Notice what bores you now, and set this year's price — in love and at work."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is in easy contact with your natal Venus: for a day or two, you like what you already have — the flat, the friend, the coat you nearly returned. Contentment shows, and it's attractive, because you've stopped comparing. Spend a little on pleasure, not on proving anything."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is squaring off with your natal Venus: for a day or two your appetite and your values disagree — the jacket you can't afford, the ex who only texts at midnight. Ask whether you want the thing itself, or the feeling of being worth it."}},"venus>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is crossing your natal Mars: for a day or two desire turns warm and direct, and you chase what you want with charm instead of force. Attraction tends to run both ways. Make the first move, suggest the date, or pitch the deal with a smile."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is in easy step with your natal Mars: for a day or two your drive softens without losing force, so effort feels like play. Dance class, a match with friends, sex without overthinking, a negotiation you win nicely. Go after the fun thing first."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is pulling against your natal Mars: for a day or two desire and irritation get tangled — you want them and they're annoying you, or you spend fast to scratch an itch. Underneath is wanting more than you're getting. Say that, instead of picking a fight about the dishes."}},"mars>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Sun: for several days you have more fuel, more nerve and much less patience. Being blocked feels like being erased, so you push. Give it a target: a hard training week, a project with a deadline, the conversation where you stand your ground."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is fuelling your natal Sun: for several days you have stamina and the nerve to use it, without the usual fight with yourself. Ask for the raise, start the training plan, take the lead in the meeting. Momentum built this week tends to stick."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is squaring off with your natal Sun: for several days you keep hitting walls — a boss, a bank, a partner with a different plan — and you take each one as a challenge to who you are. Choose one fight worth having, and sleep more than you want to."}},"mars>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Moon: for several days your feelings run hot and close to the skin — quick tears, quick temper, a fierce urge to protect your people. Tiredness turns into anger fast. Move your body daily, eat on time, and keep arguments out of the kitchen."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is in easy step with your natal Moon: for several days you can stand up for what you need without it becoming a scene, because the feeling and the action finally agree. Fix the broken shelf, set the house rule, say no to the extra shift."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is pressing on your natal Moon: for several days home feels crowded, family knows exactly which button to press, and sleep turns light. The anger is mostly depletion in disguise. Eat properly, go to bed early, and take the long way round the relative who always starts it."}},"mars>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Mercury: for several days your mind is quick and your tongue quicker. You cut through waffle, win arguments, edit ruthlessly — and lose patience with anyone slower. Use it on the report or the negotiation; sleep on any message written in anger."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is sharpening your natal Mercury: for several days you can focus hard and speak plainly, and people take it as confidence, not aggression. Cram for the exam, close the deal, have the direct conversation you've been softening for weeks."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is clashing with your natal Mercury: for several days your mind stays braced for an argument, so you interrupt, assume the worst, type faster than you think. Traffic and comment sections are a trap. Say less, say it later, and never in capitals."}},"mars>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Venus: for several days attraction gets physical and impatient. You want the person, the jacket, the weekend away, and you want it now, because desire stops asking permission. Make the move if it's mutual; sleep on anything that costs more than a week's pay."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is warming your natal Venus: for several days wanting and going after it feel natural, not greedy. Ask them out, finish the creative project, chase the money you're owed — charm and push are working as a team."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is goading your natal Venus: for several days love and money turn into a contest — who pays, who texts first, who wanted it more. Jealousy sits closer to the surface. Spending to win, or to sulk, costs double now. Say the want out loud instead."}},"mars>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is back on your natal Mars: your Mars return, the reset of your drive that comes round every two years or so. For several days you're restless and short with anything that wastes your time. Pick what you'll fight for until the next one, and start this week."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is in easy contact with your natal Mars: for several days your body and your will pull the same way, so effort turns into results instead of frustration. Add weight at the gym, tackle the stubborn job, ask directly for what you want."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is grinding against your natal Mars: for several days your drive hits friction — plans stall, people push back, and you push harder. Most bruises now, physical or social, come from rushing. Go ten per cent slower than you want to, especially on the road and at the gym."}},"jupiter>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is crossing your natal Sun: for a few weeks you take up more room, and it suits you. A boss notices, a mentor opens a door, an old plan looks doable, because you've stopped apologising for wanting it. Ask for the bigger role, then check your calendar before promising anything."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is backing your natal Sun: these weeks reward showing up as yourself. A pitch, an interview or a talk with someone senior goes better than expected, because you're not straining to impress. Openings like this pass quietly if you wait to feel ready. Say yes to one thing that makes you more visible."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Sun: for a few weeks ambition outgrows your calendar. You want the promotion, the grand gesture, partly to prove a father, an old boss or a doubter wrong. Keep the dream, halve the first step, and check it still excites you without an audience."}},"jupiter>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is sitting on your natal Moon: for a few weeks home feels bigger and kinder. Family gets in touch, guests stay late, appetite and patience grow. You feel safe enough to want more, which is the gift. Feed people, take the long bath, and notice if comfort turns into a nightly second helping."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is easing your natal Moon: these weeks loosen the background worry you carry everywhere. A call with your mother goes well, a room or a flat comes up, sleep arrives sooner. You don't have to earn this rest. When someone offers to look after you, say yes before listing reasons you don't need it."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Moon: for a few weeks feelings run large, and so do the remedies. Extra takeaway, extra plans, yes to every family request, because a full table feels like being loved. Under it sits a plainer wish to be held. Ask for that directly, and keep one evening empty."}},"jupiter>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is crossing your natal Mercury: for a few weeks your head fills with ideas, open tabs and new courses. You talk well, write fast, and people listen. The catch is breadth: ten plans started, none finished. Pick the idea you'd still explain to a friend next month and write two pages of it."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is backing your natal Mercury: for a few weeks your words land. An application, a negotiation, a class you've eyed for months or an email to someone you've never dared approach goes smoother, because you sound like you believe it. Send the message you keep drafting in your head on the commute."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Mercury: you promise more than you can read, write or answer. The yes comes out before the thought is finished, and details get waved through because the big picture feels right. It's enthusiasm, not carelessness. Before you sign or announce anything these weeks, read the small print aloud."}},"jupiter>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is touching your natal Venus: a few generous weeks for love, money and pleasure. A date goes well, a payment clears, a friend insists on paying. You feel worth spending on, and people respond to that. Enjoy it, and decide in advance the one thing you won't buy just because you feel lucky."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is easing your natal Venus: for a few weeks warmth and good taste come easily. Making up after a quarrel, asking for a fair rate, repainting a corner of the flat — all meet less resistance than usual. Use the goodwill to ask for something you normally talk yourself out of wanting."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Venus: appetite outruns the budget. The dinner, the dress, the lavish gift, the romance that sounds better than it feels — you overdo it because more looks like proof you're valued. Keep the pleasure, drop the proving. For these weeks, wait two days before any big purchase or big declaration."}},"jupiter>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is crossing your natal Mars: for a few weeks you run on extra fuel. You train harder, start the project, say the bold thing in the meeting, and mostly it works. Courage is cheap, which makes overreach cheap too. Aim the push at one goal with a finish line, not at every irritation."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is backing your natal Mars: effort pays these weeks. A new sport, a renovation, a pitch, a move you've been circling — you have the push and the luck at once. Don't spend it on arguments you've already won. Book the first session or set the date while starting still feels easy."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Mars: you want to win, and now. You sign up for too much, lift too heavy, turn a disagreement into a crusade, because holding back feels like losing. The drive is good; the scale is off. These weeks, choose one fight worth having and let the rest go."}},"saturn>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Sun: a sober chapter of several months. You feel older, more tired, more watched, and shortcuts stop working. The real question is what you're for, and whose approval, a father's or a boss's, you're still chasing. Choose one serious commitment and carry it slowly. What you build now holds."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Sun: these months turn steady work into visible results. Someone senior trusts you with more, a long project takes shape, your name starts to mean reliable. It feels less like luck than like being taken seriously. Put a date and a number on the goal you keep describing vaguely."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Sun: these months push back. A boss says not yet, a plan stalls, your body wants more sleep than you'd like. The pressure shows where your sense of self rests on someone else's approval. Drop one obligation you keep only for appearances and guard the hours it frees."}},"saturn>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Moon: for months feelings go quiet and heavy. The flat needs repairs, a parent needs care, and you end up the adult in every room. You cope by needing nothing; this chapter questions that. Build one comfort routine, a Sunday soup or a phone-free evening, and keep it."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Moon: these months are good for making home solid. Signing a lease, fixing the boiler, settling into a regular bedtime, talking to your mother on calmer terms. You feel steadier because you've stopped improvising your basic needs. Put one comforting habit in the calendar, as fixed as a work meeting."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Moon: these months can feel lonely even in company. Family duty, a cold flat, a body spent by evening, and an old reflex of swallowing need so nobody worries. The lesson: self-reliance has a ceiling. Tell one person what you need, in a full sentence, without apologising."}},"saturn>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is crossing your natal Mercury: for some months your mind turns serious. You read slower, check twice, and hear where your words were careless. Exams, contracts or one hard piece of writing ask for discipline, while the inner critic gets loud. Set a daily hour for your hardest thinking and keep it."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Mercury: these months suit study and slow, solid work. A diploma, a manuscript, a careful contract or a difficult conversation goes well because you've prepared instead of rushing. Your opinion carries weight now. Commit to one structured course or project, with deadlines you set yourself and actually keep."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Mercury: for months thinking feels like wading. Paperwork stalls, a reply never comes, you rewrite one email five times while a voice says you're not clever enough. That voice usually dates from school. Write it down rather than obey it, then finish one small piece by noon."}},"saturn>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Venus: for months love and money get honest. A relationship settles into commitment or shows its cracks; spending meets the budget. Feeling less attractive is mostly a sign you're done performing for approval. Keep bonds that survive plain talk, and price your work at what it costs you."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Venus: these months favour love that lasts and money that adds up. Moving in, a savings plan, a friendship tested and found steady. Romance looks quieter and more grown-up, and it's more trustworthy for that. Have the practical talk — rent, plans, next year — you've been calling unromantic."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Venus: these months bring scarcity in love or money. Someone goes distant, a payment is late, pleasure feels earned rather than given. The root is an old belief that affection must be deserved. Notice where you pay for closeness with extra effort, and stop paying in one place."}},"saturn>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Mars: for some months drive meets a wall. You push, results come slowly, and frustration leaks out as snapping or quiet rage. This chapter trains effort into stamina. Swap sprints for a schedule: the same workout, the same writing hour, done whether you feel like it or not."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Mars: these months reward disciplined effort. Training for a race, renovating a room, finishing a long project — your stamina holds, and setbacks don't knock you off course. Strength built now stays. Pick a goal that needs months rather than weeks and write down the weekly minimum you'll do."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Mars: these months make anger heavy. Rules, a boss, paperwork or your own body block the move you want, and pushing harder backfires — a strained back, a cold war at home. This asks for strategy, not force. Take one blocked thing and work it in small, unglamorous steps."}},"uranus>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Sun: this year, often longer, the life you built feels a size too small. A new job, a move, a break with a boss or a parent's expectations — something resets who you think you are. The restlessness is honest. Change things on purpose before boredom changes them for you."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Sun: this period gives you room to reinvent without wreckage. A side project becomes a direction, an unusual offer arrives, and people accept the version of you that's less polished and more yours. Say yes to one experiment that the cautious part of you calls a bit odd."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Sun: this period shakes the scaffolding. A boss, a parent or a role you've outgrown feels like a cage, and you want to quit everything at once. The hunger for freedom is real. Change one thing — the job or the flat, not both — before torching the lot."}},"uranus>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Moon: this year home and mood turn unpredictable. You may move, change who you live with, or wake at 4 a.m. wanting a different life. Your nerves are on alert because old forms of safety no longer fit. Build stability from rhythms — sleep, meals, a walk — rather than walls."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Moon: this period opens a freer way of living. A new flat, a fairer split of the chores, a family habit finally broken without a scene. Feelings move faster and recover faster. Try the change to your home life you keep calling impractical, starting with one room or one evening."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Moon: this period unsettles the base. Sudden family news, a move you didn't plan, patchy sleep. Part of you wants to run, part wants to cling to routine; both are fear. Keep two anchors — bedtime and one daily meal at a table — and let the rest change."}},"uranus>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Mercury: this year your thinking speeds up and turns sideways. New subjects, insights in the shower, a new way of talking. Opinions you held for years drop overnight. Your mind is rewiring, so it runs hot. Keep a notebook for the flashes and test each before announcing it."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Mercury: this period is ideal for learning something new and slightly odd. Code, a language, a field nobody expected from you. Ideas arrive whole, and people who think differently find you. Sign up for the course or the online group that excites you a little more than it makes sense."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Mercury: this period makes your mind jumpy. Plans change last minute, messages cross, you blurt the blunt thing, then wonder why. Your nerves are overloaded because too much is changing at once. Cut one input — a feed, a group chat, a news app — and take that attention back."}},"uranus>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Venus: this year your taste in love, money and beauty shifts. Sudden attractions, a relationship that needs more air, an unexpected income or expense. What used to charm you now bores you. Before you blow up a relationship, try rewriting its rules; freedom inside one is a real option."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Venus: this period lets fresh air into love and money. An unlikely friendship, a new way of earning, a partner who surprises you nicely. You like yourself more once you drop the expected script. Say yes to the date, the look or the side income that feels unlike you."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Venus: this period makes closeness feel tight. You want space, or someone you love does, and money comes and goes erratically. Part of this is real growth, part is fear of being trapped. Tell the person concerned what kind of freedom you need, before you act it out instead."}},"uranus>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Mars: this year brings bursts of courage and a shorter fuse. You quit, start, move, say the unsayable, and your body wants a new sport. The risk is abrupt exits and accidents. Give the restlessness a daily physical outlet, and drive like someone you love is in the car."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Mars: this period gives your will a quick, inventive edge. You act on ideas faster, take a risk that pays off, find a new way to train or work. Courage feels natural, not forced. Make the bold move you've been rehearsing: start the business, change the routine, switch disciplines."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Mars: this period brings friction with rules and anyone who gives orders. You snap at limits, take risks for the thrill, break things — a deal, a habit, sometimes a glass. What you're really fighting for is autonomy. Decide which freedom actually matters and fight for that one, openly."}},"neptune>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Sun: this year your sense of self goes soft. Ambition fades, you tire easily, and art, faith or quiet pull at you. A father figure may seem distant or idealised. This isn't losing yourself; it's loosening a rigid self-image. Work gently, and keep a morning walk non-negotiable."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Sun: this period lends your life a quiet sense of meaning. Creative work, music, volunteering or prayer feel natural, and people see your gentler side. Inspiration comes easily; discipline doesn't. Give the dream a time slot — an hour, twice a week — for the thing you'd do if nobody paid you."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Sun: this period fogs your sense of direction. Goals feel pointless, praise hollow, and you give too much to someone who needs rescuing. The fog comes from trying to be what others imagine. Before big decisions, get the facts in writing and let one honest friend read them."}},"neptune>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Moon: this year feelings become porous. You absorb a room's mood, cry at adverts, sleep longer and dream vividly. Home or family may feel like something you're mourning or idealising. Sensitivity is the gift; boundaries are the work. Protect sleep, go easy on wine, and notice whose sadness you carry."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Moon: this period makes home softer. Music in the kitchen, a gentler bond with your mother, an empathy people feel before you say a word. Your family instincts are sound. Make one corner of the flat just for rest — a chair, a lamp, no phone — and actually use it."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Moon: this period blurs where you end and others begin. You rescue, absorb, give in, then feel drained and vaguely betrayed. A relative may lean on you more than is fair, because you've taught everyone you're always available. Say “not tonight” once, kindly, and watch the house stay standing."}},"neptune>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Mercury: this year your mind thinks in images more than lists. Poetry, music and intuition sharpen; dates, keys and small print slip. Some conversations leave you unsure what was agreed. Confirm plans by message and keep notes, then let the dreamier mind write, draw or compose without a deadline."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Mercury: this period gives your words a softer reach. You write more beautifully, listen better, and hear what people mean rather than just what they say. Good for fiction, translation, songwriting, any work that depends on listening. Keep a notebook by the bed and give half-formed ideas somewhere to land."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Mercury: this period invites misunderstandings. You hear what you hope to hear, lose a detail, trust a vague promise, partly because the plain version stings. Before you sign, transfer money or believe a good story, ask the blunt question you'd rather skip, and wait for a straight answer."}},"neptune>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Venus: this year love feels like a film. You fall for potential, long for the unavailable, or see beauty in strangers and rainy streets. Compassion grows; so does the risk of buying a fantasy. Keep the romance, check the facts: who shows up, who pays, who calls back."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Venus: this period softens love and refines your taste. Tenderness comes easily, and art, music and beautiful rooms move you more. A relationship can feel close to sacred. Spend time on beauty for its own sake: a museum afternoon, a song learned by heart, a letter written by hand."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Venus: this period invites illusions about love or money. You idealise someone who doesn't show up, or spend on something that promises a happier you. Under it is a longing to be rescued. Treat your heart like your bank card: look closely before handing it over."}},"neptune>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Mars: this year drive goes underground. You're less sure what you want, tire faster, dodge conflict. Anger leaks sideways as sulking, sarcasm or procrastination. Desire drifts toward something still unnamed. Choose movement that feels like water — swimming, yoga, long walks — and effort for something bigger than winning comes easier."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Mars: this period lets your effort serve something you believe in. Volunteering, dance, art, a cause — you act from feeling rather than ego, and it carries further than force. Competition matters less. Put your strength behind one cause or creative project and give it a regular, protected hour."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Mars: this period blurs your willpower. You start things and drift, avoid a fight you need to have, feel worn out for no reason. Part is your body asking for rest, part is fear of your own anger. Find one honest no you've swallowed and say it aloud."}},"pluto>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Sun: a long chapter, often several years, of being rebuilt from the inside. Power struggles with a boss, a father or an institution force you to decide who you are without their approval. Old ambitions die off; let them. Ask what you'd do if nobody watched, and do that."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Sun: this period deepens your authority. You speak with more weight, take on serious responsibility, and calmly end what has run its course. People trust your intensity. Spend it on one long project — the career shift, the therapy, the business — and stay with it past the boring middle."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Sun: this period brings power struggles that feel personal. A boss, a parent or a partner pushes, and you push back harder or shrink. Underneath is a fear of being erased. The work: keep your shape without needing to win. Name your non-negotiables and stop arguing the rest."}},"pluto>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Moon: over this long stretch the oldest feelings surface — about your mother, home, food, safety. A move or a family secret can stir grief and rage you didn't know you carried. Find someone trained to hear it. What you face this year loses its quiet hold on you."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Moon: this period helps untangle family patterns at the root. You understand your mother better, renovate a home full of history, or end an old habit around food or comfort. Feelings run deep but stay bearable. Start the therapy, the family talk or the clear-out you've been circling for years."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Moon: this period brings power games at home. A relative tries to steer your life, or you catch yourself managing everyone's moods to feel safe. The old fear says if you let go, everything collapses. It doesn't. Hand back one responsibility that was never yours to carry."}},"pluto>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Mercury: this long period sharpens your mind until it sees through people. You research, investigate, uncover what was buried in a family story or a company. Words gain weight; you can wound or heal with them. Choose what you say with care, and write the true version for yourself first."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Mercury: this period gives your thinking depth and stamina. Research, therapy, investigative work, a book on a hard subject — you stay with difficult material without flinching, and your words persuade. Choose one subject worth years of attention and begin studying it seriously, with a reading list and a schedule."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Mercury: this period brings arguments without exits and thoughts that circle at night. You obsess over a message or suspicion, or start a war of words, because some secret wants out. Write the thought down, sleep on it, and decide in daylight whether it deserves a reply."}},"pluto>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Venus: this long period makes love all or nothing. Attraction runs intense, jealousy surfaces, money and intimacy get tangled. Lukewarm bonds rarely survive it; real ones go deeper. Your sense of worth is stripped back to what's actually yours. Watch for control, yours included, and say what you really want."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Venus: this period deepens love and sharpens your sense of value. Intimacy gets more honest, a relationship survives a hard truth, you start charging what you're worth. Shallow pleasures lose their pull. Have the conversation about sex, money or the future you've avoided because it felt too serious."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Venus: this period tangles love with jealousy, power plays or money. You cling, test, or stay in something because leaving feels like dying. The fear driving it is being replaceable. Look at where you trade control for closeness, and stop paying that price in one relationship."}},"pluto>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Mars: this long period turns drive into force. You can achieve something huge, or burn out trying. Anger runs volcanic, desire obsessive, and conflicts escalate fast. The point is to own your strength without needing to dominate. Pour it into a demanding physical discipline and one goal measured in years."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Mars: this period gives you rare staying power. You can rebuild your body, finish a huge project, or lead through a crisis without cracking. Pick the goal that scares you a little, commit to it for a year, and tell one person who'll hold you to it."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Mars: this period brings standoffs where neither side will back down. Rage, ruthless competition, a body pushed past its limit. The fuel is terror of being powerless. Learn to stop before scorched earth: when you want to crush someone, walk away, sleep, and decide the next morning."}}},"tarot":{"0":{"en":{"name":"The Fool","essence":"A step taken before the map exists","message":"A young traveller strolls toward a cliff edge with a bundle on a stick, a white rose in one hand and a small dog jumping at his heels. He's looking at the sky, not the drop. This is the part of you that says yes before the spreadsheet is finished: the move, the class, the call you haven't rehearsed. Most caution is memory; carry a little less of it.","today":"Say yes to one small unplanned thing — a different route home, a stranger's question, a class you'd normally scroll past — and notice how much of your hesitation was habit.","shadow":"Calling it courage when you simply haven't looked down.","question":"What would you try today if you weren't already sure how it ends?"}},"1":{"en":{"name":"The Magician","essence":"Everything you need is already on the table","message":"A young man stands at a table laid with a cup, a sword, a coin and a wand — one of everything. One hand lifts a wand to the sky, the other points at the ground: idea above, result below, himself the wire in between. You have more tools than you're using: a skill, a contact, a free hour. The trick is to start with them, not wait for better ones.","today":"Pick one thing you've been “preparing” to do and take the first visible step with what you already have: send the draft, book the call, buy the paint.","shadow":"Talking so well about the plan that nobody notices it hasn't started.","question":"Which tool already in your hands have you been ignoring?"}},"2":{"en":{"name":"The High Priestess","essence":"What you know before you can explain it","message":"A woman sits between a black pillar and a white one, a half-hidden scroll in her lap, a veil of pomegranates behind her and a crescent moon at her feet. She isn't hiding anything from you; she's waiting until you're quiet enough to hear it. The hunch about the flat or the friend who's gone vague arrived before your reasons did. That doesn't make it wrong.","today":"Keep one decision to yourself until evening. Don't poll friends or search it online; take it on a walk or into the shower, and notice which answer keeps coming back.","shadow":"Mistaking an old fear for intuition because it speaks in your voice.","question":"What do you already know that you haven't yet said out loud?"}},"3":{"en":{"name":"The Empress","essence":"What grows from care, not pressure","message":"A woman reclines on soft cushions in a garden gone generous: ripe wheat at her feet, a waterfall in the trees behind, a heart-shaped shield resting beside her. Nothing here grows under orders. This is the card of things that thrive when fed — a plant, a child, a body, a business, a meal made slowly. Pleasure isn't the prize for finishing the list. It's fertiliser.","today":"Feed something slowly today: cook one proper meal, water the plants, stretch for ten minutes, or give an hour to the project that's been growing quietly. Enjoy it while you do it.","shadow":"Smothering what you love with more care than it asked for.","question":"What in your life grows best when you stop rushing it?"}},"4":{"en":{"name":"The Emperor","essence":"Rules that end the daily argument with yourself","message":"A grey-bearded ruler sits on a stone throne carved with rams' heads, armour under his red robe, sceptre in one hand and orb in the other. Behind him, bare mountains: nothing soft grows here, and nothing collapses either. His gift is structure — the budget, the bedtime, the boundary said once and kept. Set the rule once and you stop haggling with yourself every tired evening.","today":"Make one rule and write it down: a spending limit, a time you close the laptop, a no you won't explain twice. Keep it once today and see what it frees up.","shadow":"Confusing being in charge with being right about everything.","question":"Where would one firm rule save you a dozen small arguments?"}},"5":{"en":{"name":"The Hierophant","essence":"What tradition and good teachers already know","message":"A priest in a triple crown sits between two grey pillars, one hand raised in blessing, two kneeling students before him and a pair of crossed keys at his feet. He stands for the tested way: your grandmother's recipe, the course with a syllabus, the mentor who has already made your mistakes. Not every rule is a cage. Some are a shortcut someone else paid for.","today":"Ask someone who has done what you're attempting — a renovation, a hard conversation, a career change — for the one mistake they'd avoid. Then take their advice once, even if you'd have done it differently.","shadow":"Following the rulebook so you never have to decide anything yourself.","question":"Whose experience could save you from learning this the hard way?"}},"6":{"en":{"name":"The Lovers","essence":"Choosing what you love, and meaning it","message":"A man and a woman stand naked beneath an angel who spreads its wings from the clouds. Behind her grows a tree with fruit and a serpent; behind him, a tree of flames. The card is about desire, and even more about choice. Saying a full yes to one person, city or job means letting the others go, which is why it's tempting to keep everything vague.","today":"Find one place where you're keeping two options open so nobody is disappointed. Choose one, tell the person it affects, and notice how much lighter the day feels.","shadow":"Keeping every door open so you never have to walk through one.","question":"What would you choose if no one could be disappointed by it?"}},"7":{"en":{"name":"The Chariot","essence":"Willpower that steers without reins","message":"An armoured driver stands in a stone chariot under a canopy of stars. Two sphinxes, one black and one white, sit before it facing different ways, and there are no reins. He steers by will alone. You know this one: the part of you that wants rest and the part that wants the promotion, held together long enough to get somewhere both can live with.","today":"Name the one result you want by tonight — the report sent, the room cleared, the run done — and steer back to it each time a mood or a message pulls you sideways.","shadow":"Forcing your way forward and calling the exhaustion discipline.","question":"Which two parts of you need to pull in the same direction today?"}},"8":{"en":{"name":"Strength","essence":"Gentle hands on a wild thing","message":"A woman in a white dress, crowned with flowers, rests her hands on a lion's jaws and closes them without a fight. There's no whip and no sweat on her. Her kind of strength is patience: with a temper, a craving, a frightened child, your own heart racing before a hard call. You don't defeat the lion. You calm it, because it's yours.","today":"When something flares today — irritation in a meeting, a craving, a sharp text — slow your breath before you answer, and approach it like a nervous dog: slowly, without arguing.","shadow":"Swallowing every feeling and taking the numbness for strength.","question":"What in you needs taming with kindness rather than force?"}},"9":{"en":{"name":"The Hermit","essence":"A small light carried somewhere quiet","message":"An old man in a grey cloak stands alone on a snowy peak, holding a lantern with a six-pointed star inside and looking down at the path. He isn't lost; he left on purpose. Sometimes you keep asking around because your own answer is the one you're avoiding. It comes back on a long walk, with the phone left in another room.","today":"Take thirty minutes alone with no input — no podcast, no feed, no one to reply to — and ask yourself the question you've been outsourcing to other people.","shadow":"Retreating so far that no one can reach you with help.","question":"What would you hear if you stopped asking everyone else?"}},"10":{"en":{"name":"Wheel of Fortune","essence":"The turn you didn't schedule","message":"A great wheel turns in the sky, marked with letters. A snake slides down one side, a jackal-headed figure rises on the other, and a sphinx sits calmly on top with a sword. In the corners, four winged creatures read their books, unbothered. Luck moves: the deal falls through, the old friend calls. You can't stop the wheel; what wears you out is insisting it shouldn't turn.","today":"When something changes without your permission today — a cancelled plan, a surprise bill, an unexpected yes — ask what the new position makes possible before you mourn the old one.","shadow":"Believing you're just unlucky, so nothing you do matters.","question":"Which change are you fighting that could also be a way out?"}},"11":{"en":{"name":"Justice","essence":"Clear accounts and honest consequences","message":"A figure in a red robe sits between two pillars, a raised sword in one hand and level scales in the other. One white shoe peeks out from under the hem, ready to step forward. Justice isn't revenge; it's accuracy. The bill split fairly, the apology you owe, the contract read to the end. Life gets simpler when you stop rounding the truth in your favour.","today":"Settle one account today: pay back the money, answer the email you've dodged, correct the small lie, or read the terms before you sign. Be precise, not harsh.","shadow":"Judging others by rules you quietly excuse yourself from.","question":"What would be fair here if you weren't on either side?"}},"12":{"en":{"name":"The Hanged Man","essence":"The view changes when you stop pushing","message":"A man hangs upside down by one ankle from a living tree, the other leg bent behind his knee, hands behind his back. His face is calm, and a halo glows around his head. He isn't being punished; he chose the pause. Pushing harder only tightens the knot. The stuck project, the reply that won't come, the decision on hold: from another angle, the delay is information.","today":"Stop forcing one stuck thing for a day. Instead of sending a third reminder or rewriting the plan again, ask what this delay is showing you that speed would hide.","shadow":"Stalling indefinitely and wearing the delay like a halo.","question":"What would you see if you looked at this problem upside down?"}},"13":{"en":{"name":"Death","essence":"An ending that clears the ground","message":"A skeleton in black armour rides a white horse under a banner marked with a white rose. A king has fallen, a priest pleads, and a child simply looks up. Far off, the sun rises between two towers. Something is finishing — a role, a habit, a version of you that stopped fitting a while ago. It hurts most where you've invested most.","today":"Let one thing end cleanly today: unsubscribe, delete the draft you'll never send, clear the shelf, or tell someone you're stepping back. Skip the funeral; open the window.","shadow":"Keeping something on life support because letting go feels like failure.","question":"What has already ended that you're still paying rent on?"}},"14":{"en":{"name":"Temperance","essence":"The right mix, poured slowly","message":"A winged angel stands with one foot in a pool and one on dry land, pouring water from one cup into another so steadily that none spills. Behind, a path climbs toward a sunrise between the hills. The skill here is dosage: work and rest, coffee and water, honesty and tact. All-or-nothing feels decisive; the slow mix is what actually lasts.","today":"Find one place where you've swung to an extreme — skipped meals then a takeaway binge, silence then a rant — and correct it by a quarter turn, not a full reversal.","shadow":"Diluting everything until nothing you do has any taste.","question":"What in your day needs a little more of something, not a total change?"}},"15":{"en":{"name":"The Devil","essence":"The chain you could slip off","message":"A horned figure crouches on a black pedestal, torch pointed down. Chained to the block below stand a naked man and woman with small horns of their own. The chains hang loose around their necks. This is the habit that runs you — the scroll at midnight, the ex you check on, the spending that soothes. It holds because it still pays you something: relief, numbness, an excuse.","today":"Pick the habit that ate the most time or money yesterday and make it slightly harder: log out, leave the card at home, put the phone in another room after ten.","shadow":"Blaming the chain while keeping one hand wrapped around it.","question":"What do you keep going back to, and what does it give you?"}},"16":{"en":{"name":"The Tower","essence":"What breaks was already cracked","message":"Lightning strikes a tall tower on a rock and knocks the crown from its top. Flames burst from the windows and two figures fall headfirst through the dark. It looks like disaster, and briefly it is. But the tower stood on something false: a plan that couldn't hold, a story you kept telling yourself. The sudden truth is cheaper than the slow collapse.","today":"Find one thing you're propping up that's already cracked — a plan, a pretence, a polite silence — and stop spending effort hiding the crack. Say the true sentence.","shadow":"Blowing everything up because slow repair feels too humiliating.","question":"Which part of your life is standing on a story you no longer believe?"}},"17":{"en":{"name":"The Star","essence":"Hope that heals by being shared","message":"After the Tower, a woman kneels naked by a pool under one large star and seven small ones, pouring from two jugs — one back into the water, one onto the earth. Nothing is rushed. The worst is behind a door you've already walked through, and what returns now is quiet: appetite, sleep, the wish to make something again.","today":"Give a little attention to whatever is recovering — a friendship, your stamina, an old idea — and feed it without demanding it bloom on schedule.","shadow":"Waiting for a sign instead of filling the jug yourself.","question":"What is coming back to life in you, and how can you tend it today?"}},"18":{"en":{"name":"The Moon","essence":"When fear draws shapes in the dark","message":"A full moon with a sleeping face hangs between two towers. Below, a dog and a wolf howl at it, and a crayfish crawls out of a pool onto a path that winds off into the hills. Everything looks bigger at night. The worry about money, the message you read three ways — some of it is instinct, some is just tiredness wearing a mask.","today":"Before you act on a fear today, check it in daylight: eat something, drink water, ask one direct question. Leave anything big until after you've slept.","shadow":"Treating every 3 a.m. thought as a prophecy.","question":"Which fear shrinks when you say it plainly to someone?"}},"19":{"en":{"name":"The Sun","essence":"Plain joy, nothing to prove","message":"A naked child rides a white horse beneath a huge, smiling sun, arms flung wide, a red banner streaming behind. Sunflowers lean over a garden wall. Nothing in this card is hiding. It's warmth without strategy: laughing out loud, being good at something in public, a day that simply goes well. You don't need to brace for the catch.","today":"Do one thing today purely because it's fun or warm — call the friend who makes you laugh, eat outside, show someone what you made — and don't apologise for enjoying it.","shadow":"Performing happiness so no one notices you're tired.","question":"What would you do today if you didn't have to look serious?"}},"20":{"en":{"name":"Judgement","essence":"The call you can't pretend not to hear","message":"An angel blows a trumpet from the clouds, a flag with a red cross hanging from it. Below, grey figures rise from open coffins floating on the water, arms raised toward the sound. Something wakes you: you see your own life clearly and can't unsee it. An old ambition returns, or an old excuse stops working. Answer while the sound is loud.","today":"Write down the thing you keep promising yourself you'll do “one day” — the course, the move, the apology — and take the first step that makes it awkward to back out.","shadow":"Replaying old mistakes instead of climbing out of them.","question":"What are you being called back to that you've been ignoring?"}},"21":{"en":{"name":"The World","essence":"Finishing well, and knowing you have","message":"A dancer floats inside a great oval wreath tied with red ribbons, a wand in each hand, a purple sash wrapped around her. In the four corners, an angel, an eagle, a lion and a bull look on. The circle is closed: the degree finished, the debt cleared, the year survived. Take the bow before you rush to the next thing, or nothing will ever feel finished.","today":"Mark one thing you've finished, however small — the tax return, the hard week, the wall you painted. Tell someone, tick it off properly, and take an hour before starting anything new.","shadow":"Never calling anything finished, so you never have to let it go.","question":"What have you completed that you haven't yet let yourself celebrate?"}},"22":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Wands","essence":"The spark before the plan","message":"A hand reaches out of a cloud holding a living wand, fresh leaves sprouting from it, a few already drifting down. Below lie a river, green hills and a castle in the distance. This is desire at its first flicker: the idea in the shower, the sudden urge to start a band or a business. It won't stay this bright for long; act while it's hot.","today":"Catch one idea that excites you today and give it a body within the hour: a note with three next steps, a rough sketch, a message to someone who'd help.","shadow":"Collecting exciting beginnings and never letting one become a middle.","question":"What makes you want to start something right now?"}},"23":{"en":{"name":"Two of Wands","essence":"Restless in a castle you built","message":"A man in a red hat stands on castle battlements, a small globe in one hand and a wand in the other, a second wand fixed to the wall beside him. He owns what he can see and is still looking past it. You've built something decent — a job, a routine, a city — and the comfort hasn't cured the itch. The question is no longer whether, but where.","today":"Spend twenty minutes sketching where you'd go next if you stopped waiting: write two real options, one concrete step for each, and pick which one to test this week.","shadow":"Planning the trip forever from the safety of the balcony.","question":"What do you keep looking at beyond the walls you've built?"}},"24":{"en":{"name":"Three of Wands","essence":"Watching for the ships you sent","message":"A man stands on a ridge with his back to us, three staves planted in the ground, looking out over a golden bay where ships are already sailing. He made his move and is watching it unfold. The application is in, the pitch is sent, the first orders arrive. Your plan has met the world; the temptation now is to stand on the cliff refreshing your inbox.","today":"Something you started is already moving. Instead of checking on it again, plan the next leg: who to contact if it works, what to prepare, where you'd take it next.","shadow":"Expecting results before the ships could possibly have landed.","question":"What have you already set in motion that deserves a bigger plan?"}},"25":{"en":{"name":"Four of Wands","essence":"A welcome worth stopping for","message":"Four wands stand in the ground with a garland of flowers and fruit strung between them like a gate. Two figures raise bouquets in greeting, and a castle and a small crowd wait beyond. You've arrived somewhere you worked to reach: the keys to a new flat, the probation passed, the first dinner in a finished kitchen. Mark it, or the effort turns invisible even to you.","today":"Turn one small win into a shared moment today: tell your family the news, bring cake to work, have friends over for no bigger reason than that things are going well.","shadow":"Waiting for a bigger reason before you let anyone celebrate you.","question":"What small win deserves a toast with the people who helped?"}},"26":{"en":{"name":"Five of Wands","essence":"Everyone swinging, no one leading","message":"Five young men raise their staves and swing them at each other in a jumble of angles. Nobody's hurt, nobody's winning, and it isn't clear what they're fighting about. It's what happens in a group with no agreed direction: the meeting where everyone talks, the family plan with five versions, the group chat argument. Usually the fight is about who gets heard.","today":"In the next disagreement, say what you want in one sentence, ask the other person to do the same, and check whether you're arguing about direction or just about who's driving.","shadow":"Picking fights just to feel something when everything else is stuck.","question":"What are you really competing for in this argument?"}},"27":{"en":{"name":"Six of Wands","essence":"Being seen for what you did","message":"A rider crowned with laurel sits high on a white horse, holding a wand with a second wreath tied to it, while a crowd on foot lifts their staves around him. Credit arrives in public: the praise in the team meeting, the post that lands, the client who tells a friend. Let it in. Brushing off praise doesn't make you humble, just harder to thank.","today":"Say yes to visibility today: share the result, put your name on the work, accept the compliment with a plain thank you. If someone helped, name them in public too.","shadow":"Needing the crowd's applause before your work feels real.","question":"What did you do well recently that you've been too modest to mention?"}},"28":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Wands","essence":"Holding your ground from higher up","message":"A man stands on a ledge, fending off six staves that rise from below with one held crossways in both hands. Look at his feet: one boot, one shoe. He didn't have time to dress for this. You're defending a position you've earned — your price, your idea, your boundary — while others want a piece of it. Being outnumbered isn't the same as being wrong.","today":"When someone pushes back today, restate your position once, calmly, without new justifications. Hold it unless they show you a fact you didn't have — not just more pressure.","shadow":"Treating every question as an attack you must repel.","question":"What are you defending that's genuinely worth the effort?"}},"29":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Wands","essence":"Everything moving at once, fast","message":"Eight staves fly through a clear sky in parallel, angled down toward a green valley and a river. No people, no hands, nothing to stop them. Everything speeds up: replies land at once, plans get confirmed, tickets get booked, news arrives faster than you can take it in. Things that stalled for weeks suddenly move. The skill now is catching, not pushing.","today":"Clear the runway: answer the three messages you've been sitting on, confirm the plan, send the invoice. Keep replies short and decisions quick, and let momentum do some of the work.","shadow":"Replying to everything instantly and thinking about nothing.","question":"What would change if you answered today instead of next week?"}},"30":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Wands","essence":"Tired, wary, and nearly there","message":"A man with a bandaged head leans on a wand and glances over his shoulder, eight more staves standing behind him like a fence. He's been hit before and he's expecting it again. You're in the last stretch of something long: the final month of a degree, the renovation, the hard year. Your wariness is earned. You're also closer than you feel.","today":"Protect your reserves for one more push: cancel one optional thing, eat properly, ask for a hand with the heaviest task. Then take the next step, not the whole remaining distance.","shadow":"Suspecting everyone because the last person let you down.","question":"Who could you let past the fence to help with the final stretch?"}},"31":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Wands","essence":"Carrying more than anyone asked you to","message":"A man trudges toward a distant town with ten heavy staves clutched in his arms, bent so low that his face is hidden behind them. He can't see where he's going. Every stick is something you said yes to, one at a time: the extra shift, the family admin, the friend's move, the project nobody else wanted. Some of it was never yours to carry.","today":"List everything you're carrying this week, then put one stick down: hand it over, delay it, or say plainly that you can't. Notice who notices — often fewer people than you feared.","shadow":"Turning exhaustion into proof that you're good and needed.","question":"Which stick in your arms belongs to someone else?"}},"32":{"en":{"name":"Page of Wands","essence":"Curiosity with its sleeves rolled up","message":"A young man in a feathered cap and a tunic patterned with salamanders stands in the desert, holding a tall sprouting staff and studying it as if it were about to speak. He has no plan yet, only fascination. This is the beginner's thrill: the first guitar lesson, the new language app, the hobby you'd be embarrassed to explain. Be bad at it happily.","today":"Try something new at beginner level: watch a tutorial and do the first exercise, book a trial class, ask an expert a naive question. Let it be clumsy.","shadow":"Announcing big plans to everyone before you've tried them once.","question":"What are you curious about that you've never let yourself be bad at?"}},"33":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Wands","essence":"Passion at full gallop","message":"A knight in armour and a salamander-patterned tunic rides a rearing horse in the desert, flame-coloured plumes streaming from his helmet, staff held high. He's already moving before he's decided where. Call it the urge to act now: quit, book the flight, text first, start the business on Monday. That heat gets things done. It also burns through people and plans if nobody steers.","today":"Put your impatience to work: pick the one task you've been circling and finish it in one fast sitting. Save the big irreversible moves for after you've slept.","shadow":"Mistaking the thrill of leaving for knowing where you're going.","question":"Where is your impatience useful, and where is it just running away?"}},"34":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Wands","essence":"Warmth that knows its own worth","message":"A queen holds a staff and a sunflower on a throne carved with lions, a black cat at her feet. She sits wide and easy, clearly in charge. Confidence like hers is practical: running a household, a team or a dinner party without losing your temper or your shine. People warm to you once you stop asking permission to take up room.","today":"Walk into one room today — a meeting, a party, a family call — as if you're welcome there. Speak first, take the good seat, give your opinion without the apology in front of it.","shadow":"Needing to be the brightest person in every room.","question":"What would you do today if you trusted that people like you?"}},"35":{"en":{"name":"King of Wands","essence":"Vision with the nerve to lead it","message":"A king leans forward on a throne carved with lions and salamanders, a flowering staff in hand, a small salamander at his feet. He looks about to stand and give an order. This is leadership by vision: the founder, the coach, the friend who says “here's where we're going.” People follow you because you've decided, not because you're the loudest.","today":"Make the call someone has been waiting on: set the date, choose the direction, assign the tasks. Say it in one clear sentence, and own it if it turns out wrong.","shadow":"Leading so hard that nobody else gets a say.","question":"Where are people waiting for you to decide?"}},"36":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Cups","essence":"A heart full enough to spill over","message":"A hand reaches out of a cloud holding a single cup, and it is already overflowing: five streams fall into a pond of lilies while a dove drops a small white wafer into it. You didn't earn this by effort. It is the moment feeling returns — a crush, a crying jag that clears the air, a sudden fondness for someone you'd written off.","today":"Let one feeling all the way in today instead of managing it: say the warm thing out loud, cry at the song, text the person who crossed your mind first.","shadow":"Treating a rush of feeling as a promise someone made you","question":"What feeling do you keep postponing because you're too busy to have it?"}},"37":{"en":{"name":"Two of Cups","essence":"Meeting someone exactly halfway","message":"Two people stand face to face, each holding out a cup to the other, as if signing something without paper. Above them floats a staff crowned with a winged lion: desire, and the words that keep it honest. This is the card of being met as an equal — the date that goes both ways, the colleague who returns the favour, the apology that gets one back.","today":"Make one exchange even today. Answer the message with the same care it was sent with, split the bill or the chore fairly, and notice who meets you halfway without being asked.","shadow":"Mirroring someone so closely you forget what you wanted","question":"Who do you feel like an equal with, and when did you last tell them?"}},"38":{"en":{"name":"Three of Cups","essence":"The friends who make you laugh again","message":"Three women dance in a ring with their cups raised high, and the ground at their feet is heaped with pumpkins and grapes. Nobody is in charge; nobody is watching from the edge. This is friendship as nourishment — the group chat that turns a bad day into a joke, the birthday you nearly skipped, the people who knew you before you had it together.","today":"Make a plan with friends rather than waiting to be invited: a coffee, a walk, a ridiculous voice note. Celebrate one small win out loud, yours or someone else's.","shadow":"Hiding in the crowd so no one notices how you actually are","question":"Who do you laugh with most easily, and when did you last see them in person?"}},"39":{"en":{"name":"Four of Cups","essence":"The offer you're too fed up to see","message":"A young man sits under a tree with his arms folded, glaring at three cups lined up on the grass. From a cloud beside him, a hand offers a fourth, and he hasn't noticed. This is the flatness after too much of the same: the scroll, the same three takeaway places, the friend you've stopped listening to. Often the boredom is a disappointment you haven't admitted yet.","today":"Say yes to one thing you'd normally wave away today — an invitation, a new route, a different lunch. Then name, privately, what you're actually disappointed about.","shadow":"Refusing every new cup because the old ones let you down","question":"What have you stopped noticing because you decided in advance it wouldn't help?"}},"40":{"en":{"name":"Five of Cups","essence":"Grief that hasn't turned around yet","message":"A figure in a long black cloak bows over three spilled cups, their contents soaking into the ground. Behind him two more stand upright, and a bridge leads across the river toward home. He can't see them yet. This card honours loss — the breakup, the job, the parent you hoped for and didn't get — and quietly points out what is still standing.","today":"Give the loss its due: name it, write it down, or tell one person it still hurts. Then turn round once and count what's still standing — two cups is not nothing.","shadow":"Replaying the spill so long you forget the bridge home","question":"What is still standing behind you that you haven't turned to look at?"}},"41":{"en":{"name":"Six of Cups","essence":"Simple kindness that tastes like childhood","message":"In an old courtyard, a boy bends to hand a smaller girl a cup full of white flowers. Five more cups bloom around them, and a guard walks away, as if nothing here needs guarding. This is the sweetness of the familiar: your grandmother's recipe, a friend from school, the street you grew up on — and a reminder of how you were before you got careful.","today":"Do one thing the younger you would have loved: the old song, the cheap sweets, the drawing, the call to a childhood friend. Give a small gift with no reason attached.","shadow":"Living in the old days because today asks more of you","question":"What did you love at ten that you could bring back into this week?"}},"42":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Cups","essence":"Too many dreams, not one decision","message":"A dark figure stands before seven cups floating on a cloud, each holding a different prize: a castle, a pile of jewels, a wreath, a snake, a dragon, a veiled glowing shape. All of them look possible from here. This is the card of the twelve open tabs — the flats, the career pivots, the people you could date — and the quiet comfort of never choosing.","today":"Pick one of the daydreams and give it a real-world test today: a price, a date, a phone call, one hour of actual work. The rest can wait.","shadow":"Keeping every option open so you never risk losing one","question":"Which of your daydreams would survive a Tuesday morning?"}},"43":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Cups","essence":"Walking away from what no longer feeds you","message":"Under a watchful moon, a figure in a red cloak walks away from eight cups stacked neatly on the shore. Nothing is broken; there's only a gap where one cup should be, and he has stopped pretending not to see it. This is the quiet leaving — the job that's fine, the friendship that's fine, the city that's fine — when fine has become the problem.","today":"Notice one place where you keep showing up out of habit. You don't have to leave today. Stop pretending it's enough, and write down what's missing.","shadow":"Leaving every time things get ordinary and calling it growth","question":"What are you staying with only because leaving would be awkward?"}},"44":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Cups","essence":"The wish, granted and actually enjoyed","message":"A well-fed man sits on a bench with his arms crossed and a satisfied grin, nine cups lined up on the shelf behind him like trophies. This is the wish card: something you wanted is here, or close. The harder part, for many people, is letting it be enough — eating the good meal slowly instead of photographing it and planning the next.","today":"Enjoy something you already have, deliberately: the coat you saved for, the quiet flat, the person beside you. Say thank you to someone who made it possible.","shadow":"Smugness, or needing others to see how well you're doing","question":"Which wish of yours has already come true without a celebration?"}},"45":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Cups","essence":"Home as the people, not the walls","message":"A couple stands arm in arm, free hands lifted toward a rainbow of ten cups. Beside them two children dance, ignoring the view, and a small house sits on the hill. This is belonging you can live inside: the Sunday lunch that runs long, the friend who has your spare key, the chosen family that turns up when the boiler breaks.","today":"Make home feel like home in one small way today: cook for someone, call the relative you actually like, fix the drawer, set the table properly. Notice who you'd tell good news to first.","shadow":"Performing a perfect family for photos while nobody talks","question":"Who feels like home to you, and do they know it?"}},"46":{"en":{"name":"Page of Cups","essence":"A soft surprise that makes you smile","message":"A young page in a flowered tunic stands by the sea, holding up a cup — and a small fish has popped its head out to look at him. He isn't alarmed; he's charmed. This is the card of tender surprises: an odd idea for a story, a shy message from someone you like, a feeling you'd usually laugh off before it finished arriving.","today":"Take one strange, soft impulse seriously today: write the silly poem, send the shy message, buy the flowers for no reason. Don't explain it to anyone.","shadow":"Sulking like a teenager when a feeling isn't returned","question":"What small, odd idea keeps surfacing that you keep dismissing as silly?"}},"47":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Cups","essence":"Romance that arrives at walking pace","message":"A knight in a winged helmet rides a white horse at a slow walk, holding a cup out in front of him like a proposal. He isn't charging anywhere; he wants to be seen arriving. This is the card of the gesture — the invitation, the long message, the plan you pitch with your whole heart — and of the romantic who loves the offer more than the follow-through.","today":"Make one generous offer today and mean it: the invitation, the compliment, the “I'd love to help with that”. Then put the next step in your calendar so it actually happens.","shadow":"Falling for the idea of someone instead of the person","question":"Who are you courting in your head instead of in real life?"}},"48":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Cups","essence":"Listening until you hear what isn't said","message":"A queen sits on a throne at the very edge of the sea, gazing at an ornate cup with a lid — the only covered cup in the suit. She isn't drinking from it; she's listening to it. This is emotional intelligence: the friend who hears the real problem under the small one, who can sit with your mess without trying to tidy it.","today":"In one conversation today, listen for the feeling under the words and name it gently: “that sounds exhausting”. Do the same for yourself before bed.","shadow":"Absorbing everyone's moods until you can't find your own","question":"Whose feelings are you carrying today that were never yours to hold?"}},"49":{"en":{"name":"King of Cups","essence":"Calm in the middle of rough water","message":"A king sits on a stone throne set in the middle of a choppy sea, a cup in one hand and a sceptre in the other. A ship strains on one side, a fish leaps on the other; he feels the swell and doesn't let it steer. This is feeling held steady — the parent who stays calm in the hospital corridor, the manager who answers the furious email without heat.","today":"When something stirs you up today, wait ten minutes before you reply, speak or buy. Feel the whole wave, then answer from the far side of it.","shadow":"Staying so calm that nobody can tell what you feel","question":"What would you say right now if you weren't managing everyone's reaction?"}},"50":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Swords","essence":"One clear thought that cuts through fog","message":"A hand bursts from a cloud gripping a sword straight up, its point through the ring of a golden crown hung with olive and palm. Below lie bare mountains: nothing soft here. This is the moment of clarity — the sentence that finally explains the problem, the honest feedback, the “no” you've been circling for weeks. Truth arrives sharp and usually a little cold.","today":"Write what's bothering you in one plain sentence today — no adjectives, no excuses. Read it back slowly: the answer is often already inside the wording.","shadow":"Being right so sharply that nobody can hear it","question":"What do you already know but haven't yet said in plain words?"}},"51":{"en":{"name":"Two of Swords","essence":"Refusing to look so you needn't choose","message":"A blindfolded woman sits on a stone bench with her back to the sea, arms crossed over her chest, a long sword balanced in each hand. She is perfectly still because moving would mean choosing. This is the stand-off you keep postponing: the two job offers, a friend's two versions of the story, the conversation you defend yourself against by not having it.","today":"Take the blindfold off for a quarter of an hour: write both options side by side with what each would cost you. You don't have to decide today, only to look.","shadow":"Calling it peace when it's only refusing to feel","question":"What decision are you avoiding by keeping yourself perfectly balanced?"}},"52":{"en":{"name":"Three of Swords","essence":"A painful truth, finally felt","message":"A red heart hangs in a grey sky, pierced clean through by three swords, while rain pours behind it. There's no figure, no story, only the hurt itself. This is the sentence that lands — the overheard comment, the text you weren't meant to see, the thing that was true all along. It hurts because it's accurate, and accurate pain can heal cleanly.","today":"Name one hurt you've been carrying — new or old — exactly as it is, to yourself or one trusted person. Then let it rain for an evening without fixing anything.","shadow":"Reopening the wound so often it never gets to close","question":"Which hurt are you still explaining away instead of feeling?"}},"53":{"en":{"name":"Four of Swords","essence":"Lying down before you fall down","message":"In a quiet church, a knight lies stretched out on a tomb, hands folded, eyes closed. Three swords hang on the wall above him and a fourth rests beneath, put down for now. A stained-glass window lets in the only colour. This is rest as a decision, not a collapse: the phone in another room, the cancelled evening, the afternoon nap you stop apologising for.","today":"Schedule twenty minutes of real nothing today: no phone, no podcast, no tidying. A tired mind makes every problem look like a threat; let it go quiet first.","shadow":"Hiding from a problem and calling it a break","question":"What would you stop worrying about if you'd slept properly for three nights?"}},"54":{"en":{"name":"Five of Swords","essence":"Winning the argument, losing the people","message":"A man smirks as he gathers up swords, three in his arms and two left on the ground, while two figures walk off toward the shore, one with a hand over his face. The sky is torn with wind. This is the argument you win and regret: the group chat pile-on, the last word at dinner, the point you made so well that nobody calls back.","today":"Before you send a sharp reply today, ask what you'd actually win and who you'd lose. Sometimes the strongest move is putting the sword down and going home.","shadow":"Needing to be right because being wrong feels like disappearing","question":"Which fight are you still trying to win that costs more than it's worth?"}},"55":{"en":{"name":"Six of Swords","essence":"Moving toward calmer water, slowly","message":"A ferryman poles a boat across the water, a hunched woman and a child huddled in it beside six upright swords. The water is choppy on one side and smooth on the side they're heading toward. This is leaving a hard stretch behind — the move after the breakup, the new job after the bad one. The swords come along, but someone else is steering for a while.","today":"Accept help getting from here to there today — a lift, a friend's advice, someone who has done it before. Choose the calmer route, even if it takes longer.","shadow":"Leaving the place but packing every argument to take along","question":"What are you ready to leave behind, and who could row for a while?"}},"56":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Swords","essence":"Getting away with it — or trying to","message":"A man tiptoes away from a camp of bright tents, five swords clutched awkwardly in his arms, grinning back over his shoulder. Two swords stay stuck in the ground behind him: he couldn't carry everything. This is the clever shortcut — the excuse that isn't quite true, the credit quietly taken, the plan you keep to yourself because you suspect it wouldn't survive a question.","today":"Check one shortcut you're tempted by today: would you be comfortable explaining it out loud? If yes, take it quietly. If not, carry less and do it straight.","shadow":"Lying to yourself first so the lie to others feels fine","question":"What are you doing alone because you're afraid of being asked about it?"}},"57":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Swords","essence":"A cage made mostly of thoughts","message":"A woman stands blindfolded with her arms loosely tied, eight swords planted in the mud around her. Look closer: the swords don't close the circle, and the knots are slack. She could walk out if she could see. This is the trap built from thoughts — “I can't afford it”, “they'd never let me”, “it's too late” — repeated until they feel like walls.","today":"Write down one “I can't” you've said this week and test it: one question to a real person, one search, one small step. Most walls are thinner than they sound.","shadow":"Waiting to be rescued from knots you could untie","question":"Which “I can't” in your life is really “I'm scared to”?"}},"58":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Swords","essence":"The 3 a.m. thoughts that lie","message":"A woman sits bolt upright in bed in the dark, face in her hands, nine swords lined up on the black wall behind her. Notice that none of them touch her. This is the 3 a.m. card: the email you replay, the symptom you search, the conversation you rehearse until it becomes a catastrophe. Worry is louder at night because there's nothing to do with it.","today":"Take the worry out of your head and onto paper today: write the fear, then the next practical step, then when you'll take it. Fears shrink in daylight and in writing.","shadow":"Treating a frightening thought as proof that it's true","question":"What is the actual worst case, and what would you do on day one?"}},"59":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Swords","essence":"The end that finally lets you stop","message":"A man lies face down by the water with ten swords in his back — the deck's most dramatic card, almost theatrical. But look past him: the black sky is breaking into a gold line of dawn over a calm sea. This is the thing that is truly over — the project, the pretence, the relationship you kept resuscitating. It can't get worse, which is its own relief.","today":"Today, stop reviving something that has clearly ended: delete the draft, cancel the subscription, stop rereading the old thread. Then do one ordinary, steadying thing slowly — a shower, a walk, breakfast.","shadow":"Making a drama of the ending so you needn't start again","question":"What is already over that you keep giving one more chance?"}},"60":{"en":{"name":"Page of Swords","essence":"Curious, alert, asking one more question","message":"A young page stands on a windy hilltop, sword raised in both hands, glancing back over his shoulder as if he heard something. Clouds race, birds scatter, trees bend. He is all attention. This is the beginner's mind with an edge: the question nobody else asks in the meeting, the article you fact-check, the new skill you're clumsy at but hungry for.","today":"Ask the question you've been too polite to ask today — at work, in a shop, on a family call. Then check one thing you believe against a reliable source.","shadow":"Gossip and suspicion passed off as curiosity","question":"What are you curious about that you've been pretending to already understand?"}},"61":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Swords","essence":"Full speed toward the point","message":"A knight charges at full gallop, sword raised, leaning so far forward he's ahead of his own horse. Clouds are ripped sideways, trees bend in the wind he makes. This is thought turned into speed: the email sent in two minutes, the plan pitched before anyone's finished their coffee, the decision made on the train. Brilliant for a deadline, rough on everyone in the way.","today":"Use the speed on one stuck task today: draft it, send it, book it within the hour. For anything involving feelings, slow down by half and listen first.","shadow":"Cutting people off mid-sentence because you're sure you know","question":"Where would going slower actually get you there faster?"}},"62":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Swords","essence":"Kind enough to tell you the truth","message":"A queen sits in profile on a throne set high among the clouds, sword upright in one hand, the other lifted as if to say “go on, I'm listening — but get to the point.” A single bird flies above her. She has seen enough to stop being fooled. This is clear-eyed kindness: the friend who reads your contract, the boss who gives straight feedback, the no without a lecture.","today":"Say one true thing plainly today without padding it in apologies: the price, the deadline, the “that doesn't work for me”. Warmth and directness can share a sentence.","shadow":"Cutting people with accuracy because softness once got you hurt","question":"Where are you over-explaining something that needs only one sentence?"}},"63":{"en":{"name":"King of Swords","essence":"The fair decision, made and owned","message":"A king sits facing you squarely, sword upright and slightly tilted, eyes level. His throne is carved with butterflies, but nothing about him flutters. This is judgement you can trust: the person who reads all the small print, hears both sides and then actually decides — the referee, the good lawyer, the parent who sets a rule and explains it once.","today":"Settle one decision you've been putting off today: gather the facts, give yourself an hour, choose, and tell whoever it affects why — in two sentences.","shadow":"Rules applied so coldly that nobody dares tell you anything","question":"What would you decide if you were advising a friend instead of yourself?"}},"64":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Pentacles","essence":"A real start you can hold","message":"From a cloud, an open palm offers a single gold coin, heavy and bright, above a garden of white lilies. Beyond the hedge, an arch opens onto a path toward the mountains. This is opportunity in solid form: the job offer, the first paid client, the savings account opened, the gym membership actually used. Small, real and yours to plant.","today":"Plant one small, tangible seed today: put a little money aside, send the invoice, book the check-up, buy the good shoes. Something you could point to next month.","shadow":"Waiting for the perfect offer while ignoring the one in your hand","question":"What small, concrete thing could you start today that would still matter in a year?"}},"65":{"en":{"name":"Two of Pentacles","essence":"Juggling well, with a little rhythm","message":"A young man in a tall hat dances on the spot, keeping two coins in the air, linked by a ribbon that loops like a figure eight. Behind him, two ships climb huge waves. He's not in control of the sea, only of his footwork. This is the juggle: two jobs, rent and a birthday, the school run and the deadline — kept moving with rhythm, not panic.","today":"List what you're juggling today and decide which two balls matter most. Keep those moving, let one drop on purpose, and move your body between tasks.","shadow":"Saying yes to everything and calling the chaos flexibility","question":"Which of the things you're juggling could you put down without anyone noticing?"}},"66":{"en":{"name":"Three of Pentacles","essence":"Good work, made better by others","message":"In a stone church, a mason stands on a bench working at an arch while a monk and a man holding the plans look up and talk it through. Three pentacles are carved into the stone above them. Each one knows something the others don't. This is skilled teamwork: the colleague who checks your draft, the builder who listens, the project that gets better because you asked.","today":"Show unfinished work today to one person whose eye you trust, and ask a specific question: “what would you cut?” Credit someone by name for their part in a shared win.","shadow":"Doing it all yourself because nobody else does it properly","question":"Whose skill would make your work better if you stopped being proud about asking?"}},"67":{"en":{"name":"Four of Pentacles","essence":"Holding on tight to feel safe","message":"A crowned man sits with a city behind him, hugging one coin to his chest, another balanced on his head, two pinned under his feet. He can't stand up, eat or wave without losing something. This is safety that tightens into a grip: savings worth protecting, and the small pleasure or risk you refuse even when you can afford it, because enough has never felt like enough.","today":"Today, loosen your grip on one thing by a notch — money, a role, a plan, a person: spend a little on something good, share the task, ask for help.","shadow":"Confusing control with safety, and stinginess with good sense","question":"How much would actually feel like enough, and how would you know?"}},"68":{"en":{"name":"Five of Pentacles","essence":"Out in the cold, near a lit door","message":"Two figures limp through falling snow, one on crutches, the other wrapping a thin shawl tighter. Above them glows a stained-glass window, warm and lit, and they walk right past it. This is the hard patch — the overdraft, the sick week, the feeling of being left out — made worse by pride or shame that stops you knocking on the door that's right there.","today":"Ask for one concrete kind of help today, however awkward: a payment plan, a lift, a shared meal, a day off. If you're doing fine, offer one instead.","shadow":"Believing you deserve the cold, so not knocking","question":"Who would help you right now if you let them know what's going on?"}},"69":{"en":{"name":"Six of Pentacles","essence":"Giving and receiving, weighed fairly","message":"A well-dressed merchant holds a set of scales in one hand and drops coins into the open palm of one of two kneeling figures. The other waits his turn. Nobody here is equal yet, and the scales say he's thinking about fairness. This is the card of give and take: the loan, the tip, the favour, the raise — and who feels small afterwards.","today":"Give something today in a way that leaves the other person their dignity: pay promptly, tip well, help without a speech. And accept one offer without arguing it down.","shadow":"Giving so you can stay the one in charge","question":"Where do you find it easier to give than to receive, and why?"}},"70":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Pentacles","essence":"Leaning on the hoe, checking the growth","message":"A young farmer leans on his hoe and studies a leafy bush heavy with six coins, one more lying at his feet. The work isn't finished; he's stopped to look. This is the honest mid-point check: the savings that grow slowly, the language app at day forty, the relationship you're tending. Patience matters, and so does asking whether this crop deserves another season.","today":"Pick one long project and measure it honestly today: what you've put in, what's grown, what hasn't. Then decide: keep watering, change method, or stop.","shadow":"Digging up the seeds every day to check they're growing","question":"What are you impatient with that is actually growing at the right speed?"}},"71":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Pentacles","essence":"Getting good by doing it again","message":"A craftsman sits at his bench, head down, tapping a design into a coin. Six finished ones hang on the post beside him; another waits on the floor. The town is far behind, and he doesn't look up. This is skill built the unglamorous way: the scales you practise, the code you rewrite, the sourdough on its ninth attempt. Repetition is where talent turns into something reliable.","today":"Give one skill a focused, phone-free half hour today and do the boring part properly. Don't judge the result; count the repetitions.","shadow":"Perfecting one detail forever so you never have to finish","question":"What would you be excellent at in a year if you practised it daily?"}},"72":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Pentacles","essence":"Earned comfort, enjoyed in your own company","message":"A woman in a robe stitched with flowers stands alone in a ripe vineyard, a hooded falcon resting on her gloved hand. The grapes are heavy, the house behind her is hers. The falcon's hood is the price: discipline bought all this. This is self-made ease: the flat you furnished on your own salary, the evening you enjoy without company, the good coffee you can now simply afford.","today":"Prove to yourself today that you can look after yourself well: cook a proper meal for one, pay a bill early, book yourself a table. Then enjoy your own company, phone face down.","shadow":"Independence so complete that needing anyone feels like failure","question":"Where could you trust your own resources instead of waiting for someone to provide?"}},"73":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Pentacles","essence":"What lasts longer than one life","message":"Under a stone archway an old man in a patterned robe sits stroking two white dogs, while a couple talks nearby and a child reaches toward a dog. Ten coins hang over the scene like a family tree. This is wealth measured in decades: the house that stays in the family, the recipe, the pension, the habits your grandparents passed on, good and bad, without noticing.","today":"Give the long term one small act today: sort an important document, ask an older relative for a family story, put a little aside, label the old photos.","shadow":"Living by the family script without asking if it fits","question":"What do you want to pass on, and what should stop with you?"}},"74":{"en":{"name":"Page of Pentacles","essence":"A beginner studying something real","message":"A young page stands in a spring field, holding a single coin up in both hands and staring at it as if it might explain itself. Behind him a ploughed patch waits. He hasn't done anything yet; he's paying attention. This is the start of a practical skill or plan: the first budget spreadsheet, the evening course, the new job's first week, the vegetable bed.","today":"Learn one practical thing properly today: how your payslip is calculated, how to change a tyre, how a recipe really works. Then explain it to someone else, out loud.","shadow":"Collecting courses and plans while the field stays unploughed","question":"What practical skill would make next year noticeably easier?"}},"75":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Pentacles","essence":"Slow, steady and actually finishing","message":"A knight sits on a heavy black horse that is standing completely still at the edge of a ploughed field. He holds his coin and looks at it, not at the horizon. Of all the knights, he's the only one not moving. This is the reliable grind: the run three mornings a week, the debt paid down monthly, the colleague who always delivers, boring and unbeatable.","today":"Do the dull, necessary task first today — the expense report, the laundry, the twenty minutes on the course — at a steady pace, and finish it completely before anything fun.","shadow":"Mistaking a rut for reliability and refusing every change","question":"Which small routine, kept for three months, would change the most?"}},"76":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Pentacles","essence":"Care you can eat, wear and sleep in","message":"A queen sits in a garden thick with roses, a big gold coin cradled in her lap like something alive. A rabbit hides in the grass. Her throne is carved with fruit and goats: plenty, but earned. This is care made practical — the full fridge, the clean sheets, the friend who brings soup and also fixes your CV, the budget that leaves room for flowers.","today":"Look after someone properly today, yourself included: a real meal, an early night, clean sheets, a walk in daylight. Then make one corner of home easier to live in.","shadow":"Mothering everyone so nobody notices you're running on empty","question":"Who looks after you the way you look after everyone else?"}},"77":{"en":{"name":"King of Pentacles","essence":"Solid ground you built and share","message":"A king sits in a garden so overgrown with grapevines that they've crept onto his robe. One hand rests on a gold coin, the other holds a sceptre; bulls are carved into his throne and a castle stands behind him. This is success that feeds people: the business that pays on time, the parent who covers the deposit, the boss who builds something others can stand on.","today":"Handle one money or work matter today the way a calm, solvent adult would: pay on time, name a fair price, spend an hour on something that will still stand next year.","shadow":"Measuring your worth, and everyone else's, by what they earn","question":"What are you building that other people will be able to rely on?"}}}};
